export const content: Record<string, string> = {
  "马尾瀑布“火瀑布”": "Horsetail Fall Firefall",
  "2 月中下旬的晴天，日落前十来分钟的夕阳把酋长岩东侧的马尾瀑布照成橙红色，像一道流动的火焰；要同时满足瀑布有水、西边天空无云，很多年都看不到。": "On clear days in mid-to-late February, the sun in the last 10 minutes or so before sunset turns Horsetail Fall, on the east side of El Capitan, a glowing orange-red, like a stream of fire. It needs water in the fall and a cloudless western sky at the same time, and in many years it never happens.",
  "不用买票；在 Yosemite Falls 停车场（Yosemite Valley Lodge 西边）停车，步行约 2.4 公里到 El Capitan Picnic Area 观景区，停车场满了就停 Yosemite Village 或 Curry Village 再坐免费班车。": "No tickets needed. Park at the Yosemite Falls parking area (west of Yosemite Valley Lodge) and walk about 1.5 miles to the El Capitan Picnic Area viewing area. If the lot is full, park at Yosemite Village or Curry Village and take the free shuttle.",
  "2026 年 2 月不需要进园预约，但观景期间 Northside / Southside Drive 部分路段禁止停车，周末日落后可能临时封路；2027 年的安排以 NPS 公告为准。": "No park reservation was required in February 2026, but parking is prohibited along parts of Northside and Southside Drive during the viewing period, and roads may close temporarily after sunset on weekends. Check NPS announcements for 2027 arrangements.",
  "半穹顶登顶许可证抽签": "Half Dome Cables Permit Lottery",
  "登顶半穹顶的最后约 120 米要抓着钢缆爬。钢缆通常在阵亡将士纪念日（5 月最后一个周一）前的周五装上、10 月第二个周一的次日拆除，这段时间每天限约 300 人，必须有许可证。": "The last 400 feet or so to the top of Half Dome go straight up the steel cables. The cables usually go up the Friday before Memorial Day (the last Monday in May) and come down the day after the second Monday in October. During that time, about 300 people a day are allowed, and everyone needs a permit.",
  "在 Recreation.gov 抽签：3 月 1–31 日预抽签（每份申请最多 6 人），4 月中旬出结果；季节内每天还有日抽签，提前两天申请、当晚出结果。每份申请 10 美元，中签后每人再付 10 美元。": "Apply through the Recreation.gov lottery. The preseason lottery runs March 1–31 (up to six people per application), with results in mid-April. During the season there's also a daily lottery: apply two days ahead and get results that evening. Each application costs $10, and winners pay another $10 per person.",
  "优胜美地瀑布月虹": "Yosemite Falls Moonbows",
  "4–6 月瀑布水量最大的季节，满月前后的夜晚，月光会在上、下优胜美地瀑布的水雾里照出彩虹；肉眼看偏灰白，用相机长曝光才拍得出颜色。": "In April–June, when the falls run highest, a full moon can light up rainbows in the mist of Upper and Lower Yosemite Fall. To the naked eye they look grayish white; it takes a long camera exposure to bring out the colors.",
  "免费、不用预约；常见的观赏位置在下优胜美地瀑布步道的桥附近，选满月当晚或前后一两晚，带头灯、三脚架和防水外套。": "Free, no reservation needed. A popular viewing spot is near the bridge on the Lower Yosemite Fall Trail. Go on the night of the full moon or a night or two either side, and bring a headlamp, a tripod, and a waterproof jacket.",
  "山谷观光车与冰川点巴士团": "Valley Floor Tour & Glacier Point Tour",
  "特许经营商 Yosemite Hospitality 的导览车团，都从 Yosemite Valley Lodge 出发：两小时的山谷观光车全年运营（暖季是敞篷游览车），冰川点团往返约 4 小时，全天的 Grand Tour 把山谷、冰川点和马里波萨巨杉林串在一起，不想自己开山路的人很方便。": "Guided bus tours run by the concessioner Yosemite Hospitality, all departing from Yosemite Valley Lodge. The 2-hour Valley Floor Tour runs year-round (in an open-air tram in the warmer months), the Glacier Point Tour takes about 4 hours round trip, and the full-day Grand Tour links the valley, Glacier Point, and the Mariposa Grove of Giant Sequoias. A good option if you'd rather not drive the mountain roads yourself.",
  "在 travelyosemite.com 或 Valley Lodge 旅游服务台订票，成人价约：山谷观光车 41 美元、冰川点团往返 72.5 美元、Grand Tour 141 美元（含午餐）；夏季满月前后还有夜间敞篷观光车，7 月到 9 月初有去图奥勒米草甸的徒步巴士。": "Book at travelyosemite.com or at the Valley Lodge tour desk. Approximate adult prices: Valley Floor Tour $41, Glacier Point Tour round trip $72.50, and Grand Tour $141 (lunch included). In summer there are also open-air moonlight tours around the full moon, and from July to early September a hikers' bus runs to Tuolumne Meadows.",
  "2026 年 Grand Tour 运营到 10 月 12 日；冰川点团只在 Glacier Point Road 开通时发车（该路 2026 年 9 月 23 日起因 Dome Fire 烟雾临时封闭）。": "In 2026 the Grand Tour runs through October 12. The Glacier Point Tour departs only when Glacier Point Road is open (the road has been temporarily closed since September 23, 2026, because of smoke from the Dome Fire).",
  "默塞德河漂流": "Merced River Rafting",
  "夏天水位合适时，可以在 Curry Village 租充气筏，从 Stoneman Bridge 顺流漂约 5 公里到 Sentinel Beach，一路看半穹顶、优胜美地瀑布和哨兵岩，水流平缓，适合家庭。": "In summer, when water levels allow, rent an inflatable raft at Curry Village and float about 3 miles from Stoneman Bridge to Sentinel Beach, with views of Half Dome, Yosemite Falls, and Sentinel Rock along the way. The current is gentle and good for families.",
  "只能当天在 Curry Village 租船点现场订（8 点开始售票，常常卖完），租筏约 36 美元/人，回程班车另收费；每条筏至少一名成人，体重不足 50 磅（约 23 公斤）的孩子不能上船。": "Same-day only, in person at the Curry Village raft stand (tickets go on sale at 8 a.m. and often sell out). Raft rental is about $36 per person; the return shuttle costs extra. Each raft needs at least one adult, and children under 50 pounds can't go.",
  "每年按水位、水温决定开放日期，通常 6–7 月；只有当天早上 8 点 Pohono Bridge 水位低于 7 英尺时才允许漂流。": "Opening dates are set each year based on water level and temperature, usually June–July. Rafting is allowed only if the river at Pohono Bridge reads below 7 feet at 8 a.m. that day.",
  "Badger Pass 滑雪场": "Badger Pass Ski Area",
  "加州最老的滑雪场，在 Glacier Point Road 上、海拔约 2,200 米，雪道平缓，适合初学者和孩子；同一处还有雪地滑圈、越野滑雪和雪鞋租借，护林员冬季常从这里带免费的雪鞋徒步。": "California's oldest ski area, on Glacier Point Road at about 7,200 feet. The gentle runs suit beginners and kids, and there's also snow tubing, cross-country skiing, and snowshoe rentals. In winter, rangers often lead free snowshoe walks from here.",
  "在 travelyosemite.com 买票，全天缆车票成人约 79 美元、7–12 岁约 59.5 美元，6 岁以下免费；雪季上山的路常要求带防滑链。": "Buy tickets at travelyosemite.com. A full-day lift ticket is about $79 for adults and $59.50 for ages 7–12; kids under 6 ski free. Tire chains are often required on the road up during the snow season.",
  "雪季约 12 月中旬到 3 月下旬，开放日期看当年降雪；2025–26 雪季营业到 3 月 29 日前后。": "The season runs roughly mid-December to late March, depending on snowfall. In 2025–26 the ski area was open until about March 29.",
  "Curry Village 露天溜冰场": "Curry Village Ice Skating Rink",
  "山谷东头的露天溜冰场，抬头就是冰川点和半穹顶，1929 年就有了，是优胜美地的冬季传统，冬天带孩子来山谷可以玩一两个小时。": "An outdoor rink at the east end of the valley, with Glacier Point and Half Dome overhead. It has been here since 1929 and is a Yosemite winter tradition. With kids in the valley in winter, it's good for an hour or two.",
  "现场买票、可以租冰鞋，按场次收费，价格以 Yosemite Hospitality 官网为准。": "Buy tickets and rent skates on site. Admission is per session; check Yosemite Hospitality's website for prices.",
  "通常 11 月中旬到次年 3 月中旬开放，看天气。": "Usually open mid-November to mid-March, weather permitting.",
  "优胜美地登山学校攀岩课": "Yosemite Mountaineering School",
  "在世界攀岩圣地上一节入门攀岩课：没有经验也能报名，教练带着在花岗岩上学攀爬和绳索下降；也可以请私人向导带爬经典路线。": "Take an intro climbing class in one of the world's great climbing destinations. No experience needed: instructors teach you to climb granite and rappel. Private guides can also take you up classic routes.",
  "向 Yosemite Mountaineering School（Yosemite Hospitality 经营，电话 209-372-8344）预约，春到秋在山谷开课、夏季也在图奥勒米草甸开课；团体入门课每人约 200 多美元，以官网报价为准。": "Book with Yosemite Mountaineering School (run by Yosemite Hospitality; 209-372-8344). Classes run in the valley from spring through fall and in Tuolumne Meadows in summer. Group intro classes are a little over $200 per person; check the website for current prices.",
  "水晶洞导览": "Crystal Cave Tour",
  "Giant Forest 附近的大理石溶洞，为保护脆弱的钟乳石只能跟导览进入：洞内环线约 50 分钟，从停车场到洞口还要走约 800 米陡坡（单程），洞里常年约 10°C，要带外套。": "A marble cave near Giant Forest. To protect its fragile formations, you can enter only on a guided tour. The loop inside takes about 50 minutes, and the steep walk from the parking area to the entrance is about half a mile one way. The cave stays around 50°F year-round, so bring a jacket.",
  "只在 Sequoia Parks Conservancy 官网卖票，至少提前 36 小时，旺季建议提前两个月，洞口不售票；Crystal Cave Road 窄而弯，车长（含拖车）超过 22 英尺不能上。": "Tickets are sold only on the Sequoia Parks Conservancy website, at least 36 hours ahead; in peak season, book two months out. No tickets are sold at the cave. Crystal Cave Road is narrow and winding, and vehicles over 22 feet (including trailers) aren't allowed.",
  "2026 年因 Crystal Cave Road 9 月 8 日起封路抢修，导览提前在 9 月 7 日结束（原定到 11 月 1 日）；预计 2027 年春末恢复，届时部分时段道路可能仍在施工。": "In 2026, Crystal Cave Road closed for emergency repairs starting September 8, so tours ended early on September 7 (they were scheduled through November 1). Tours are expected to resume in late spring 2027, though roadwork may still affect some times.",
  "Boyden 溶洞导览": "Boyden Cavern Tour",
  "在去 Cedar Grove 的 180 号公路上、Grant Grove 以东约 30 公里，藏在国王峡谷约 600 米高的大理石峭壁里，导览约 45–60 分钟，是水晶洞之外另一处能进的溶洞（属于国家森林，不在公园范围内）。": "Tucked into marble cliffs about 2,000 feet high in Kings Canyon, on Highway 180 on the way to Cedar Grove, about 19 miles east of Grant Grove. Tours take about 45–60 minutes. It's the one cave besides Crystal Cave that you can tour (it's in the national forest, outside the park).",
  "在 boydencavern.com 网上预订，平日上午通常也有现场票，周末和节假日名额少；价格以官网为准。": "Book online at boydencavern.com. Weekday mornings usually have walk-up tickets too, but weekends and holidays have fewer spots. Check the website for prices.",
  "2026 年每天开放到 11 月 8 日，季节开关看 180 号公路和天气。": "In 2026 it's open daily through November 8; seasonal opening and closing depend on Highway 180 and the weather.",
  "Grant Grove / Cedar Grove 骑马": "Guided Horseback Rides",
  "国王峡谷有两处特许经营的马厩：Grant Grove Stables 带 1–2 小时的巨杉林骑行，Cedar Grove Pack Station 沿国王河骑行，从一小时到一整天都有，适合想换种方式看巨杉和峡谷的人。": "Kings Canyon has two concessioner-run stables. Grant Grove Stables leads 1–2-hour rides through the sequoias, and Cedar Grove Pack Station rides along the Kings River, from an hour to a full day. A different way to see the big trees and the canyon.",
  "电话向马厩预约（建议提前订），Cedar Grove 有时能现场报名；有体重和年龄限制，价格以马厩报价为准。": "Call the stables to reserve (booking ahead is recommended); Cedar Grove sometimes takes walk-ups. Weight and age limits apply, and prices are set by the stables.",
  "通常 6 月到 10 月中旬营业，开关日期看天气。": "Usually open June to mid-October; opening and closing dates depend on the weather.",
  "Sequoia Shuttle 进园班车": "Sequoia Shuttle",
  "夏季从 Visalia、Lemon Cove、Three Rivers 发车到 Giant Forest 博物馆的预约班车，接上园内免费班车可到谢尔曼将军树、莫罗岩、新月草甸和 Lodgepole，不用自己开约 1 小时的盘山路，也不用抢停车位。": "A reservation-only summer shuttle from Visalia, Lemon Cove, and Three Rivers to the Giant Forest Museum. Connect to the free in-park shuttles to reach the General Sherman Tree, Moro Rock, Crescent Meadow, and Lodgepole, without driving the roughly hour-long mountain road or hunting for parking.",
  "要提前预约（最晚发车前 90 分钟），往返约 15 美元；园内 Giant Forest 各线路免费、不用预约。": "Reserve ahead (no later than 90 minutes before departure); round trip is about $15. The in-park Giant Forest routes are free and need no reservation.",
  "运营期约为阵亡将士纪念日周末到劳动节（5 月底到 9 月初）；夏季周末和节假日班车运营时，Moro Rock / Crescent Meadow 路对私家车关闭，只能坐班车或步行。": "Runs roughly Memorial Day weekend to Labor Day (late May to early September). On summer weekends and holidays when the shuttle is running, Moro Rock/Crescent Meadow Road is closed to private vehicles; take the shuttle or walk.",
  "Kaweah 河漂流": "Kaweah River Whitewater Rafting",
  "Three Rivers 镇边的 Kaweah 河是加州落差最大的漂流河段之一，春季融雪时有几家公司开半天到一天的激流漂流团，住 Three Rivers 的话顺路就能玩（在公园外）。": "The Kaweah River beside the town of Three Rivers is one of the steepest whitewater runs in California. During spring snowmelt, several outfitters run half-day to full-day rafting trips. An easy add-on if you're staying in Three Rivers (outside the park).",
  "向 Three Rivers 当地的漂流公司预订（如 Kaweah Whitewater Adventures 等），按河段难度和时长收费，以各家官网为准。": "Book with a local Three Rivers outfitter (such as Kaweah Whitewater Adventures). Prices vary by river section and trip length; check each company's website.",
  "季节完全看融雪量：通常 4 月到 6 月初，雪多的年份能到 7 月，雪少的年份可能很短。": "The season depends entirely on snowmelt: usually April to early June, into July in big snow years, and possibly very short in low snow years.",
  "暗夜星空节": "Sequoia & Kings Canyon Dark Sky Festival",
  "公园和 Sequoia Parks Conservancy 每年合办的星空节，连续几晚有天文爱好者架起望远镜带大家看星系和星团，白天还有讲座、电影和音乐活动。": "An annual festival run by the parks and Sequoia Parks Conservancy. Over several nights, amateur astronomers set up telescopes and show you galaxies and star clusters; daytime brings talks, films, and music.",
  "活动免费（园内活动要付公园门票），部分讲座或特别活动可能要提前报名，以 Sequoia Parks Conservancy 官网为准。": "Events are free (the park entrance fee applies for in-park events). Some talks or special events may require advance registration; see the Sequoia Parks Conservancy website.",
  "2026 年在 9 月 11–13 日举办（已结束，首次在 Three Rivers 也设了会场）；2027 年日期以官网公告为准。": "The 2026 festival ran September 11–13 (now over), with a venue in Three Rivers for the first time. Check the website for 2027 dates.",
  "冬季雪地玩耍与雪鞋": "Winter Snowplay & Snowshoeing",
  "冬天巨杉林常被大雪覆盖，公园设了三处玩雪区：红杉这边的 Wolverton（谢尔曼将军树以北约 3 公里），国王峡谷 Grant Grove 附近的 Columbine 和 Big Stump，可以滑雪橇、滑雪圈；巨杉步道也能穿雪鞋走。": "In winter the sequoia groves are often under deep snow. The parks have three snowplay areas for sledding and tubing: Wolverton in Sequoia (about 2 miles north of the General Sherman Tree), and Columbine and Big Stump near Grant Grove in Kings Canyon. You can also snowshoe the sequoia trails.",
  "玩雪区免费；Wuksachi Lodge 营业时通常出租雪鞋和登山杖，Grant Grove Market 卖雪橇等玩雪用品。冬季山路随时可能要求带防滑链，出发前查路况（559-565-3341）。": "Snowplay areas are free. When Wuksachi Lodge is open, it usually rents snowshoes and poles, and Grant Grove Market sells sleds and other snow gear. Tire chains may be required on mountain roads at any time in winter; check road conditions before you go (559-565-3341).",
  "护林员带队的雪鞋徒步 2025 年冬季没有开办，之后是否恢复看 NPS 活动日历。": "Ranger-led snowshoe walks were not offered in winter 2025; check the NPS events calendar to see whether they return.",
  "“国家圣诞树”纪念仪式": "Trek to the Tree",
  "1925 年起每年 12 月第二个周日，在被定为美国“国家圣诞树”的格兰特将军树下举行仪式、献花环，由护林员主持，是国王峡谷最有名的节日活动。": "Every year since 1925, on the second Sunday of December, rangers lead a ceremony and wreath laying beneath the General Grant Tree, designated the Nation's Christmas Tree. It's Kings Canyon's best-known holiday event.",
  "现场参加免费（需付公园门票）；Sanger 商会通常另有含大巴接送的付费套餐。2026 年是 12 月 13 日，遇到暴风雪会取消，山路常要带防滑链。": "Attending is free (the park entrance fee applies). The Sanger Chamber of Commerce usually offers a paid package with bus transportation. In 2026 it's on December 13. It's canceled in blizzards, and chains are often required on the mountain roads.",
  "冬季灰鲸观鲸船": "Winter Gray Whale Watching",
  "灰鲸每年在墨西哥的繁殖潟湖和白令海之间往返，12 月中下旬到次年 3 月中旬最常经过圣巴巴拉海峡；Island Packers 从 Ventura 和 Oxnard 开约 3–3.5 小时的观鲸船，海豚几乎每趟都能看到。": "Gray whales migrate each year between their breeding lagoons in Mexico and the Bering Sea, passing through the Santa Barbara Channel most often from mid-to-late December to mid-March. Island Packers runs 3–3.5-hour whale-watching trips from Ventura and Oxnard, and dolphins show up on almost every trip.",
  "向 Island Packers 网上预订，冬季观鲸船约 12 月到 4 月中旬运营，票价以官网为准；Santa Barbara 港也有其他观鲸船公司。": "Book online with Island Packers. Winter whale-watching trips run about December to mid-April; check the website for fares. Other whale-watching companies operate out of Santa Barbara Harbor.",
  "夏季蓝鲸与座头鲸观鲸船": "Summer Blue & Humpback Whale Cruise",
  "夏天海峡里的涌升流带来大量磷虾，地球上最大的动物蓝鲸，以及座头鲸、长须鲸会来这里觅食；Island Packers 的全天不登岛观鲸船（约 10:00 到 15:00 或 16:00）开到更远的海域去找。": "In summer, upwelling in the channel brings huge swarms of krill, drawing blue whales (the largest animals on Earth), humpbacks, and fin whales to feed. Island Packers' full-day whale-watching trips (no island landing, roughly 10 a.m. to 3 or 4 p.m.) head farther offshore to find them.",
  "成人约 90 美元、55 岁以上约 85 美元、3–12 岁约 74 美元，向 Island Packers 预订；看到鲸不保证，去登岛的船上也常能遇到鲸。": "About $90 for adults, $85 for ages 55 and up, and $74 for ages 3–12; book with Island Packers. Sightings aren't guaranteed, and whales often turn up on the island boats too.",
  "阿纳卡帕岛巨型金鸡菊花季": "Giant Coreopsis Bloom",
  "巨型金鸡菊是加州海岸和海峡群岛特有的“树状”菊科植物，平时像一片枯树桩，冬季雨后长叶开花，通常 1 月下旬到 3 月最盛；Anacapa、Santa Barbara 和 San Miguel 岛开得最好，花季时 Anacapa 满岛金黄。": "Giant coreopsis is a treelike sunflower found only on the California coast and the Channel Islands. Most of the year it looks like a field of dead stumps, but after winter rains it leafs out and blooms, usually peaking from late January through March. Anacapa, Santa Barbara, and San Miguel islands put on the best show, and at peak bloom Anacapa turns gold.",
  "坐 Island Packers 的 Anacapa 一日游船；冬春每周班次少、风浪大容易停航，行程里要留机动日。雨水多的年份开得最好。": "Take an Island Packers day trip to Anacapa. In winter and spring there are only a few trips a week, and rough seas often cancel them, so leave a spare day in your itinerary. Wet years bring the best bloom.",
  "西美鸥繁殖季": "Western Gull Nesting Season",
  "Anacapa 岛是全世界最大的西美鸥繁殖地，4 月底到 7 月步道两旁都是鸟巢和毛茸茸的雏鸟，亲鸟会大声鸣叫、俯冲护巢，场面很热闹。": "Anacapa Island has the largest western gull breeding colony in the world. From late April through July, nests and fluffy chicks line both sides of the trail, and the parents call loudly and dive at anyone who comes close. It's a lively scene.",
  "坐 Anacapa 一日游船即可；经过鸟巢别停留太久，戴顶帽子，鸟多时气味也比较重。": "A day trip to Anacapa is all you need. Don't linger near nests, wear a hat, and expect a strong smell when the birds are thick.",
  "海蚀洞皮划艇": "Sea Cave Kayaking",
  "在 Santa Cruz 岛蝎子湾跟授权向导划海上皮划艇，钻进悬崖下的海蚀洞、穿过海藻林，没有经验也能参加；全年都有团，8–10 月风浪最小、海水最清。": "Paddle sea kayaks with an authorized guide at Scorpion Anchorage on Santa Cruz Island, slipping into sea caves under the cliffs and through kelp forests. No experience needed. Tours run year-round; August–October brings the calmest seas and clearest water.",
  "向 Channel Islands Adventure Company（805-884-9283）预订向导团，皮划艇已放在岛上，船票另向 Island Packers 买（要坐早班船、订下午较晚的回程）；自己带或在大陆租的皮划艇要提前打电话订船上运输位，蝎子湾每天限 18 条。": "Book a guided tour with Channel Islands Adventure Company (805-884-9283); the kayaks are already on the island. Buy your boat ticket separately from Island Packers (take an early boat out and book a late-afternoon return). If you bring your own kayak or rent one on the mainland, call ahead to reserve space for it on the boat; Scorpion is limited to 18 kayaks a day.",
  "天气不好向导公司会取消，可以改期或退款。": "Guide companies cancel in bad weather; you can reschedule or get a refund.",
  "蝎子湾海藻林浮潜": "Snorkeling at Scorpion Anchorage",
  "蝎子湾码头边的海藻林是海峡群岛最方便的浮潜点，常能看到橙色的加州宝石鱼（Garibaldi）、海星和海狮；夏末到 10 月水温最高（约 18°C 上下）、能见度最好。": "The kelp forest beside the Scorpion Anchorage pier is the easiest snorkeling spot in the Channel Islands, often with bright orange garibaldi, sea stars, and sea lions. Late summer through October brings the warmest water (around 64°F) and the best visibility.",
  "岛上不租任何装备，面镜、脚蹼和防寒服要在大陆租好带上船；也可以报 Channel Islands Adventure Company 的浮潜团（10 岁以上、要会游泳并有浮潜经验）。": "No gear is rented on the island. Rent a mask, fins, and wetsuit on the mainland and bring them on the boat. You can also join a Channel Islands Adventure Company snorkel tour (ages 10 and up; you must be able to swim and have snorkeling experience).",
  "彩绘洞海上巡游": "Painted Cave Cruise",
  "Santa Cruz 岛西北岸的 Painted Cave 是世界上最大、最深的海蚀洞之一，洞口岩壁上是彩色的岩层和地衣；海况好时船会直接开进洞里。": "Painted Cave, on the northwest shore of Santa Cruz Island, is one of the largest and deepest sea caves in the world, its entrance walls streaked with colorful rock layers and lichens. In good conditions, the boat goes right inside.",
  "订 Island Packers 早上 8:30 出发的 Prisoners Harbor 一日游时可以加购 Painted Cave（加价以官网为准）；Santa Rosa 岛和 San Miguel 岛一日游的回程也会绕过去，不另收费。": "When you book Island Packers' 8:30 a.m. Prisoners Harbor day trip, you can add Painted Cave (see the website for the extra cost). Day trips to Santa Rosa and San Miguel islands also swing by on the way back at no extra charge.",
  "能不能进洞看当天海况，风浪大时只在洞外看或取消。": "Whether the boat can go in depends on the day's sea conditions; in rough water it stays outside, or the cave visit is canceled.",
  "阿纳卡帕岛沿岸巡游": "Anacapa Shoreline Cruise",
  "不登岛的约 3–3.5 小时巡游，沿 Anacapa 岛海岸看拱门岩、海狮和海豚，季节对时也有鲸；适合带小孩、行动不便或不想爬 157 级台阶的人，也是 Anacapa 靠不了岸时的替代。": "A 3–3.5-hour cruise with no landing, following the Anacapa shoreline past Arch Rock, sea lions, and dolphins, plus whales in season. Good with young kids, for anyone with limited mobility or who'd rather skip the 157 steps, and as a fallback when boats can't land on Anacapa.",
  "成人约 52 美元、55 岁以上约 49 美元、3–12 岁约 38 美元，Ventura 和 Oxnard 都有班次，全年运营但淡季班次少；有时和登岛船同一班，船会先在岛上放下登岛的乘客。": "About $52 for adults, $49 for ages 55 and up, and $38 for ages 3–12. Departures from both Ventura and Oxnard, year-round but with fewer trips in the off-season. Sometimes it shares a boat with the island trip, dropping off landing passengers first.",
  "罗斯福马鹿发情季": "Roosevelt Elk Rut",
  "8 月下旬到 10 月是罗斯福马鹿的发情期，公鹿顶着大角在草原上高声鸣叫、争夺母鹿群，Elk Prairie、Elk Meadow 和 Gold Bluffs Beach 一带最容易看到；这时公鹿脾气暴躁，比平时更要离远。": "From late August through October, Roosevelt elk are in rut: bulls with big antlers bugle across the prairies and compete for herds of cows. Elk Prairie, Elk Meadow, and Gold Bluffs Beach are the most reliable spots. Bulls are aggressive now, so give them even more room than usual.",
  "免费、不用预约；清晨和傍晚最活跃，至少隔开约 23 米（一辆校车的长度），用长焦或望远镜看，别在路中间停车。": "Free, no reservation needed. Elk are most active in the early morning and evening. Stay at least 75 feet away (about the length of a school bus), use a telephoto lens or binoculars, and don't stop in the middle of the road.",
  "灰鲸迁徙": "Gray Whale Migration",
  "每年 11–12 月灰鲸南下去墨西哥、3–4 月北上回阿拉斯加，都会贴着海岸经过；在克拉马斯河口观景台和海岸环线的 High Bluff 观景台常能看到喷出的水柱，晴天海面平静时离岸只有几百米。": "Gray whales pass close to shore heading south to Mexico in November–December and north to Alaska in March–April. From the Klamath River Overlook and the High Bluff Overlook on Coastal Drive you can often see their spouts; on calm, clear days they may be only a few hundred yards offshore.",
  "免费，带上望远镜，选无风的晴天上午；高峰期护林员有时会在观景台办观鲸活动，看 NPS 活动日历。": "Free. Bring binoculars and pick a calm, clear morning. During peak migration, rangers sometimes host whale-watching programs at the overlooks; check the NPS events calendar.",
  "红杉林下杜鹃花季": "Rhododendron Bloom",
  "5 月到 6 月中旬，太平洋杜鹃在红杉林下开出一团团粉紫色的花，巨树配花海是这个季节才有的画面，伯德·约翰逊夫人林是最有名的观赏地。": "From May to mid-June, Pacific rhododendrons bloom in clusters of pink and purple beneath the redwoods, a pairing of giant trees and flowers you only see this time of year. Lady Bird Johnson Grove is the best-known place to see them.",
  "免费；开花早晚每年差一两周，伯德·约翰逊夫人林停车场中午前后常满，尽量早上去。": "Free. Bloom timing shifts by a week or two from year to year. The Lady Bird Johnson Grove lot often fills around midday, so go in the morning.",
  "Smith 河护林员皮划艇": "Ranger-led Smith River Kayak Tour",
  "夏季水位合适时，护林员带队坐双人充气皮划艇漂约 5 公里的 Smith 河（加州最大的自由流淌水系，一到二级小急流），边划边讲河流和红杉的关系，全程约 3 小时；同一季节还有护林员带的 Smith 河浮潜活动。": "In summer, when water levels allow, rangers lead trips in two-person inflatable kayaks down about 3 miles of the Smith River (California's largest free-flowing river system, with Class I–II rapids), talking about how the river and the redwoods depend on each other. Trips last about 3 hours. Rangers also lead Smith River snorkel programs in the same season.",
  "活动免费，报名时收 30 美元装备押金（结束后退还），每场开放前 10 天通过 Redwood Parks Conservancy 的链接报名；10 岁以上、会在流水中游泳，体重 23–100 公斤，每组最多 4 人，中午 12 点在 Jedediah Smith 日间使用区集合。": "Free, with a $30 equipment deposit at registration (refunded afterward). Registration for each trip opens 10 days ahead through a Redwood Parks Conservancy link. Ages 10 and up; you must be able to swim in moving water and weigh 50–220 pounds. Groups of up to four; meet at noon at the Jedediah Smith Day Use Area.",
  "只在人手和水位允许时举办，2025 年因水位低 7 月底就停办；每年的日期以 NPS 公告为准。": "Offered only when staffing and water levels allow; in 2025, low water ended the program in late July. Check NPS announcements for each year's dates.",
  "潮池观察与护林员导览": "Tidepool Walks",
  "退潮时礁石海滩的石缝里能看到海星、海葵和寄居蟹，Enderts Beach 是园区潮池最好的地方之一；5 月中到 9 月中护林员会按潮汐安排 1–2 小时的潮池导览。": "At low tide, the crevices of rocky beaches hold sea stars, anemones, and hermit crabs. Enderts Beach is one of the best tidepooling spots in the parks. From mid-May to mid-September, rangers lead 1–2-hour tidepool walks timed to the tides.",
  "免费、不用预约，日期跟着潮汐定，看 NPS 活动日历；自己去先查 Crescent City 潮汐表，最低潮前后一小时最好，穿能湿水的防滑鞋。": "Free, no reservation needed. Dates follow the tides; check the NPS events calendar. On your own, check the Crescent City tide table first; the hour on either side of low tide is best. Wear grippy shoes that can get wet.",
  "Trees of Mystery 红杉林缆车": "Trees of Mystery SkyTrail",
  "Klamath 以北 101 号公路边的私营景点（不在公园范围内），门口是巨大的伐木工 Paul Bunyan 和蓝牛雕像，坐约 10 分钟的 SkyTrail 缆车越过红杉林到山顶观景台，再沿林间步道走下来，适合带孩子。": "A privately owned attraction on Highway 101 north of Klamath (outside the park), with giant statues of Paul Bunyan and Babe the Blue Ox at the entrance. Ride the SkyTrail gondola about 10 minutes over the redwoods to a hilltop viewing deck, then walk back down on a forest trail. Good with kids.",
  "现场买票，2026 年成人约 30 美元、60 岁以上约 25 美元、3–12 岁约 15 美元，当天可以反复坐缆车；开放时间随季节变化，以官网为准。": "Buy tickets on site. In 2026, about $30 for adults, $25 for ages 60 and up, and $15 for ages 3–12, with unlimited gondola rides that day. Hours change with the seasons; check the website.",
  "公园每年降雪约 9 米，冬天只能开车到西南入口的游客中心；每逢周末护林员带队穿雪鞋走进雪原，边走边讲火山和动物怎么过冬，约 2 小时，不需要经验。": "The park gets about 30 feet of snow a year, and in winter you can drive only as far as the visitor center at the southwest entrance. On weekends, rangers lead snowshoe walks out into the snowfields, talking about the volcanoes and how animals get through the winter. About 2 hours; no experience needed.",
  "免费，不能提前预约：当天在 Kohm Yah-mah-nee 游客中心领票，每场限 40 人，雪鞋捐 1 美元即可借用；8 岁以上，未成年人要有成人陪同。去之前打电话（530-595-4480）确认当天是否举行。": "Free; no advance reservations. Pick up a ticket at the Kohm Yah-mah-nee Visitor Center the day of the walk; each walk is limited to 40 people. Borrow snowshoes for a $1 donation. Ages 8 and up; minors must be with an adult. Call ahead (530-595-4480) to confirm the walk is on that day.",
  "2026 年是 1 月 3 日到 3 月 29 日的周六、周日 13:30–15:30；2027 年安排以 NPS 公告为准，雪不够或人手不足会取消。": "In 2026, walks ran Saturdays and Sundays, 1:30–3:30 p.m., from January 3 to March 29. Check NPS announcements for 2027; walks are canceled if there isn't enough snow or staff.",
  "春季无车公路徒步骑行": "Hike and Bike the Highway",
  "每年春天公园要清掉公路上 9–12 米厚的积雪，清完一段就先对行人和自行车开放、还不通汽车，可以在两侧雪墙之间骑车或步行；最后通车的一段通常是 Devastated Area 到拉森峰停车场之间的约 19 公里。": "Each spring the park plows 30–40 feet of snow off the highway. As each section is cleared, it opens to walkers and cyclists before cars, so you can ride or walk between walls of snow. The last section to open is usually the roughly 12 miles between the Devastated Area and the Lassen Peak parking area.",
  "免费、不用报名，没有固定活动日；哪几段能走看 NPS 网站上的清雪进度表和公告，可以牵绳遛狗。": "Free, no registration, and no set event date. Check the plowing progress and announcements on the NPS website to see which sections are open. Leashed dogs are allowed.",
  "开放时间完全看当年雪量和清雪进度，全线通车后就不再有无车时段；2026 年全线已通车。": "Timing depends entirely on the year's snowpack and plowing progress; once the whole road opens to cars, the car-free window ends. In 2026 the road is fully open.",
  "拉森暗夜星空派对": "Dark Skies at Lassen",
  "公园每年夏天在 Kohm Yah-mah-nee 游客中心后院办的星空之夜，天文爱好者架起望远镜，护林员讲星座和天文，拉森远离城市灯光，银河非常清楚。": "An annual summer night of stargazing behind the Kohm Yah-mah-nee Visitor Center. Amateur astronomers set up telescopes and rangers talk about constellations and astronomy. Far from city lights, Lassen has a strikingly clear Milky Way.",
  "免费、不用票或预约（要有公园门票）；带保暖衣物、毯子和红光手电。平时夏季也有零星的夜空观测活动，看游客中心公告。": "Free; no tickets or reservations (the park entrance fee applies). Bring warm layers, a blanket, and a red flashlight. Occasional night sky programs also run through the summer; check visitor center notices.",
  "2026 年在 8 月 7–8 日举办（已结束）；2027 年日期以 NPS 活动页为准。": "The 2026 event was held August 7–8 (now over). Check the NPS events page for 2027 dates.",
  "曼萨尼塔湖划皮划艇": "Kayaking on Manzanita Lake",
  "曼萨尼塔湖只许无动力船，湖面平静，划到湖中间回头就是拉森峰和 Chaos Crags 的倒影，早上风小时最好；Butte Lake、Summit Lake 也能自带船划。": "Manzanita Lake allows only non-motorized boats, so the water stays calm. Paddle to the middle and look back at Lassen Peak and Chaos Crags reflected in the lake; mornings, before the wind picks up, are best. You can also bring your own boat to Butte Lake and Summit Lake.",
  "约 5 月下旬到 9 月，在 Manzanita Lake 露营商店（10:00–16:00）租单人或双人皮划艇，含救生衣，价格见 lassenlodging.com；海伦湖、Emerald Lake、Reflection Lake 禁止划船。": "From about late May to September, rent single or double kayaks, life jackets included, at the Manzanita Lake Camper Store (10 a.m.–4 p.m.); see lassenlodging.com for prices. Boating isn't allowed on Lake Helen, Emerald Lake, or Reflection Lake.",
  "高山野花季": "Wildflower Season",
  "野花跟着雪线往上开：曼萨尼塔湖和 Warner Valley 一带 5 月下旬到 7 月初，西南区 6–7 月（磨坊溪瀑布步道的黄色骡耳菊），Summit Lake 一带 6 月下旬到 8 月初，拉森峰高处要到 7 月下旬到 9 月。": "Wildflowers follow the snowline uphill: late May to early July around Manzanita Lake and Warner Valley, June–July in the southwest area (yellow mule's ears along the Mill Creek Falls Trail), late June to early August around Summit Lake, and late July to September high on Lassen Peak.",
  "免费；花期每年随积雪早晚变化，出发前可以向游客中心打听当周开得最好的步道。": "Free. Bloom times shift each year with the snowpack; before you go, ask at a visitor center which trails are best that week.",
  "火山口湖每年平均降雪约 13 米，冬天护林员带队穿雪鞋在湖边的森林和雪原里走 1.6–3 公里，讲动植物怎么熬过漫长的雪季；雪鞋免费提供，不需要经验。": "Crater Lake averages about 43 feet of snow a year. In winter, rangers lead snowshoe walks of 1–2 miles through the forest and snowfields near the rim, talking about how plants and animals survive the long snow season. Snowshoes are provided free; no experience needed.",
  "免费（只收冬季门票每车 20 美元），名额有限，要提前打电话 541-594-3100 预约；8 岁以上。通常 11 月下旬到 4 月的周六、周日和节假日 12:30 出发，寒假和春假期间平日也有。": "Free (you pay only the winter entrance fee of $20 per vehicle). Space is limited, so reserve ahead by phone at 541-594-3100. Ages 8 and up. Walks usually start at 12:30 p.m. on Saturdays, Sundays, and holidays from late November through April, with weekday walks during winter and spring breaks.",
  "雪不够或天气太差会取消；去 Rim Village 的路封闭时改在公园总部附近走。": "Canceled if there isn't enough snow or the weather is too severe. When the road to Rim Village is closed, walks move to the area around park headquarters.",
  "环湖观光小巴": "Crater Lake Trolley",
  "特许经营商的封闭式观光小巴，从 Rim Village 出发沿 Rim Drive 开约 2 小时，在几个主要观景点停车拍照，导游一路讲马扎马火山和湖泊研究，不用自己开山路、找车位。": "A concessioner-run enclosed trolley leaves Rim Village and travels Rim Drive for about 2 hours, stopping at several major overlooks for photos while the guide talks about Mount Mazama and lake research. No mountain driving or hunting for parking.",
  "在 craterlaketrolley.net 预订或电话 541-882-1896，也可以在 Rim Village 的售票车上买当天余票；成人约 44 美元、65 岁以上约 42 美元、6–13 岁约 25 美元，6 岁以下免费。": "Book at craterlaketrolley.net or call 541-882-1896; you can also buy any remaining same-day seats at the ticket van in Rim Village. About $44 for adults, $42 for ages 65 and up, and $25 for ages 6–13; kids under 6 ride free.",
  "通常 6 月下旬到 9 月、10:00–15:00 每小时一班（看天气）；2026 年因东环湖路施工，路线改为顺时针开到 Skell Head 再原路返回。": "Usually runs late June through September, hourly 10 a.m.–3 p.m. (weather permitting). In 2026, because of construction on East Rim Drive, the route runs clockwise to Skell Head and returns the same way.",
  "湖上游船与巫师岛": "Boat Tours & Wizard Island",
  "平时夏季每天有游船绕火山口湖一圈，也有船送人登上湖中的巫师岛爬火山锥；上船要先走 Cleetwood Cove 步道下到湖边。": "In a normal summer, daily boat tours circle Crater Lake, and other boats take visitors to Wizard Island to climb its cinder cone. To board, you first hike down the Cleetwood Cove Trail to the shore.",
  "恢复后通过特许经营商 Explor Crater Lake 订票，旺季要提前订；3 岁以上才能上船。": "Once tours resume, book through the concessioner Explor Crater Lake; reserve early for peak season. Passengers must be 3 or older.",
  "Cleetwood Cove 步道和码头 2026 年起整体重建，2026–2028 年没有游船、也上不了巫师岛，NPS 预计 2029 年恢复；这期间看湖只能在环湖公路和各条山顶步道上。": "The Cleetwood Cove Trail and marina are being completely rebuilt starting in 2026. There are no boat tours or Wizard Island trips in 2026–2028, and NPS expects them to resume in 2029. Until then, you can see the lake only from Rim Drive and the trails along the rim.",
  "“骑行环湖”无车日": "Ride the Rim",
  "往年 9 月会选两个周六，把整条东环湖路（约 40 公里）只留给骑车和步行的人，不用和汽车抢路，可以慢慢骑或走一段看湖。": "In past years, the park set aside two Saturdays in September when all of East Rim Drive (about 25 miles) was open only to cyclists and walkers. With no cars to share the road with, you could ride or walk a stretch at your own pace and take in the lake.",
  "免费、不用报名（要付公园门票）；环湖路坡长，累计爬升约 1,150 米，量力而行。": "Free, no registration (the park entrance fee applies). The road has long climbs, with about 3,750 feet of total elevation gain, so know your limits.",
  "2026 年因东环湖路、Cleetwood Cove 等多项工程取消，下一届还没定日期，以 NPS 骑行页面公告为准。": "Canceled in 2026 because of construction on East Rim Drive, at Cleetwood Cove, and elsewhere. No date has been set for the next one; watch the NPS bicycling page for announcements.",
  "夏季护林员讲解与夜空活动": "Summer Ranger Talks & Night Sky Programs",
  "6 月下旬到 9 月中旬，护林员几乎每天在 Rim Village 的辛诺特观景台讲火山口湖的形成，傍晚在 Crater Lake Lodge 露台讲座，夏季还有夜空观测活动；园区远离城市，银河很清楚。": "From late June to mid-September, rangers give talks almost daily at Sinnott Memorial Overlook in Rim Village on how Crater Lake formed, plus evening talks on the Crater Lake Lodge terrace and, in summer, night sky programs. Far from any city, the park has a strikingly clear Milky Way.",
  "免费、不用预约，当天的时间表贴在游客中心，也可以问 Steel 游客中心。": "Free, no reservation needed. The day's schedule is posted at visitor centers, or ask at the Steel Visitor Center.",
  "Castle Crest 野花草甸": "Castle Crest Wildflowers",
  "公园总部旁一条约 0.8 公里的小环线，穿过泉水滋润的草甸，盛夏满是猴面花、羽扇豆等野花，是火山口湖看野花最方便的地方；普莱克尼瀑布步道沿途夏天也有很多花。": "A short loop of about half a mile next to park headquarters, through spring-fed meadows full of monkeyflower, lupine, and other wildflowers in midsummer. It's the easiest place to see wildflowers at Crater Lake, and the Plaikni Falls Trail also has plenty of flowers in summer.",
  "免费；从 Steel 游客中心旁的步道口出发，花期看当年积雪，通常 7 月下旬到 8 月最好。": "Free. Start from the trailhead next to the Steel Visitor Center. Bloom timing depends on the year's snowpack; late July through August is usually best.",
  "雷尼尔山的高山草甸是美国最有名的野花地之一：多数年份 7 月中旬开始开花，8 月初 Paradise 和 Sunrise 的草甸最壮观，羽扇豆、火焰草、熊草铺满山坡，背后就是冰川雪山。": "Mount Rainier's subalpine meadows are among the best-known wildflower displays in the U.S. In most years the bloom starts in mid-July and peaks in early August in the meadows at Paradise and Sunrise, when lupine, paintbrush, and beargrass cover the slopes below the glaciers.",
  "免费；花季正是旺季，周末 Paradise 停车场上午就会满，尽量平日早上到。NPS 夏季在网站上更新各区的开花情况，只走步道、别踩进草甸。": "Free. Bloom season is also peak season: the Paradise lot fills by midmorning on weekends, so aim for an early weekday arrival. In summer, NPS posts bloom updates for each area on its website. Stay on the trails and off the meadows.",
  "2026 年的野花报告已于 9 月初结束，下一季从 2027 年夏天开始更新。": "The 2026 wildflower reports ended in early September; updates for the next season begin in summer 2027.",
  "秋季草甸红叶": "Fall Color in the Meadows",
  "8 月底以后高山草甸开始转色，9 月下旬到 10 月初越橘和花楸把 Paradise、倒影湖一带的山坡染成红色和金色，人比夏天少，也是秋季看雪山倒影的好时候。": "After late August the subalpine meadows start to turn, and from late September to early October huckleberry and mountain ash paint the slopes around Paradise and Reflection Lakes red and gold. There are fewer people than in summer, and it's a good time for reflections of the mountain.",
  "免费；10 月起随时可能下雪，Stevens Canyon Road 等道路在 11 月前后封闭，出发前查 NPS 路况。": "Free. Snow can fall any time from October on, and Stevens Canyon Road and other roads close around November; check NPS road status before you go.",
  "天堂区护林员雪鞋徒步": "Paradise Ranger-Guided Snowshoe Walks",
  "冬天 Paradise 积雪常有好几米深，护林员带队穿雪鞋在雪原和林间走约 2.4 公里、约 2 小时，讲动植物和人怎么适应严冬，雪鞋由公园免费借用，不需要经验。": "In winter the snow at Paradise is often many feet deep. Rangers lead snowshoe walks of about 1.5 miles (about 2 hours) through snowfields and forest, talking about how plants, animals, and people adapt to harsh winters. The park lends snowshoes for free; no experience needed.",
  "免费、先到先得：通常 12 月下旬到 3 月的周六、周日 11:00 出发，提前 1 小时在天堂游客中心服务台登记，每场限 25 人、8 岁以上。冬季（11 月 1 日–5 月 1 日）所有车辆进园都必须随车带防滑链，Longmire 到 Paradise 的路每晚关闭。": "Free, first come, first served. Walks usually start at 11 a.m. on Saturdays and Sundays from late December through March. Sign up at the information desk in the Paradise visitor center an hour ahead; each walk is limited to 25 people, ages 8 and up. In winter (November 1–May 1), all vehicles entering the park must carry tire chains, and the road from Longmire to Paradise closes every night.",
  "官方的 Paradise 雪橇区 2025–26 冬季没有开放；2026–27 冬季的雪鞋徒步和雪橇区安排看 NPS 冬季活动页。": "The official Paradise sledding area did not open in winter 2025–26. Check the NPS winter recreation page for 2026–27 snowshoe walks and sledding.",
  "向导带队攀登雷尼尔山": "Guided Summit Climb",
  "雷尼尔山（4,392 米）是美国本土冰川最多的山，登顶要爬升 2,700 多米、走冰川，没有技术经验的人可以报授权向导公司的多日登顶团，先上一天冰川技术课再冲顶。": "Mount Rainier (14,410 feet) is the most heavily glaciated peak in the contiguous U.S. The summit takes roughly 9,000 feet of elevation gain and glacier travel. Climbers without technical experience can join a multi-day guided climb with an authorized guide service, starting with a day of glacier skills training before the summit push.",
  "授权向导公司有 RMI Expeditions、Alpine Ascents International、International Mountain Guides；RMI 的 4 天登顶团 2026 年约 2,595–2,995 美元。另需每人 82 美元的年度登山费和夏季每晚 12 美元的荒野许可（向导团通常代办）。": "The authorized guide services are RMI Expeditions, Alpine Ascents International, and International Mountain Guides. RMI's 4-day summit climb costs about $2,595–2,995 in 2026. On top of that you need an $82 annual climbing fee per person and, in summer, a $12-per-night wilderness permit (guide services usually handle these).",
  "登山旺季是 5 月到 9 月中旬，热门日期提前几个月就满；需要很好的体能，登顶日要连续走 10–14 小时。": "The climbing season runs from May to mid-September, and popular dates fill months in advance. You need to be very fit: summit day means 10–14 hours of nonstop effort.",
  "Crystal Mountain 雷尼尔山缆车": "Mt. Rainier Gondola at Crystal Mountain",
  "东北入口外 Crystal Mountain 滑雪场的缆车（不在公园内），约 10 分钟升到海拔约 2,100 米的山顶，正对雷尼尔山东北面，山顶有餐厅，不爬山也能看到近在眼前的冰川雪山。": "The gondola at Crystal Mountain ski area, outside the northeast entrance (not in the park), rises in about 10 minutes to a summit at about 6,900 feet, facing the northeast side of Mount Rainier. There's a restaurant at the top, and you get a close-up view of the glaciers without hiking.",
  "在 Crystal Mountain 官网买票，提前两天以上网上买比现场便宜 5 美元；票价以官网为准。冬季滑雪季缆车也运营。": "Buy tickets on the Crystal Mountain website; buying online at least two days ahead saves $5 over the walk-up price. Check the website for fares. The gondola also runs during the winter ski season.",
  "2026 年夏季：5 月 22 日–6 月 21 日只在周五到周日开，6 月 26 日–8 月 30 日每天开，9 月 4–20 日又只在周末开（夏季已结束）。": "Summer 2026: Fridays–Sundays only May 22–June 21, daily June 26–August 30, and weekends only again September 4–20 (the summer season is over).",
  "飓风岭冬季雪上活动": "Hurricane Ridge Winter Recreation",
  "冬天飓风岭（海拔约 1,600 米）常被厚雪覆盖，可以跟护林员穿雪鞋走一小段、自己越野滑雪或穿雪鞋，山脊上还有一个小型滑雪场和滑雪圈场地，8 岁以下的孩子可以在儿童玩雪区免费滑雪橇。": "In winter, Hurricane Ridge (about 5,250 feet) is often under deep snow. Join a ranger for a short snowshoe walk, cross-country ski or snowshoe on your own, or try the small ski area and tubing area on the ridge. Kids under 8 can sled for free in the children's snowplay area.",
  "护林员雪鞋徒步免费：周六、周日 13:30 出发，13:00 在停车场的临时游客服务站集合，每场限 20 人，雪鞋由公园提供；滑雪和滑雪圈在停车场的滑雪场售票车买票。山上没有餐饮、饮用水和装备租借，吃的和保暖衣物要自带。": "Ranger-led snowshoe walks are free. They start at 1:30 p.m. on Saturdays and Sundays, meeting at 1 p.m. at the temporary visitor information station in the parking lot; each walk is limited to 20 people, and the park provides snowshoes. Buy ski and tubing tickets at the ski area's ticket trailer in the parking lot. There's no food, drinking water, or gear rental on the ridge, so bring your own food and warm clothes.",
  "冬季约 11 月下旬到 3 月底，Hurricane Ridge Road 一般只在周五到周日（和部分节假日）9:00–16:00 开放上山，风雪大时随时封路；11 月 1 日到 4 月 1 日所有车辆必须随车带防滑链。": "The winter season runs roughly late November to late March. Hurricane Ridge Road is generally open to uphill traffic only Fridays–Sundays (and some holidays), 9 a.m.–4 p.m., and can close at any time in wind or snow. From November 1 to April 1, all vehicles must carry tire chains.",
  "飓风岭星空观测": "Hurricane Ridge Astronomy Program",
  "夏季晴朗的夜晚，天文志愿者在飓风岭架起望远镜，带大家看星系、星云和行星；公园 95% 是荒野、几乎没有人造光，是西雅图周边看银河最方便的地方之一。": "On clear summer nights, volunteer astronomers set up telescopes at Hurricane Ridge to show you galaxies, nebulae, and planets. With 95% of the park designated wilderness and almost no artificial light, it's one of the easiest places near Seattle to see the Milky Way.",
  "免费、不用预约，只在天气好时举办，具体日期看 NPS 活动日历或夏季的 Bugler 公园报；山顶夜里很冷，带厚外套。": "Free, no reservation needed, and held only in good weather. Check the NPS events calendar or the summer Bugler park newspaper for dates. Nights on the ridge are cold; bring a warm jacket.",
  "索尔达克鲑鱼洄游": "Sol Duc Salmon Run",
  "秋天银鲑逆流而上回到出生的溪流产卵，在 Sol Duc 路边的 Salmon Cascades 观景台能看到鲑鱼一次次跃上激流，9 月下旬到 10 月初最容易看到，去索尔达克瀑布的路上顺路。": "In fall, coho salmon swim upstream to spawn in the streams where they hatched. At the Salmon Cascades overlook along the Sol Duc road you can watch them leap the rapids again and again; late September to early October is the best time. It's right on the way to Sol Duc Falls.",
  "免费；观景台就在 Sol Duc Hot Springs Road 边，停车后走几步就到。Sol Duc 路冬季常因冰雪封闭，出发前查路况（360-565-3131）。": "Free. The overlook is right beside Sol Duc Hot Springs Road, a few steps from the parking area. The Sol Duc road often closes for snow and ice in winter; check road conditions before you go (360-565-3131).",
  "海岸潮池观察": "Tidepooling",
  "奥林匹克海岸的礁石潮池里有巨型绿海葵、紫色海星和海胆，Kalaloch 的 Beach 4 和 Rialto 的 Hole-in-the-Wall 最有名，Second Beach、Ruby Beach 也很好；夏季护林员会按潮汐带潮池导览。": "Tidepools along the Olympic coast hold giant green anemones, purple sea stars, and sea urchins. Beach 4 at Kalaloch and Hole-in-the-Wall at Rialto are the best known, and Second Beach and Ruby Beach are also good. In summer, rangers lead tidepool walks timed to the tides.",
  "免费；一定要赶“负潮”（潮高低于 1 英尺），夏季的大退潮多在清晨，出发前查 Destruction Island 潮汐表，穿防滑、能湿水的鞋，只看不摸、不翻石头。": "Free. Time your visit for a minus tide (a tide below 1 foot); in summer the lowest tides usually come in the early morning. Check the Destruction Island tide table before you go, wear grippy shoes that can get wet, and look without touching or turning over rocks.",
  "Mora Road 2026 年 7 月 8 日到 10 月 15 日施工全封，这段时间去不了 Rialto Beach / Hole-in-the-Wall，可以改去 Beach 4 或 Ruby Beach。": "Mora Road is fully closed for construction July 8–October 15, 2026, so Rialto Beach and Hole-in-the-Wall are out of reach during that time; go to Beach 4 or Ruby Beach instead.",
  "天使港出海观鲸": "Port Angeles Whale Watching",
  "5 月中到 10 月，从天使港出海进入胡安·德富卡海峡和萨利希海，常能看到虎鲸、座头鲸和小须鲸（在公园外）；另外每年 4–5 月和 10–11 月灰鲸迁徙时，在 Kalaloch、Rialto 等海滩也可能从岸上看到喷水。": "From mid-May through October, boats from Port Angeles head into the Strait of Juan de Fuca and the Salish Sea, where orcas, humpbacks, and minke whales are common (outside the park). During the gray whale migration in April–May and October–November, you may also see spouts from shore at beaches such as Kalaloch and Rialto.",
  "向天使港的观鲸公司预订：Island Adventures（Port Angeles Whale Watch Co.）约 5 月 14 日到 10 月 31 日开 4–5 小时的船，Puget Sound Express 的半日团约 3–4 小时、2026 年成人约 145 美元；价格以各家官网为准。": "Book with a Port Angeles whale-watching company. Island Adventures (Port Angeles Whale Watch Co.) runs 4–5-hour trips from about May 14 to October 31; Puget Sound Express half-day trips last about 3–4 hours and cost about $145 for adults in 2026. Check each company's website for prices.",
  "新月湖划船": "Paddling on Lake Crescent",
  "新月湖湖水极清、四周是森林山峦，早上风小时划皮划艇或独木舟最舒服，能看清湖底的石头；下午常起风、浪可到 30 厘米以上，要早点回岸。": "Lake Crescent is exceptionally clear and ringed by forested mountains. Mornings, before the wind comes up, are the most pleasant time to kayak or canoe, and you can see the rocks on the bottom. Afternoon winds often build waves of a foot or more, so head back to shore early.",
  "Lake Crescent Lodge 和 Log Cabin Resort 夏季出租皮划艇、独木舟和桨板（价格以特许经营商官网为准），也可以在 Storm King 或 Fairholme 船坡自己下水；湖水常年低于 10°C，一定穿救生衣。": "Lake Crescent Lodge and Log Cabin Resort rent kayaks, canoes, and paddleboards in summer (see the concessioners' websites for prices), or you can launch your own at the Storm King or Fairholme boat ramps. The water stays below 50°F year-round; always wear a life jacket.",
  "迪亚布洛湖游船（Skagit Tours）": "Skagit Tours Diablo Lake Cruises",
  "北瀑布学会和西雅图城市电力合办的湖上游船，从 Diablo 大坝旁的环境学习中心出发，在碧绿的迪亚布洛湖上转一圈，讲冰川地质和水电站历史，不徒步也能深入湖区。": "Lake cruises run jointly by North Cascades Institute and Seattle City Light. They leave from the Environmental Learning Center beside Diablo Dam and loop around the turquoise water of Diablo Lake, covering glacial geology and the history of the hydroelectric project. A way to get deep into the lake country without hiking.",
  "2026 年 7 月 3 日到 9 月 7 日每周三至周日有午餐团（约 3 小时、约 $50）和下午游船（约 2 小时、约 $35），9 月 12–27 日只在周末开；名额少，在 North Cascades Institute 官网提前订。": "July 3–September 7, 2026, Wednesday through Sunday: a lunch cruise (about 3 hours, about $50) and an afternoon cruise (about 2 hours, about $35); September 12–27, weekends only. Space is limited; book ahead on the North Cascades Institute website.",
  "坐船去 Stehekin 小村": "Lady of the Lake to Stehekin",
  "公园管理的 Lake Chelan 国家游憩区北端有个不通公路的小村 Stehekin，只能坐船、坐水上飞机或徒步进去；从 Chelan 坐 Lady of the Lake 渡轮沿约 80 公里长的冰川湖北上，在村里逛面包店、看 Rainbow Falls，当天再坐船回来。": "Stehekin, a small village with no road in, sits at the north end of Lake Chelan National Recreation Area, which the park manages. You can reach it only by boat, floatplane, or on foot. Take the Lady of the Lake ferry from Chelan up the roughly 50-mile glacial lake, visit the bakery, see Rainbow Falls, and catch the boat back the same day.",
  "Lake Chelan Boat Company 全年运营，夏季每天多班、冬季班次少；从 Chelan 出发单程 1.5–4 小时（看船型），当天往返约 $60 起，村里停留 1.5–6 小时，在 ladyofthelake.com 提前订票。": "Lake Chelan Boat Company runs year-round, with several trips a day in summer and fewer in winter. One way from Chelan takes 1.5–4 hours depending on the boat; same-day round trips start at about $60, with 1.5–6 hours in the village. Book ahead at ladyofthelake.com.",
  "2026 年夏季 North Cascades Lodge at Stehekin 整季关闭，只能住私人民宿；Sisi Fire 导致 Stehekin Valley Road 从 Stehekin Valley Ranch 到 High Bridge 一段和 Agnes Gorge 等步道关闭，渡轮照常，出发前看 NPS 火灾和洪水公告。": "In summer 2026, North Cascades Lodge at Stehekin is closed for the season, so private rentals are the only lodging. The Sisi Fire has closed Stehekin Valley Road from Stehekin Valley Ranch to High Bridge, along with Agnes Gorge and other trails. The ferry runs as usual; check NPS fire and flood alerts before you go.",
  "罗斯湖划船和水上出租": "Ross Lake Resort Boat Rentals & Water Taxi",
  "罗斯湖一直伸到加拿大，湖上唯一的住处 Ross Lake Resort 是一排漂在水上的木屋，不住店也可以当天来租皮划艇、独木舟、立桨板或小汽艇，徒步和露营的人可以坐它的水上出租去湖边步道口。": "Ross Lake reaches all the way into Canada. Its only lodging, Ross Lake Resort, is a row of floating cabins. Even if you're not staying, you can come for the day to rent kayaks, canoes, stand-up paddleboards, or small motorboats, and hikers and campers can take its water taxi to trailheads along the lake.",
  "2026 年营业期 6 月 11 日到 10 月 31 日；从 20 号公路 MP 134 的 Ross Dam 步道口下山约 1 英里，在路边电话叫接驳车（$5/人单程），或过坝再走约 2.5 英里；租船 8:00 取、17:30 前还，湖上午后风大，上午早去。": "Open June 11–October 31 in 2026. From the Ross Dam Trailhead at milepost 134 on Highway 20, hike about 1 mile down and call for the shuttle truck from the roadside phone ($5 per person one way), or cross the dam and walk about 2.5 miles. Pick up rental boats at 8 a.m. and return them by 5:30 p.m. Afternoon winds are strong on the lake, so go early.",
  "金色落叶松季": "Golden Larch Season",
  "9 月底到 10 月中旬，20 号公路东侧高山上的亚高山落叶松（alpine larch）变成金黄色，枫树山口环线、蓝湖、Cutthroat Pass 一带最集中，是华盛顿州秋天最热门的徒步。": "From late September to mid-October, the alpine larches high in the mountains along the east side of Highway 20 turn gold, most densely around the Maple Pass Loop, Blue Lake, and Cutthroat Pass. It's the most popular fall hike in Washington.",
  "不用预约，但周末步道口一早就停满；停车要付国家森林日票 $5，或挂 Northwest Forest Pass、国家公园年卡；10 月中下旬可能下雪，出发前查 WSDOT 路况。": "No reservations, but trailhead parking fills early on weekends. Parking requires a $5 national forest day pass, a Northwest Forest Pass, or an America the Beautiful pass. Snow is possible in mid-to-late October; check WSDOT road conditions before you go.",
  "Skagit 河冬季看白头海雕": "Skagit River Bald Eagle Watching",
  "每年冬天几百只白头海雕聚到公园西边的 Skagit 河，吃产完卵的大麻哈鱼（chum salmon），Rockport 到 Marblemount 一段河边的大树和砾石滩最容易看到，12 月中旬到 1 月下旬最多。": "Each winter, hundreds of bald eagles gather on the Skagit River west of the park to feed on spawned-out chum salmon. The big trees and gravel bars between Rockport and Marblemount are the best places to see them, and numbers peak from mid-December to late January.",
  "Rockport 的 Howard Miller Steelhead Park 里有季节性的 Bald Eagle Interpretive Center（约 12 月下旬到 2 月中旬的周末开放，有免费导览步行），1 月每个周末 Concrete、Rockport、Marblemount 一带办 Skagit Eagle Festival；也可以跟漂流公司坐橡皮艇顺流看鹰（约 3 小时，要预订）。": "Howard Miller Steelhead Park in Rockport is home to the seasonal Bald Eagle Interpretive Center (open weekends from about late December to mid-February, with free guided walks). Every weekend in January, the Skagit Eagle Festival takes place around Concrete, Rockport, and Marblemount. You can also float the river with a rafting company to watch the eagles (about 3 hours; reservations required).",
  "马鹿发情季": "Elk Rut",
  "9 月到 10 月上旬是马鹿（elk）的发情季，公鹿在猛犸温泉镇的草坪、麦迪逊河边和吉本草甸一带高声鸣叫、争夺母鹿，清晨和傍晚最容易看到。公鹿这时非常好斗，会冲撞人和车，至少保持 25 码（约 23 米），最好在车里看。": "September to early October is the elk rut. Bulls bugle and compete for cows on the lawns of Mammoth Hot Springs, along the Madison River, and around Gibbon Meadows, and they're easiest to see in the early morning and evening. Bulls are very aggressive now and will charge people and cars. Stay at least 25 yards away, and ideally watch from your car.",
  "野牛发情季": "Bison Rut",
  "7 月中旬到 8 月中旬，野牛大群聚集在海登谷和拉马尔谷繁殖，公牛低吼、打滚扬尘、互相顶撞，比平时热闹得多。公牛这时脾气暴躁，只在车里或 25 码（约 23 米）以外看。": "From mid-July to mid-August, large bison herds gather in Hayden and Lamar valleys to breed. Bulls bellow, roll in the dust, and butt heads, so there's far more going on than usual. Bulls are short-tempered now; watch only from your car or from at least 25 yards away.",
  "冬季拉马尔谷看狼": "Winter Wolf Watching in Lamar Valley",
  "北门到东北门的公路冬季照常通车，狼群在雪地上追猎马鹿、野牛时很显眼，是一年里看狼最好的季节；清晨沿拉马尔谷慢慢开，留意路边架着单筒望远镜的人群。": "The road from the North Entrance to the Northeast Entrance stays open in winter, and wolves stand out against the snow as they hunt elk and bison, making this the best season of the year for wolf watching. Drive slowly through Lamar Valley in the early morning and watch for groups with spotting scopes along the road.",
  "自驾就能去，冬季路面常结冰，要四驱或雪地胎；Gardiner 有向导带的看狼团（配高倍望远镜、熟悉狼群动向），一日团约 $200–400/人，包车更贵。": "You can drive yourself, but winter roads are often icy, so use four-wheel drive or snow tires. Outfitters in Gardiner run guided wolf-watching tours (with high-powered scopes and guides who know the packs' movements); day tours cost about $200–400 per person, and private tours cost more.",
  "冬季雪地车游园": "Snowcoach & Snowmobile Tours",
  "每年 12 月 15 日到次年 3 月中旬，除北门到东北门一段外，园内公路只通雪地车；想看冬天的老忠实、大峡谷，只能跟雪地车（snowcoach）或有向导的雪地摩托团进园。": "From December 15 to mid-March, park roads other than the North Entrance–Northeast Entrance stretch are open only to over-snow vehicles. To see Old Faithful or the Grand Canyon of the Yellowstone in winter, you have to go by snowcoach or on a guided snowmobile tour.",
  "West Yellowstone、Gardiner、Jackson（经南门 Flagg Ranch）都有一日团，雪地车去老忠实约 $190–300/人（不含门票）；也可以提前订冬季营业的 Old Faithful Snow Lodge（2026–27 年冬季约 12 月 16 日到 3 月 7 日）住一两晚。自己骑雪地摩托要参加 NPS 的非商业向导项目抽签。": "Day tours leave from West Yellowstone, Gardiner, and Jackson (via Flagg Ranch at the South Entrance); a snowcoach trip to Old Faithful is about $190–300 per person (entrance fee not included). You can also book a night or two at Old Faithful Snow Lodge, which opens in winter (about December 16 to March 7 for winter 2026–27). To ride your own snowmobile, enter the lottery for the NPS Non-Commercially Guided Snowmobile Access Program.",
  "黄石湖观光游船": "Yellowstone Lake Scenicruise",
  "从湖区 Bridge Bay 码头出发的一小时湖上游船，开到 Stevenson 岛附近，讲湖区历史，能看到老汽船 E.C. Waters 的残骸，常见白头海雕和水鸟。": "A 1-hour cruise from Bridge Bay Marina out to near Stevenson Island, with commentary on the lake's history. You'll see the wreck of the old steamboat E.C. Waters and, often, bald eagles and waterbirds.",
  "2026 年 6 月 12 日到 9 月 20 日每天多班，成人约 $25、3–11 岁约 $14；在 Yellowstone National Park Lodges 官网或电话 307-344-7311 预订，也可以到码头问当天余票。": "Several departures daily June 12–September 20, 2026; about $25 for adults and $14 for ages 3–11. Book on the Yellowstone National Park Lodges website or by phone at 307-344-7311, or ask at the marina about same-day seats.",
  "Roosevelt 骑马和牛仔晚餐": "Horseback Rides & Old West Dinner Cookout (Roosevelt)",
  "东北角 Roosevelt Lodge 旁的马厩夏季有 1–2 小时的骑马团；牛仔晚餐（Old West Dinner Cookout）是骑马、坐驿站马车或篷车到 Yancey's Hole 草地上吃牛排烧烤，是园内少有的西部牛仔体验。": "Stables next to Roosevelt Lodge in the park's northeast corner run 1–2-hour trail rides in summer. The Old West Dinner Cookout takes you by horseback, stagecoach, or wagon to a meadow at Yancey's Hole for a steak cookout, one of the few Old West experiences in the park.",
  "2026 年骑马 6 月 6 日到 9 月 7 日（1 小时约 $100、2 小时约 $158），牛仔晚餐 6 月 6 日到 9 月 13 日（坐篷车约 $95、骑马约 $137）；骑马要满 8 岁、身高 48 英寸（约 122 厘米）以上、体重 240 磅（约 109 公斤）以下，在 Yellowstone National Park Lodges 提前预订，打雷时取消。": "In 2026, trail rides run June 6–September 7 (about $100 for 1 hour, $158 for 2 hours), and the cookout runs June 6–September 13 (about $95 by wagon, $137 on horseback). Riders must be at least 8 years old, at least 48 inches tall, and under 240 pounds. Book ahead with Yellowstone National Park Lodges; rides are canceled during thunderstorms.",
  "春秋无车骑行": "Spring & Fall Bicycling on Car-Free Roads",
  "每年春天铲完雪、道路对汽车开放前（通常 4 月上旬到 4 月第三个周五），西门到猛犸约 49 英里的公路只对自行车和行人开放，可以在没有车的路上骑过麦迪逊河谷和吉本瀑布；11 月初道路对汽车关闭后，麦迪逊到老忠实等几段也有一两周能骑。": "Each spring, after plowing and before the roads open to cars (usually early April through the third Friday in April), the roughly 49 miles from the West Entrance to Mammoth are open only to cyclists and pedestrians, so you can ride car-free through the Madison River valley and past Gibbon Falls. After the roads close to cars in early November, a few stretches, such as Madison to Old Faithful, are also open to bikes for a week or two.",
  "不用预约，只能白天骑；园内这时没有任何服务，要在 West Yellowstone 租车、自带补给，路上可能遇到铲雪车、野牛和熊，带防熊喷雾。": "No reservations; daytime riding only. There are no services in the park at this time, so rent a bike in West Yellowstone and bring your own supplies. You may meet plows, bison, and bears; carry bear spray.",
  "开放没有固定日期，看当年积雪和铲雪进度，以 NPS 自行车页面的开放状态为准。": "There are no fixed dates; openings depend on the year's snowpack and plowing progress. Check the NPS bicycling page for current status.",
  "蛇河漂流": "Snake River Scenic Floats & Whitewater Rafting",
  "园内的风景漂流从 Deadman's Bar 顺流而下约 16 公里到 Moose，水流平缓，一路看提顿群峰，常见秃鹰、河狸和驼鹿；想要刺激可以去 Jackson 以南的蛇河峡谷漂激流。": "The scenic float inside the park drifts about 10 miles from Deadman's Bar to Moose on gentle water, with the Teton Range in view the whole way and bald eagles, beavers, and moose often along the banks. For more excitement, raft the whitewater of the Snake River Canyon south of Jackson.",
  "都要跟持证的漂流公司去，建议提前在官网预订：园内风景漂流全程约 2.5–3 小时（船上 1–1.5 小时），成人约 $80 起；蛇河峡谷激流约 3–4 小时，每人约 $100–135。": "Both require a licensed outfitter; book ahead online. In-park scenic floats take about 2.5–3 hours total (1–1.5 hours on the water) and start at about $80 for adults. Snake River Canyon whitewater trips take about 3–4 hours and cost about $100–135 per person.",
  "杰克逊湖游船": "Jackson Lake Scenic & Meal Cruises",
  "从 Colter Bay 码头出发，在 Mount Moran 脚下的杰克逊湖上转一圈，讲解湖区的地质和历史；早餐、晚餐游船会登上湖中的 Elk Island 吃牛仔式烧烤。": "Cruises leave Colter Bay Marina and loop around Jackson Lake at the foot of Mount Moran, with commentary on the lake's geology and history. Breakfast and dinner cruises stop at Elk Island for a cowboy-style cookout.",
  "Grand Teton Lodge Company 经营，要预约，约 1.5–2.5 小时，$39–95。": "Run by Grand Teton Lodge Company; reservations required. About 1.5–2.5 hours, $39–95.",
  "2026 年干旱加上下游灌溉放水，湖水位太低，大船开不出码头，餐食游船 7 月 13 日、观光游船 7 月 16 日提前停航（往年开到 9 月上中旬）。": "In 2026, drought plus irrigation releases downstream left the lake too low for the large boats to leave the marina, so meal cruises ended early on July 13 and scenic cruises on July 16 (in a typical year they run into early or mid-September).",
  "骑马游": "Horseback Rides",
  "从 Jackson Lake Lodge、Colter Bay 和 Headwaters（Flagg Ranch）的马厩出发，跟向导骑马走 1–2 小时，穿过树林和草地，边走边看杰克逊湖和群峰。": "Guided 1–2-hour rides leave from the stables at Jackson Lake Lodge, Colter Bay, and Headwaters (Flagg Ranch), passing through forest and meadows with views of Jackson Lake and the peaks.",
  "Grand Teton Lodge Company 经营，要预约，$71–106；8 岁以上、身高 4 英尺（约 122 厘米）以上、体重不超过 225 磅（约 102 公斤），要能听懂英语指令。": "Run by Grand Teton Lodge Company; reservations required, $71–106. Riders must be 8 or older, at least 4 feet tall, no more than 225 pounds, and able to understand instructions in English.",
  "2026 年 Colter Bay 马厩 9 月 7 日结束，Jackson Lake Lodge 开到 10 月初，Headwaters 只在 6–8 月。": "In 2026, the Colter Bay stables closed September 7, the Jackson Lake Lodge stables run into early October, and Headwaters operates only June–August.",
  "看野生动物": "Wildlife Watching",
  "清晨和傍晚最容易碰到：牛轭湾和 Willow Flats 的柳丛里常有驼鹿，摩门街周围的 Antelope Flats 草原有野牛和叉角羚，蛇河沿岸有秃鹰和河狸，夏末 Moose-Wilson Road 常见黑熊；冬天马鹿集中在 Jackson 镇北的国家麋鹿保护区。": "Early morning and evening are best. Moose often browse the willows at Oxbow Bend and Willow Flats; bison and pronghorn graze the Antelope Flats grasslands around Mormon Row; bald eagles and beavers live along the Snake River; and black bears are common on Moose-Wilson Road in late summer. In winter, elk gather on the National Elk Refuge just north of the town of Jackson.",
  "自驾就能看，不用预约；Jackson 也有带单筒望远镜的付费观赏团。和熊、狼保持 100 码（约 91 米）以上，和其他动物至少 25 码（约 23 米）。": "Easy to do on your own by car, with no reservation needed; Jackson also has paid wildlife tours with spotting scopes. Stay at least 100 yards from bears and wolves and at least 25 yards from other animals.",
  "2026 年 9 月 8 日–11 月 15 日 Moose-Wilson Road 北段施工封闭。": "The north end of Moose-Wilson Road is closed for construction September 8–November 15, 2026.",
  "秋色与马鹿发情": "Fall Colors & Elk Rut",
  "9 月底到 10 月初山杨和三角杨变成金黄，牛轭湾、Moose-Wilson Road 和蛇河沿岸最漂亮；同一时期马鹿进入发情季，清晨和傍晚能听到公鹿高亢的求偶叫声，Taggart Lake 步道口一带和牛轭湾西边的 Cattleman's Bridge 是常去的地方。": "In late September and early October, aspens and cottonwoods turn gold, especially at Oxbow Bend, along Moose-Wilson Road, and along the Snake River. It's also the elk rut: in the early morning and evening you can hear the bulls' high-pitched bugling, often around the Taggart Lake Trailhead and Cattleman's Bridge west of Oxbow Bend.",
  "园内住宿和游客中心 9 月底到 10 月中旬陆续关门，10 月夜里常结冰甚至下雪；发情期的公鹿很凶，至少保持 25 码（约 23 米）。": "In-park lodging and visitor centers close in stages from late September to mid-October, and October nights often bring ice or even snow. Bulls in rut are aggressive; stay at least 25 yards away.",
  "国家麋鹿保护区马拉雪橇": "National Elk Refuge Sleigh Rides",
  "每年冬天几千头马鹿到 Jackson 镇北的国家麋鹿保护区过冬，坐马拉雪橇驶进鹿群，近距离看公鹿的大角。": "Each winter, thousands of elk spend the season on the National Elk Refuge just north of Jackson. A horse-drawn sleigh takes you right into the herd for a close look at the bulls' antlers.",
  "在 Jackson Hole & Greater Yellowstone 游客中心停车场的售票点买票，2025–26 季成人 $42、5–12 岁 $27，先到先得，也可以提前预约；从游客中心坐接驳车去上车点，全程约 1 小时。": "Buy tickets at the ticket office in the Jackson Hole & Greater Yellowstone Visitor Center parking lot. In the 2025–26 season, $42 for adults and $27 for ages 5–12, first come, first served, or reserve ahead. A shuttle takes you from the visitor center to the sleighs; the whole trip takes about 1 hour.",
  "2025–26 季 12 月 20 日–4 月 4 日，每天 10:00–16:00（圣诞节休息），每季日期略有不同。": "The 2025–26 season ran December 20–April 4, daily 10 a.m.–4 p.m. (closed Christmas Day). Dates vary slightly from season to season.",
  "冬季越野滑雪与雪鞋": "Cross-country Skiing & Snowshoeing",
  "冬天 Teton Park Road 从 Taggart Lake 步道口到 Signal Mountain Lodge 约 22 公里不通车，约 12 月中到 3 月中每周压雪三次，一条道给越野滑雪，一条道给步行、雪鞋和牵绳的狗；Moose-Wilson Road 封闭段和信号山山顶路也能滑。": "In winter, about 14 miles of Teton Park Road from the Taggart Lake Trailhead to Signal Mountain Lodge are closed to cars. From about mid-December to mid-March the road is groomed three times a week, with one lane for cross-country skiing and one for walking, snowshoeing, and leashed dogs. The closed section of Moose-Wilson Road and the Signal Mountain Summit Road are also open for skiing.",
  "自带或在 Jackson 租雪板、雪鞋；护林员带队的雪鞋徒步从 Taggart Lake 步道口出发，免费但要电话预约（307-739-3399）。": "Bring your own skis or snowshoes, or rent them in Jackson. Ranger-led snowshoe walks start at the Taggart Lake Trailhead; they're free, but reserve by phone (307-739-3399).",
  "死亡谷暗夜节": "Death Valley Dark Sky Festival",
  "死亡谷是国际暗夜协会最高等级（Gold Tier）的暗夜公园，每年 2–3 月挑一个新月前后的周末办暗夜节，有天文和行星科学讲座、望远镜观星、野外讲解和儿童活动，主会场在 Furnace Creek。": "Death Valley is a Gold Tier International Dark Sky Park, the highest rating from the International Dark-Sky Association. Each February or March, on a weekend near the new moon, the park holds a dark sky festival with astronomy and planetary science talks, telescope stargazing, field programs, and kids' activities, centered at Furnace Creek.",
  "活动免费（买了公园门票就能参加），这几天园内住宿紧张，要早订。": "Events are free with park admission. In-park lodging is tight that weekend, so book early.",
  "2026 年是 2 月 6–8 日，2027 年日期以 NPS 公告为准。": "In 2026 it was February 6–8; check NPS announcements for 2027 dates.",
  "春季沙漠野花": "Spring Wildflowers",
  "雨水多的年份，2 月下旬到 3 月低海拔的冲积扇和路边会开满黄色的沙漠金（desert gold）等野花，高海拔 4–6 月接着开；Badwater Road 两段和 190 号公路 Furnace Creek 到 Stovepipe Wells 之间最常见。": "In wet years, yellow desert gold and other wildflowers cover the low-elevation alluvial fans and roadsides from late February into March, followed by blooms at higher elevations in April–June. They're most common along two stretches of Badwater Road and on Highway 190 between Furnace Creek and Stovepipe Wells.",
  "花况完全看前一年秋冬的降雨，大多数年份只是零星开花；2026 年春是 2016 年以来最好的一次“超级花开”，3 月初最盛。出发前看 NPS 野花页面，禁止采摘。": "The bloom depends entirely on the previous fall and winter's rain, and most years bring only scattered flowers. Spring 2026 brought the best superbloom since 2016, peaking in early March. Check the NPS wildflower page before you go; picking flowers is prohibited.",
  "护林员讲解和夜空活动": "Ranger Programs",
  "每年 11 月中旬到次年 4 月中旬，护林员在恶水盆地、和谐硼砂厂、金色峡谷和梅斯基特沙丘带讲解和短途步行，晚上在 Furnace Creek 有室内讲座和观星讲解；夏季太热，不办户外活动。": "From mid-November to mid-April, rangers lead talks and short walks at Badwater Basin, Harmony Borax Works, Golden Canyon, and Mesquite Flat Sand Dunes, with indoor evening talks and stargazing programs at Furnace Creek. Summer is too hot for outdoor programs.",
  "免费、不用预约，时间表在游客中心和 NPS 网站公布；要在 Recreation.gov 提前两周预约的化石足迹徒步（1–3 月、每团 12 人、往返约 11 公里）2026 年停办，2027 年日期 12 月公布。": "Free, no reservation needed; schedules are posted at visitor centers and on the NPS website. The fossil footprint hike (January–March, 12 people per group, about 7 miles round trip), which requires a Recreation.gov reservation two weeks ahead, is suspended in 2026; 2027 dates will be announced in December.",
  "死亡谷 '49ers 年度聚会": "Death Valley '49ers Encampment",
  "纪念 1849 年淘金者穿越死亡谷的年度聚会，已经办了七十多年，有西部乡村音乐、历史和地质讲座、老兵致敬、摊位和观星，气氛像小镇集市。": "An annual gathering honoring the 1849 gold seekers who crossed Death Valley, held for more than 70 years. Expect Western and country music, history and geology talks, a tribute to veterans, vendor booths, and stargazing, with the feel of a small-town fair.",
  "大部分活动免费；2026 年 10 月 29 日到 11 月 1 日在 Stovepipe Wells 举办（同时庆祝 Stovepipe Wells 建成 100 周年），这几天园内住宿紧张，要早订。": "Most events are free. In 2026 it runs October 29–November 1 at Stovepipe Wells (also celebrating Stovepipe Wells' 100th anniversary). In-park lodging is tight those days, so book early.",
  "租吉普车或跟团走越野路": "Jeep Rentals & 4x4 Tours",
  "赛马场干湖这类长距离搓板砾石路，普通租车合同通常不允许开；Furnace Creek 可以按天租高底盘吉普车（带备胎、地图和卫星定位器），也可以跟向导的越野团去赛马场。": "Standard rental car contracts usually don't allow long washboard gravel roads like the one to the Racetrack. In Furnace Creek you can rent a high-clearance Jeep by the day (with a spare tire, maps, and a satellite messenger), or join a guided 4x4 tour to the Racetrack.",
  "Farabee's 在 The Oasis 旁营业，租车季约 9 月到次年 5 月，吉普车一天约 $325（超里程另计），赛马场越野团约 $280–385/人，旺季提前订。": "Farabee's operates next to The Oasis. The rental season runs about September to May; a Jeep is about $325 a day (extra mileage is charged separately), and Racetrack tours are about $280–385 per person. Book ahead in peak season.",
  "Titus Canyon Road 2026 年 10 月 1 日到 2027 年 9 月 30 日封闭维修；赛马场路段 2026 年 9 月没有封闭公告，出发前再查 NPS 路况。": "Titus Canyon Road is closed for repairs October 1, 2026–September 30, 2027. As of September 2026 there was no closure notice for the Racetrack road; check NPS road conditions again before you go.",
  "Furnace Creek 骑马": "Furnace Creek Stables Trail Rides",
  "The Ranch at Death Valley 旁的马厩在凉快的季节有 1–2 小时的沙漠骑马，还有日出、日落场，满月前后几晚有月光骑行。": "The stables next to The Ranch at Death Valley offer 1–2-hour desert rides in the cooler months, plus sunrise and sunset rides and moonlight rides on the nights around the full moon.",
  "约 10 月到次年 5 月中旬营业，在马厩或 The Oasis 官网预订，价格以官网为准。": "Open about October to mid-May. Book at the stables or on The Oasis website; check the website for prices.",
  "天使降临许可证抽签": "Angels Landing Permit Lottery",
  "天使降临最后一段铁链路要许可证，分季节抽签和前一天抽签两种；没抽中也可以走到 Scout Lookout，风景差不太多。": "The final chain section of Angels Landing requires a permit, issued through a seasonal lottery and a day-before lottery. If you don't win, you can still hike to Scout Lookout, where the views are nearly as good.",
  "都在 Recreation.gov 申请：季节抽签每季报名一次（2026–27 年 12–2 月的名额 2026 年 10 月 1–20 日报名、10 月 25 日出结果；3–5 月名额通常 2 月中旬报名），可以填 7 个志愿；前一天抽签每天 0:01–15:00（山地时间）报名、16:00 出结果。每份申请 $6（最多 6 人），抽中再付 $3/人。": "Apply for both on Recreation.gov. The seasonal lottery has one application window per season (for December–February 2026–27 permits, apply October 1–20, 2026, with results October 25; for March–May, applications usually open in mid-February), and you can list up to seven choices. The day-before lottery is open daily from 12:01 a.m. to 3 p.m. Mountain Time, with results at 4 p.m. Each application costs $6 (up to six people), and winners pay $3 per person.",
  "窄缝溯溪装备和全程穿越": "The Narrows: Gear Rental & Top-Down Permits",
  "从 Temple of Sinawava 往上游在维珍河里走不用许可证，但每年春季融雪（大约 3 月下旬到 5、6 月）流量超过 150 cfs 时关闭，发布山洪警告时也关闭；6–10 月水温最合适，7–9 月午后要防山洪。": "Wading up the Virgin River from the Temple of Sinawava doesn't require a permit, but the route closes when the flow tops 150 cfs during spring snowmelt (roughly late March into May or June) and whenever a flash flood warning is issued. June–October brings the most comfortable water temperatures; in July–September, watch for afternoon flash floods.",
  "Springdale 的户外店（如 Zion Outfitter）出租溯溪鞋、氯丁橡胶袜和登山杖，10 月到次年 5 月水冷要租干式背带裤或干式服；从上游 Chamberlain's Ranch 走 16 英里全程要野外许可证（在 Recreation.gov 或游客中心申请），还要自己安排接送。": "Outfitters in Springdale (such as Zion Outfitter) rent canyoneering shoes, neoprene socks, and hiking sticks. From October to May the water is cold, so rent dry bibs or a drysuit. Hiking the full 16 miles top-down from Chamberlain's Ranch requires a wilderness permit (apply on Recreation.gov or at a visitor center), and you'll need to arrange your own shuttle.",
  "园内溪水有有毒蓝藻警告：别把头埋进水里，别喝溪水。": "The park has issued toxic cyanobacteria warnings for its streams: don't submerge your head, and don't drink the water.",
  "左叉峡谷“地铁隧道”": "The Subway (Left Fork of North Creek)",
  "Kolob Terrace Road 旁的一条峡谷，走到里面有一段被水流掏成圆管状的岩壁，形似地铁隧道，底部是一串碧绿的水潭；从下游往返约 9 英里，要涉水、爬大石头，NPS 评为非常费力，从上游下来还要会绳降和游泳。": "A canyon off Kolob Terrace Road where the water has carved the rock into a round, tunnel-like tube, with a string of emerald pools along the floor. From the bottom, it's about 9 miles round trip with wading and boulder scrambling, rated very strenuous by NPS. Coming down from the top also requires rappelling and swimming.",
  "只能当天往返，要野外许可证：在 Recreation.gov 参加提前 2–4 个月的季节抽签（每月 27 日出结果）或出发前 2 天的每日抽签，申请费 $6、许可证 $10/人；冬季 Kolob Terrace Road 常因积雪封闭。": "Day trips only, with a wilderness permit: enter the seasonal lottery on Recreation.gov 2–4 months ahead (results on the 27th of each month) or the daily lottery 2 days before your trip. The application fee is $6, and the permit is $10 per person. Kolob Terrace Road often closes for snow in winter.",
  "锡安峡谷骑马": "Canyon Trail Rides (Zion Lodge)",
  "Zion Lodge 对面的马厩有 1 小时沿维珍河走到族长庭院附近的骑马，和 3 小时绕 Sand Bench 台地的路线，是峡谷里唯一的骑马活动。": "The stables across from Zion Lodge offer a 1-hour ride along the Virgin River to near the Court of the Patriarchs and a 3-hour ride around the Sand Bench. These are the only horseback rides in the canyon.",
  "3 月到 10 月营业，1 小时约 $60（7 岁以上）、3 小时约 $125（10 岁以上），体重 220 磅（约 100 公斤）以下；在 canyonrides.com 预订，提前 30 分钟到 Zion Lodge 对面的 Emerald Pools 步道口签到（班车季坐班车到 Zion Lodge 站）。": "Open March–October. About $60 for 1 hour (ages 7 and up) and $125 for 3 hours (ages 10 and up); riders must weigh under 220 pounds. Book at canyonrides.com and check in 30 minutes early at the Emerald Pools Trailhead across from Zion Lodge (during shuttle season, take the shuttle to the Zion Lodge stop).",
  "骑电动自行车游峡谷": "E-Biking Zion Canyon Scenic Drive",
  "班车季私家车不能开进锡安峡谷景观道，路上只有班车和自行车，骑电动自行车可以随时停下拍照，不用排队等班车；从游客中心沿帕鲁斯步道接景观道，骑到尽头 Temple of Sinawava 约 13 公里。": "During shuttle season, private cars aren't allowed on Zion Canyon Scenic Drive; only shuttles and bikes use the road. On an e-bike you can stop for photos whenever you like, with no shuttle lines. From the visitor center, take the Pa'rus Trail to the scenic drive; riding to the end at the Temple of Sinawava is about 8 miles.",
  "Springdale 有多家店出租电动自行车，全天约 $80–100；骑车遇到班车要靠边停下让行，自行车不能穿过 Zion–Mt. Carmel 隧道。": "Several shops in Springdale rent e-bikes, about $80–100 for a full day. When a shuttle comes along, pull over and stop to let it pass. Bikes aren't allowed through the Zion–Mt. Carmel Tunnel.",
  "秋季红叶": "Fall Colors",
  "海拔较高的科罗布峡谷和东侧台地 9 月底到 10 月中旬先变色，锡安峡谷里沿河的三角叶杨通常 10 月下旬到 11 月上旬最黄，衬着红色岩壁很好看，天气也凉快。": "The higher country in Kolob Canyons and on the east side mesas turns first, from late September to mid-October. In Zion Canyon, the cottonwoods along the river usually peak from late October to early November, bright yellow against the red cliffs, and the weather is cooler too.",
  "布莱斯天文节": "Bryce Canyon Astronomy Festival",
  "每年 6 月在新月前后办 3–4 天的天文节，有天文讲座、几十台望远镜的夜间观星、星座导览和儿童活动，是这个国际暗夜公园一年里最热闹的几晚。": "Each June, around the new moon, the park holds a 3–4-day astronomy festival with talks, night sky viewing through dozens of telescopes, constellation tours, and kids' activities. These are the busiest nights of the year at this International Dark Sky Park.",
  "免费（有公园门票即可）；晚间主讲座当天早上 8 点起在游客中心领票，天文摄影工作坊等要提前报名；这几天周边住宿紧张。": "Free with park admission. Tickets for the main evening talk are handed out at the visitor center starting at 8 a.m. that day; astrophotography workshops and some other events require advance registration. Nearby lodging is tight during the festival.",
  "2026 年是 6 月 11–13 日，2027 年日期以 NPS 公告为准；平时每年也有约 100 场护林员天文讲解，新月前后一周夜空最暗。": "In 2026 it was June 11–13; check NPS announcements for 2027 dates. The park also offers about 100 ranger astronomy programs a year, and the week around the new moon has the darkest skies.",
  "满月夜徒步": "Full Moon Hikes",
  "每月满月前后，护林员带队在月光下走 1–2 英里、约 2–3 小时，看月光里的石柱群；11 月到次年 3 月积雪超过 16 英寸（约 40 厘米）时改成雪鞋满月徒步。": "Each month around the full moon, rangers lead hikes of 1–2 miles (about 2–3 hours) by moonlight among the hoodoos. From November to March, when the snow is deeper than 16 inches, they become full moon snowshoe hikes.",
  "在 Recreation.gov 抢票：每次 14 天前放 15 张、5 天前再放 10 张（美东时间上午 10 点），每单最多 6 张，只收 $1 手续费；当天下午 3 点带鞋底有抓地纹路的登山鞋到游客中心签到，鞋不合格不能参加。": "Get tickets on Recreation.gov: 15 are released 14 days ahead and another 10 five days ahead (at 10 a.m. Eastern Time), up to six per order, with only a $1 fee. Check in at the visitor center at 3 p.m. that day wearing hiking boots with lugged soles; if your footwear doesn't pass, you can't go.",
  "冬季雪鞋徒步和冬季节": "Ranger Snowshoe Hikes & Winter Festival",
  "积雪够厚时，护林员带约 2 小时、1 英里左右的雪鞋徒步，免费提供雪鞋和手杖；每年 2 月总统日周末，门口的 Ruby's Inn 和公园合办冬季节，有越野滑雪、雪鞋团、摄影讲座和雪雕比赛。": "When the snow is deep enough, rangers lead snowshoe hikes of about 1 mile (about 2 hours), with snowshoes and poles provided free. Each February on Presidents' Day weekend, Ruby's Inn at the park entrance and the park hold a winter festival with cross-country skiing, snowshoe tours, photography talks, and a snow sculpture contest.",
  "雪鞋徒步不能提前预约，当天早上 8 点起在游客中心报名、满为止，8 岁以上；冬季节大多数活动免费，热门课程和团要提前在 Ruby's Inn 网站报名（2026 年是 2 月 14–16 日）。": "Snowshoe hikes can't be reserved: sign up at the visitor center starting at 8 a.m. the day of, until spots fill; ages 8 and up. Most winter festival events are free, but popular classes and tours require advance registration on the Ruby's Inn website (in 2026 the festival was February 14–16).",
  "骑马下到圆形剧场": "Canyon Trail Rides (Bryce)",
  "从 The Lodge at Bryce Canyon 旁的马厩出发，骑马沿 Queen's Garden 步道下到石柱林底部再回来（约 2 小时），或绕躲猫猫环线（约 3 小时，经过 Wall of Windows），比徒步省力、视角也不同。": "From the stables next to The Lodge at Bryce Canyon, ride down the Queen's Garden Trail to the floor of the amphitheater and back (about 2 hours), or take the Peekaboo Loop (about 3 hours, past the Wall of Windows). It's easier than hiking and gives you a different perspective.",
  "2 小时约 $85（4–10 月、7 岁以上），3 小时约 $125（5–10 月、10 岁以上、要体力好），体重 220 磅（约 100 公斤）以下；在 canyonrides.com 预订，提前 45 分钟到马厩签到。": "About $85 for 2 hours (April–October, ages 7 and up) and $125 for 3 hours (May–October, ages 10 and up, good fitness required); riders must weigh under 220 pounds. Book at canyonrides.com and check in at the stables 45 minutes early.",
  "布莱斯地质节": "Bryce Canyon Geology Festival",
  "每年 7 月办两天的地质节，游客中心前有周边几个州的地质、古生物和历史机构摆展位讲解，还有儿童化石挖掘区，晚上在 The Lodge 有主题讲座。": "A two-day geology festival held each July. Geology, paleontology, and history organizations from the surrounding states set up booths in front of the visitor center, there's a fossil dig for kids, and evening talks take place at The Lodge.",
  "免费（有公园门票即可），晚间讲座当天在游客中心领免费票；2026 年是 7 月 17–18 日。": "Free with park admission. Pick up free tickets for the evening talks at the visitor center that day. In 2026 it was July 17–18.",
  "骑骡子（南缘）": "Grand Canyon Mule Rides",
  "从南缘村出发的百年传统：Canyon Vistas 沿崖顶林间小路骑约 2 小时（全程约 3 小时）；Havasupai Gardens 一日骑行沿光明天使步道下到峡谷里的绿洲再上来，约 7 小时。": "A century-old tradition that starts in the South Rim village. The Canyon Vistas ride follows a wooded trail along the rim for about 2 hours (about 3 hours in all). The Havasupai Gardens day ride descends the Bright Angel Trail to the oasis inside the canyon and back, about 7 hours.",
  "Canyon Vistas 约 $193/人，Havasupai Gardens 约 $510/人（含午餐）；要 9 岁以上、身高 4 英尺 9 英寸（约 145 厘米）以上，体重分别不超过 225 磅和 200 磅，能听懂流利英语、不恐高；在 Grand Canyon National Park Lodges 电话或官网预订，热门日期要提前半年以上，最好前一天到 Bright Angel Lodge 交通柜台签到。": "Canyon Vistas is about $193 per person and Havasupai Gardens about $510 per person (lunch included). Riders must be at least 9 years old and at least 4 feet 9 inches tall, weigh no more than 225 pounds and 200 pounds respectively, understand fluent English, and not be afraid of heights. Book by phone or online with Grand Canyon National Park Lodges; popular dates need more than six months' notice. Ideally, check in the day before at the Bright Angel Lodge transportation desk.",
  "去谷底幻影牧场过夜的骡队因步道状况取消到 2027 年 2 月底；两种一日骑行 2026 年 9 月照常出发。": "Overnight mule trips to Phantom Ranch are canceled through the end of February 2027 because of trail conditions; both day rides were running as usual in September 2026.",
  "谷底幻影牧场过夜": "Phantom Ranch Lottery",
  "峡谷底部科罗拉多河边唯一的住处，只能徒步、骑骡或漂流到达，住一晚可以把南缘到谷底的往返分成两天，是很多人一生一次的行程。": "The only lodging at the bottom of the canyon, beside the Colorado River, reachable only on foot, by mule, or by raft. A night here splits the South Rim–to–river round trip into two days, and for many people it's a once-in-a-lifetime trip.",
  "每月 1 日在 Grand Canyon National Park Lodges 网站开放抽签，报名的是约 14 个月后那个月的住宿，抽中后付款；没抽中可以之后刷退订放出的名额。": "On the 1st of each month, a lottery opens on the Grand Canyon National Park Lodges website for stays in the month about 14 months out; you pay if you win. If you don't, you can keep checking later for cancellations.",
  "2026 年 8 月 29 日山洪冲毁 Bright Angel 峡谷一带的步道、桥和供水管线，幻影牧场、North Kaibab 步道和 South Kaibab 步道 Tip-Off 以下都关闭，住宿至少停到 10 月 31 日，11 月以后的预订暂时照常，以官网通知为准。": "A flash flood on August 29, 2026, destroyed trails, bridges, and the water pipeline around Bright Angel Canyon. Phantom Ranch, the North Kaibab Trail, and the South Kaibab Trail below the Tip-Off are closed, and lodging is suspended through at least October 31. Reservations from November on are being honored for now; check the official website for updates.",
  "科罗拉多河漂流": "Colorado River Rafting Trips",
  "跟持证漂流公司从 Lees Ferry 出发，在峡谷里的科罗拉多河上漂 3–18 天，过急流、在河滩露营、徒步进支流峡谷，是从谷底看大峡谷的方式。": "Join a licensed outfitter at Lees Ferry for 3–18 days on the Colorado River through the canyon: running rapids, camping on beaches, and hiking into side canyons. It's the way to see the Grand Canyon from the bottom.",
  "全程坐摩托艇至少 7 天、划桨船更久，每人通常要几千美元，热门日期常要提前一到两年订；只想体验一天，可以去 Page 附近 Glen Canyon 大坝下的平水漂流，或 Hualapai 部落从西段 Diamond Creek 出发的一日急流漂流。": "A full trip takes at least 7 days by motorized raft and longer by oar boat. Expect to pay several thousand dollars per person, and popular dates often book one to two years out. For a one-day taste, try the smooth-water float below Glen Canyon Dam near Page, or the Hualapai Tribe's one-day whitewater trip from Diamond Creek in the western canyon.",
  "2026 年 8 月底山洪后幻影牧场和两座吊桥关闭，在幻影牧场上下船的半程漂流可能受影响，以漂流公司通知为准。": "After the late-August 2026 flash flood, Phantom Ranch and the two suspension bridges closed, which may affect partial trips that start or end at Phantom Ranch; check with your outfitter.",
  "大峡谷观光火车": "Grand Canyon Railway",
  "从 66 号公路小镇 Williams 坐复古火车到南缘村，单程约 2 小时 15 分，车上有西部歌手表演，回程还有“劫车”小剧场，在南缘停留约 3.5 小时后原车返回，不用在园内找车位。": "Ride a vintage train from Williams, a Route 66 town, to the South Rim village, about 2 hours 15 minutes each way. Western musicians perform on board, and on the way back there's a staged train robbery. You get about 3.5 hours at the South Rim before the same train heads back, and no need to find parking in the park.",
  "每天上午 9:30 从 Williams 发车，经济座往返约 $90（2026 年有 66 号公路百年纪念 $66 优惠），公园门票另算；11 月到次年 1 月晚上有《极地特快》（The Polar Express）主题亲子车，要很早订。": "Trains leave Williams daily at 9:30 a.m. Coach-class round trip is about $90 (in 2026 there's a $66 Route 66 centennial deal); the park entrance fee is extra. From November through January, The Polar Express family trains run in the evening; book very early.",
  "直升机观光": "Helicopter Tours from Tusayan",
  "南门外 Tusayan 的大峡谷机场有几家直升机公司，沿规定航线飞过南缘森林、在峡谷上空飞到北缘再绕回来，能看到开车看不到的峡谷深处和北缘。": "Several helicopter companies fly from Grand Canyon Airport in Tusayan, outside the South Entrance, along set routes over the South Rim forest and across the canyon to the North Rim and back. You see deep parts of the canyon and the North Rim that you can't see by car.",
  "25–30 分钟约 $260–370/人，45–50 分钟约 $350–430/人，另收燃油附加费，前排座位要加钱；早上风小、光线好，大风天会停飞。": "25–30 minutes costs about $260–370 per person and 45–50 minutes about $350–430 per person, plus a fuel surcharge; front seats cost extra. Mornings have calmer winds and better light, and flights are grounded in high winds.",
  "大峡谷星空派对": "Grand Canyon Star Party",
  "每年 6 月在南缘游客中心后面办约一周的星空派对，天文爱好者摆出几十台望远镜让游客排队看，每晚 8 点有天文讲座和星座导览；北缘同期也有。": "Each June, a weeklong star party takes place behind the South Rim visitor center. Amateur astronomers set up dozens of telescopes for visitors to line up at, with an astronomy talk and constellation tour every night at 8 p.m. The North Rim holds one at the same time.",
  "免费（有公园门票即可），不用预约；2026 年是 6 月 6–13 日，2027 年日期以 NPS 公告为准。": "Free with park admission; no reservation needed. In 2026 it was June 6–13; check NPS announcements for 2027 dates.",
  "西峡玻璃桥（不在国家公园内）": "Grand Canyon West Skywalk (Hualapai)",
  "很多拉斯维加斯一日团去的“大峡谷西缘”其实是 Hualapai 印第安保留地经营的 Grand Canyon West，招牌是伸出崖边的 U 形玻璃桥；门票另算、不属于国家公园，离南缘开车约 4.5 小时，别和南缘排在同一天。": "The “Grand Canyon West Rim” that many Las Vegas day tours visit is actually Grand Canyon West, run by the Hualapai Tribe on its reservation. Its signature attraction is a U-shaped glass walkway that juts out past the cliff edge. Admission is separate, and it isn't part of the national park. It's about 4.5 hours' drive from the South Rim, so don't plan both on the same day.",
  "从拉斯维加斯开车约 2.5 小时；含玻璃桥的套票约 $70–115/人，停车后坐部落的接驳车去各观景点，玻璃桥上不能带手机和相机（有收费拍照）；不收国家公园门票，国家公园年卡不能用。": "About 2.5 hours' drive from Las Vegas. Packages that include the Skywalk run about $70–115 per person; after parking, tribal shuttles take you to the viewpoints. Phones and cameras aren't allowed on the Skywalk (paid photos are available). No national park entrance fee is charged, and America the Beautiful passes aren't accepted.",
  "夏季私家车只能开到 Mile 15，再往里要坐巴士：绿色的 Transit 巴士可以中途上下车，棕褐色的讲解团巴士（Tundra Wilderness Tour 等）有导游解说，一路找灰熊、驼鹿、驯鹿、大角羊和狼，看到动物会停车。": "In summer, private vehicles can drive only to Mile 15; beyond that, you take a bus. Green transit buses let you get on and off along the way, and tan narrated tour buses (such as the Tundra Wilderness Tour) have a guide. Everyone watches for grizzlies, moose, caribou, Dall sheep, and wolves, and the bus stops for wildlife.",
  "约 5 月 20 日到 9 月中旬运营，在 ReserveDenali.com 预订：2026 年到 East Fork（Mile 43）的 Transit 巴士成人约 $33.50（15 岁及以下免费），往返约 4.5 小时；Tundra Wilderness Tour 约 $145、Denali Natural History Tour 约 $117（都含门票），夏季热门时段会售罄。": "Buses run about May 20 to mid-September; book at ReserveDenali.com. In 2026, a transit bus to East Fork (Mile 43) costs about $33.50 for adults (free for ages 15 and under) and takes about 4.5 hours round trip. The Tundra Wilderness Tour is about $145 and the Denali Natural History Tour about $117 (both include the entrance fee). Popular summer times sell out.",
  "2021 年起 Pretty Rocks 滑坡让巴士只能开到 Mile 43；新桥 2026 年 9 月 2 日通车，本季只许步行和骑车通过，NPS 计划 2027 年恢复到 Eielson 游客中心、Wonder Lake 和 Kantishna 的全程巴士。": "Since 2021, the Pretty Rocks landslide has kept buses from going past Mile 43. A new bridge opened September 2, 2026, but only to walkers and cyclists this season; NPS plans to restore full bus service to Eielson Visitor Center, Wonder Lake, and Kantishna in 2027.",
  "雪橇犬演示": "Sled Dog Demonstrations",
  "国家公园唯一的工作雪橇犬队夏季在犬舍做 30 分钟演示：护林员讲冬季巡逻，雪橇犬拉车跑一圈，前后可以逛犬舍、看狗。": "The only working sled dog team in the national parks gives 30-minute demonstrations at the kennels in summer: a ranger talks about winter patrols, and the dogs pull a sled around a loop. Before or after, you can walk through the kennels and meet the dogs.",
  "免费、不用预约；6 月 1 日到 9 月上旬每天 10:00、14:00、16:00 三场（5 月中下旬和 9 月中旬每天一两场），犬舍没有停车位，演示前约 40 分钟从游客中心坐免费班车过去；冬季狗常出去巡逻，先到冬季游客中心问一下。": "Free, no reservation needed. From June 1 to early September there are three demonstrations daily, at 10 a.m., 2 p.m., and 4 p.m. (one or two a day in mid-to-late May and mid-September). The kennels have no parking; take the free shuttle from the visitor center about 40 minutes before the demonstration. In winter the dogs are often out on patrol, so ask at the winter visitor center first.",
  "德纳里观光飞行": "Denali Flightseeing",
  "从 Talkeetna 或公园入口附近坐小飞机绕北美最高峰飞行，可以加选降落在 Ruth 冰川上站 20–30 分钟；德纳里峰常被云遮住，从空中看到的机会比地面大得多。": "Fly around North America's highest peak in a small plane from Talkeetna or near the park entrance, with the option to land on Ruth Glacier for 20–30 minutes. Denali is often hidden in clouds, and your chances of seeing it from the air are much better than from the ground.",
  "Talkeetna 的 K2 Aviation、Talkeetna Air Taxi 等公司约 $285–615/人，含冰川降落一般 $475 以上；天气不好会改期或取消（降落不成会退冰川降落的差价），行程里留一两天机动。": "Talkeetna companies such as K2 Aviation and Talkeetna Air Taxi charge about $285–615 per person; flights with a glacier landing generally start above $475. Flights are rescheduled or canceled in bad weather (if the landing doesn't happen, you're refunded the difference), so leave a day or two of slack in your itinerary.",
  "公园入口外的尼纳纳河上有几家漂流公司，平缓的风景段适合带孩子，峡谷段有 III–IV 级急流；冰川融水很冷，公司会提供干式防水服。": "Several rafting companies run the Nenana River just outside the park entrance. The gentle scenic stretch is good with kids, and the canyon run has Class III–IV rapids. Glacial meltwater is very cold, so the companies provide dry suits.",
  "约 5 月中下旬到 9 月中旬营业，2–3 小时的行程成人约 $140–150、儿童约 $90–100，峡谷急流段一般要 12 岁以上、风景段 5 岁以上，旺季提前一两天订。": "Open about mid-to-late May to mid-September. A 2–3-hour trip costs about $140–150 for adults and $90–100 for kids. The canyon whitewater run generally requires ages 12 and up, the scenic float ages 5 and up. In peak season, book a day or two ahead.",
  "秋色和秋季自驾到 Teklanika": "Fall Colors & Fall Road Access",
  "8 月下旬到 9 月中旬，苔原上的矮桦、蓝莓丛变成红色和金色，是德纳里最短也最好看的季节；巴士季结束后，私家车可以开到 Mile 30 的 Teklanika 休息区。": "From late August to mid-September, dwarf birch and blueberry bushes on the tundra turn red and gold in Denali's shortest and most colorful season. After the bus season ends, private vehicles can drive to the Teklanika Rest Area at Mile 30.",
  "不用预约；2026 年秋季自驾期为 9 月 18 日到 10 月 15 日（看天气），路上可能有冰雪泥泞，Mile 13 到 Mile 30 之间能开多远随时变化，园内服务大多已关闭，自带吃喝。春季（约 4 月下旬到 5 月 19 日）也有同样的自驾窗口。": "No reservation needed. Fall road access in 2026 runs September 18–October 15 (weather permitting). Expect ice, snow, and mud, and how far you can drive between Mile 13 and Mile 30 can change at any time. Most park services are closed, so bring your own food and water. A similar driving window opens in spring (about late April to May 19).",
  "公园路自驾抽签": "Denali Road Lottery",
  "以前每年 9 月中旬有 4 天，抽中的人可以开自己的车沿公园路一直开进去（天气好能开到尽头的 Kantishna），是私家车深入公园的唯一机会。": "In past years, for four days in mid-September, lottery winners could drive their own cars out the park road (all the way to Kantishna at the end, weather permitting). It was the only chance to take a private vehicle deep into the park.",
  "以往在 Recreation.gov 于 5 月报名抽签，每天几百个名额，抽中后付许可证费。": "In past years, you entered the lottery on Recreation.gov in May. Several hundred permits were issued per day, and winners paid a permit fee.",
  "2021 年起因 Pretty Rocks 滑坡停办，2026 年也没有举办；新桥已经建成，2027 年是否恢复以 NPS 公告为准。": "Suspended since 2021 because of the Pretty Rocks landslide, and not held in 2026. The new bridge is finished; check NPS announcements for whether the lottery returns in 2027.",
  "极光和冬季活动": "Aurora & Winter in Denali",
  "8 月下旬到次年 4 月夜里够黑时能看到极光，9–3 月机会最多；冬季公园路只清到公园总部附近，可以在冬季游客中心（Murie Science and Learning Center）免费借雪鞋，2 月有 Denali Winterfest（2026 年是 2 月 21–22 日的免门票周末）。": "From late August to April, you can see the northern lights whenever nights are dark enough, with the best chances September–March. In winter the park road is plowed only to around park headquarters. Borrow snowshoes for free at the winter visitor center (Murie Science and Learning Center), and in February there's Denali Winterfest (in 2026, a fee-free weekend on February 21–22).",
  "入口区的酒店冬季基本都关门，冬季来要住 Healy；极光看太阳活动和云量，出发前查 NOAA 或阿拉斯加大学费尔班克斯分校的极光预报。": "Hotels in the entrance area are almost all closed in winter, so stay in Healy. Auroras depend on solar activity and cloud cover; check the NOAA or University of Alaska Fairbanks aurora forecast before you go.",
  "火焰炉护林员带队徒步": "Ranger-Guided Fiery Furnace Hike",
  "护林员带队钻进火焰炉的砂岩迷宫，约 2.5 小时、3 公里左右，一路讲岩鳍和拱门怎么形成、里面有哪些动植物；途中要侧身挤过窄缝、跨过岩缝、手脚并用爬岩，是第一次进火焰炉最稳妥的方式。": "A ranger leads you into the Fiery Furnace's sandstone maze, about 2.5 hours and roughly 2 miles, explaining how fins and arches form and what lives there. You'll squeeze sideways through narrow gaps, step across cracks, and scramble up rock with hands and feet. It's the safest way to see the Fiery Furnace the first time.",
  "只在 Recreation.gov 预订，每场提前 7 天早上 8 点（山地时间）放票，旺季很快抢光；$16/人，5 岁以下不能参加，12 岁以下要有成人陪同，要穿抓地好的鞋、每人带 1 升以上的水。票要在出发前一天或当天到游客中心按指定时间领取。": "Book only on Recreation.gov. Tickets for each tour are released 7 days ahead at 8 a.m. Mountain Time and go fast in peak season. $16 per person; no children under 5, and kids under 12 must be with an adult. Wear shoes with good grip and bring at least 1 quart of water per person. Pick up tickets at the visitor center at your assigned time the day before or the day of the tour.",
  "2026 年 4 月中旬开始、9 月结束，具体场次以 Recreation.gov 为准。": "In 2026, tours ran from mid-April through September; see Recreation.gov for specific times.",
  "火焰炉自助探索许可证": "Self-Guided Fiery Furnace Exploration Permit",
  "有经验的人可以不跟团、自己进火焰炉：里面没有正式步道，只有一条逆时针路线的小标记，岔路和死路很多、GPS 信号差，适合去过一次或很会找路的人。": "Experienced hikers can explore the Fiery Furnace on their own, without a ranger. There's no formal trail inside, only small markers for a counterclockwise route, with many side passages and dead ends and a poor GPS signal. Best if you've been in once before or are very good at route-finding.",
  "在 Recreation.gov 或电话 1-877-444-6777 预订，最早提前 7 天、最晚提前 2 天；$10/人，每组最多 6 人，5 岁以下不能进，不能带宠物。出发前一天或当天全员到游客中心看安全影片后领证（8:00–10:00、14:00–15:30 每半小时一场），只限当天日出到日落。": "Book on Recreation.gov or by phone at 1-877-444-6777, from 7 days to 2 days ahead. $10 per person, up to six per group; no children under 5 and no pets. The day before or the day of your visit, your whole group must watch a safety video at the visitor center to get the permit (every half hour 8–10 a.m. and 2–3:30 p.m.). Permits are good from sunrise to sunset on your day only.",
  "全年都能申请，旺季很快订满。": "You can apply year-round; permits book up fast in peak season.",
  "护林员星空讲解": "Ranger-Led Night Sky Programs",
  "拱门是国际暗夜公园。春秋季护林员不定期和峡谷地天空之岛、死马点州立公园轮流办星空讲解，讲完用望远镜看星星，在拱门一般从游客中心或全景点开始。": "Arches is an International Dark Sky Park. In spring and fall, rangers hold occasional night sky programs, rotating with Island in the Sky in Canyonlands and Dead Horse Point State Park; each talk is followed by stargazing through telescopes. At Arches, programs usually start at the visitor center or Panorama Point.",
  "免费（有公园门票即可），不用预约；日期多在新月前后，看游客中心公告或 NPS 活动日历。带椅子或垫子、保暖衣物和红光手电，下雨也照常举办。": "Free with park admission; no reservation needed. Programs are usually around the new moon; check visitor center notices or the NPS events calendar. Bring a chair or pad, warm layers, and a red flashlight. Programs go on even if it rains.",
  "科罗拉多河一日漂流（Moab）": "Colorado River Day Rafting near Moab",
  "Moab 东北 128 号公路旁的科罗拉多河段（Fisher Towers 一带）有半天到一天的橡皮艇漂流，以平水和小急流为主，两岸是红色峭壁，适合带孩子；这段河在公园外。": "The Colorado River along Highway 128 northeast of Moab (around Fisher Towers) has half-day to full-day raft trips, mostly flat water and small rapids between red cliffs. Good with kids. This stretch of river is outside the park.",
  "Moab 有多家持证漂流公司，有半天、一天和傍晚的班次，在各家官网或 Moab 游客中心预订，价格以官网为准。": "Moab has many licensed rafting companies offering half-day, full-day, and evening trips. Book on their websites or at the Moab visitor center; check the websites for prices.",
  "5–6 月融雪季水量大、浪也大，夏末水位低、漂得慢。": "During May–June snowmelt the water is high and the waves big; by late summer the river is low and slow.",
  "谢弗小径与白缘路四驱越野": "Shafer Trail & White Rim Road 4WD",
  "从天空之岛台地顺着谢弗小径的之字形土路下到白缘台阶，可以接 Potash 路回 Moab，或者开上约 160 公里长的白缘路（White Rim Road），一路贴着悬崖边俯瞰科罗拉多河和格林河。": "From the Island in the Sky mesa, follow the switchbacking dirt road of the Shafer Trail down to the White Rim bench. From there, take Potash Road back to Moab or head out on the roughly 100-mile White Rim Road, which runs along the cliff edge above the Colorado and Green rivers.",
  "要高底盘四驱车（带低速四驱），普通租车合同一般不允许开土路。只走谢弗小径不用许可证；当天往返白缘路要日间许可证：每天 50 张，一半在 Recreation.gov 前一天早上 8 点（山地时间）放出，另一半在天空之岛游客中心和 Moab 的公园背包客办公室当天领；在白缘路上过夜要提前订露营许可证。不想自己开可以报 Moab 的越野车团，价格以各家官网为准。": "You need a high-clearance four-wheel-drive vehicle (with low range); standard rental contracts generally don't allow dirt roads. Driving just the Shafer Trail needs no permit. A day trip on the White Rim Road needs a day-use permit: 50 are issued per day, half released on Recreation.gov at 8 a.m. Mountain Time the day before, and the other half available the same day at the Island in the Sky Visitor Center and the park's backcountry office in Moab. Camping on the White Rim requires an advance campsite permit. If you'd rather not drive, Moab outfitters run 4x4 tours; check their websites for prices.",
  "雨雪后路况变化很快，出发前查 NPS 路况；在荒野里抛锚的拖车费常超过 $2,000。": "Road conditions change fast after rain or snow; check NPS road conditions before you go. Towing from the backcountry often costs more than $2,000.",
  "科罗拉多河与格林河划船漂流": "River Trips on the Colorado & Green Rivers",
  "两条河在交汇点以上都是平缓的静水，适合划独木舟、皮划艇多日露营；交汇点以下是约 23 公里长的激流峡谷（Cataract Canyon），有三到五级急流，一般跟持证公司走 2–6 天。": "Above the confluence, both rivers are calm flat water, good for multiday canoe and kayak camping trips. Below the confluence is Cataract Canyon, about 14 miles of whitewater with Class III–V rapids, usually run with a licensed outfitter over 2–6 days.",
  "最省事是跟 Moab 的持证漂流公司，从半天到一周不等；自己划要在 Recreation.gov 申请河道许可证，过夜许可提前 4 个月开放（4 月 14 日–10 月 15 日的名额 12 月 14 日开放），当天往返的许可全年可申请；上下水点都在公园外，要安排接驳。": "The easiest option is a licensed Moab outfitter, with trips from half a day to a week. To paddle on your own, apply for a river permit on Recreation.gov: overnight permits open 4 months ahead (permits for April 14–October 15 open December 14), and day-use permits are available year-round. Put-ins and take-outs are outside the park, so arrange a shuttle.",
  "5–6 月融雪季水量最大，激流峡谷最危险；夏末水位低。": "May–June snowmelt brings the highest water, when Cataract Canyon is most dangerous; water is low by late summer.",
  "Moab 观光飞行": "Scenic Flights from Moab",
  "峡谷地大部分地方开车到不了，从 Moab 北边的峡谷地机场坐小飞机，能一次看到两河交汇点、迷宫区、隆起穹丘和针尖区的全貌。": "Most of Canyonlands can't be reached by car. A small plane from Canyonlands Field north of Moab shows you the confluence, the Maze, Upheaval Dome, and the Needles all at once.",
  "Redtail Air Adventures 等公司从峡谷地机场（CNY）起飞，航线从约 45 分钟到 2 小时不等，45 分钟的航线每人约 $300 多，以官网为准；早上气流稳、光线好。": "Redtail Air Adventures and other companies fly from Canyonlands Field (CNY), with routes from about 45 minutes to 2 hours. The 45-minute flight is a little over $300 per person; check the website. Mornings bring smoother air and better light.",
  "马蹄峡谷护林员带队徒步": "Ranger-Led Hikes in Horseshoe Canyon",
  "春秋季护林员带队走到大画廊，一路讲 Barrier Canyon 风格的岩画、古代狩猎采集者和峡谷里的植物，全程约 11 公里、4–6 小时。": "In spring and fall, rangers lead hikes to the Great Gallery, talking about the Barrier Canyon–style rock art, the ancient hunter-gatherers who made it, and the canyon's plants. About 7 miles round trip, 4–6 hours.",
  "免费、不用预约，集合时间和地点看 NPS 活动日历，或问 Hans Flat 护林站；每人带约 4 升水和午饭。": "Free, no reservation needed. Check the NPS events calendar for meeting times and places, or ask at the Hans Flat Ranger Station. Bring about a gallon of water per person, plus lunch.",
  "只在春秋季、有人手时举办。": "Offered only in spring and fall, when staffing allows.",
  "东南犹他天文节（AstroFest）": "Southeast Utah AstroFest",
  "每年 6 月连续几天，峡谷地、拱门、死马点州立公园和附近几处国家保护区轮流办白天和夜间的天文活动：讲座、望远镜观星、星座导览和亲子活动。平时春秋季天空之岛也有护林员星空讲解，从大观景点开始。": "For several days each June, Canyonlands, Arches, Dead Horse Point State Park, and several nearby national monuments take turns hosting daytime and nighttime astronomy events: talks, telescope stargazing, constellation tours, and family activities. In spring and fall, Island in the Sky also has ranger night sky programs starting from Grand View Point.",
  "免费（有公园门票即可），一般不用预约；各场的时间地点看 NPS 活动页。": "Free with park admission; usually no reservation needed. See the NPS events page for times and places.",
  "2026 年是 6 月 4–7 日（已结束），2027 年日期一般在冬末春初公布。": "In 2026 it was June 4–7 (now over); 2027 dates are usually announced in late winter or early spring.",
  "果园自摘水果": "U-Pick Fruit in the Fruita Orchards",
  "弗鲁塔约 1,900 棵历史果树的果子熟了就开放自摘：杏子约 6 月下旬到 7 月中旬，桃子约 7 月下旬到 9 月初，梨约 8 月上旬到 9 月初，苹果约 8 月中旬到 10 月中旬。": "When the fruit is ripe, the roughly 1,900 historic trees in the Fruita orchards open for U-pick: apricots from about late June to mid-July, peaches late July to early September, pears early August to early September, and apples mid-August to mid-October.",
  "不用预约，只能在挂着“U-Pick Fruit”牌子的果园里摘熟透、一碰就掉的果子；在园里现吃免费，带走的在果园入口的自助称重点按牌价付钱。带围栏的果园 9:00–17:00 开放；当天哪些果园开放可以问游客中心，或打 435-425-3791（按 1 再按 5）。": "No reservation needed. Pick only in orchards posted with a U-Pick Fruit sign, and only ripe fruit that comes off at a touch. Eating in the orchard is free; for fruit you take with you, weigh it and pay the posted price at the self-pay station at the orchard entrance. Fenced orchards are open 9 a.m.–5 p.m. Ask at the visitor center which orchards are open that day, or call 435-425-3791 (press 1, then 5).",
  "成熟时间每年随天气变化，春天的晚霜会让某些果子减产。": "Ripening times vary with the weather each year, and late spring frosts can cut some crops.",
  "吉福德之家水果派": "Gifford House Pies",
  "弗鲁塔村中心 1908 年建的吉福德农舍，现在是小博物馆和商店，卖现烤的水果派（苹果、桃子、樱桃、混合莓果等口味）、肉桂卷、冰淇淋和手工小物，买了可以坐在旁边果园的草地和野餐桌上吃。": "The 1908 Gifford farmhouse in the heart of Fruita is now a small museum and store. It sells fresh-baked fruit pies (apple, peach, cherry, mixed berry, and more), cinnamon rolls, ice cream, and handmade goods; eat them on the grass or at the picnic tables in the orchard next door.",
  "不用预约，早上 9 点开门；旺季派常在中午前后卖完，想吃早点去。": "No reservation needed; opens at 9 a.m. In peak season the pies often sell out around midday, so go early.",
  "每年 3 月 14 日（圆周率日）到感恩节后的周六营业，2026 年到 11 月 28 日；9 月下旬每天 9:00–16:30。": "Open each year from March 14 (Pi Day) to the Saturday after Thanksgiving; in 2026, through November 28. In late September, hours are 9 a.m.–4:30 p.m. daily.",
  "Heritage Starfest 星空节": "Heritage Starfest",
  "公园和 Torrey 的 Entrada Institute 每年 9 月合办的星空节，有天文讲座、白天用太阳望远镜看太阳、夜里用望远镜观星；圆顶礁 2015 年被评为国际暗夜公园。": "An annual September star festival run by the park and the Entrada Institute in Torrey, with astronomy talks, daytime solar telescope viewing, and nighttime stargazing. Capitol Reef was designated an International Dark Sky Park in 2015.",
  "活动免费、不用预约，时间地点看 NPS 活动页。": "Events are free, with no reservation needed; see the NPS events page for times and places.",
  "2026 年是 9 月 11–12 日（已结束），第一天在公园里、第二天在 Torrey 镇上；2027 年日期以 NPS 公告为准。": "In 2026 it was September 11–12 (now over): the first day in the park and the second in the town of Torrey. Check NPS announcements for 2027 dates.",
  "上羚羊峡谷光束": "Upper Antelope Canyon Light Beams",
  "约 3 月底到 10 月初的晴天，正午前后阳光从上羚羊峡谷头顶的窄缝直射到谷底，形成一道道光柱，导游常往光里撒一把细沙让光束更明显；6–7 月太阳最高，光束最多最亮。": "On clear days from about late March to early October, around midday, sunlight shoots through the narrow opening above Upper Antelope Canyon all the way to the floor, forming shafts of light. Guides often toss a handful of fine sand into the light to make the beams stand out. In June–July, with the sun highest, the beams are most frequent and brightest.",
  "订上羚羊约 10:30–13:30（亚利桑那时间）出发的场次，这几档最贵、最早售罄，旺季要提前一两个月在导览公司官网订；阴天、多云看不到光束，当天也不能因此取消。": "Book an Upper Antelope tour departing about 10:30 a.m.–1:30 p.m. (Arizona time). These slots cost the most and sell out first; in peak season, book a month or two ahead on the tour company's website. Overcast or cloudy skies mean no beams, and you can't cancel that day for that reason.",
  "2026 年纳瓦霍部落公园的门票涨到每人每个地点 $15（包含在团费里）；Antelope Canyon Navajo Tours 1 月 1 日起调价，普通场 $100、正午场 $120（含门票）。": "In 2026, the Navajo Tribal Park fee went up to $15 per person per site (included in tour prices). Antelope Canyon Navajo Tours raised its prices on January 1: $100 for regular tours and $120 for midday tours (fees included).",
  "羚羊峡谷 X 摄影团": "Antelope Canyon X Photography Tour",
  "下羚羊和上羚羊的普通团都不许用三脚架，想架三脚架慢慢拍，可以报 Taadidiin Tours 在羚羊峡谷 X 的 3 小时摄影团，人少、停留时间长；5 月到 8 月初中午前后也能看到光束。": "Regular tours of Lower and Upper Antelope don't allow tripods. To set up a tripod and take your time, book Taadidiin Tours' 3-hour photography tour at Antelope Canyon X, with smaller groups and longer stops. From May to early August you can also see light beams around midday.",
  "在 antelopecanyon-x.com 预订，价格以官网为准（2026 年普通徒步团成人 $62，含部落公园门票）；签到处在 98 号公路 308 英里标旁，提前 30 分钟到。": "Book at antelopecanyon-x.com; check the website for prices (in 2026, the regular walking tour is $62 for adults, including the tribal park fee). Check-in is by mile marker 308 on Highway 98; arrive 30 minutes early.",
  "格伦峡谷平水漂流": "Horseshoe Bend Rafting Trip (Glen Canyon Float)",
  "从佩吉坐车到 Lees Ferry，坐橡皮艇在马蹄湾下游的格伦峡谷河段里逆流开上去、再顺流漂回来，全程是平水、没有急流，从谷底仰望红色崖壁，中途上岸看岩画，4 岁以上都能参加。": "Ride a bus from Page to Lees Ferry, then take a raft upstream through the stretch of Glen Canyon below Horseshoe Bend and float back down. It's all smooth water with no rapids, with red cliffs rising overhead and a stop on shore to see petroglyphs. Ages 4 and up.",
  "在 lakepowell.com 预订（Wilderness River Adventures 经营），2026 年成人（16 岁以上）$129、4–15 岁 $113.82，另收 $15 公园门票；在佩吉 199 Kaibab Rd 的 River Headquarters 签到，半天行程约 10 英里。": "Book at lakepowell.com (run by Wilderness River Adventures). In 2026, $129 for adults (16 and older) and $113.82 for ages 4–15, plus a $15 park entrance fee. Check in at River Headquarters, 199 Kaibab Rd. in Page. The half-day trip covers about 10 miles.",
  "2026 年运营期 3 月 1 日–10 月 31 日；不满 8 位全价乘客时当班会取消。": "In 2026 the season runs March 1–October 31. A departure is canceled if fewer than eight full-fare passengers book.",
  "鲍威尔湖游船（Wahweap 码头）": "Lake Powell Boat Tours from Wahweap",
  "从 Lake Powell Resort 旁的 Wahweap 码头出发：90 分钟的大坝游船开到格伦峡谷大坝跟前，Navajo Canyon 游船开进一条红岩支流峡谷，傍晚还有 2 小时的 Canyon Princess 晚餐游船。": "Tours leave Wahweap Marina next to Lake Powell Resort. The 90-minute dam cruise goes right up to Glen Canyon Dam, the Navajo Canyon cruise heads into a red rock side canyon, and in the evening there's a 2-hour Canyon Princess dinner cruise.",
  "在 lakepowell.com 预订，价格以官网为准；码头在格伦峡谷国家休闲区收费区内，另付休闲区门票（每车 $30、7 天有效，国家公园年卡可用）。": "Book at lakepowell.com; check the website for prices. The marina is inside the fee area of Glen Canyon National Recreation Area, so you also pay the recreation area entrance fee ($30 per vehicle, good for 7 days; America the Beautiful passes accepted).",
  "2026 年因水位低，去彩虹桥（Rainbow Bridge）和羚羊峡谷水上段的游船官网写“暂不开放，另行通知”。": "Because of low water in 2026, the website lists cruises to Rainbow Bridge and the water section of Antelope Canyon as “suspended until further notice.”",
  "手套岩影子（Mitten Shadow）": "Mitten Shadow",
  "每年春分、秋分前后几天，日落前约 15–25 分钟，西手套岩的影子会慢慢爬上东手套岩，整个过程只有十几分钟；春季在 3 月底前后，秋季在 9 月中旬前后最明显。": "For a few days around the spring and fall equinoxes, about 15–25 minutes before sunset, the shadow of West Mitten slowly climbs onto East Mitten; the whole thing lasts only a little over 10 minutes. It's most distinct around late March in spring and around mid-September in fall.",
  "免费，在游客中心观景台或 The View 酒店看；这几天拍照的人很多，要提前占位置，Goulding's 也有专门去看影子的团。": "Free. Watch from the visitor center overlook or The View Hotel. Crowds of photographers turn out on these days, so claim a spot early. Goulding's also runs tours specifically to see the shadow.",
  "纳瓦霍向导吉普团和骑马": "Navajo-Guided Jeep & Horseback Tours",
  "环线以外的石拱、岩画和 Mystery Valley、Hunts Mesa 等地只能跟纳瓦霍向导去：有 1.5–3.5 小时的吉普团、日出日落团和骑马团，向导会讲纳瓦霍人的传统和这些孤峰的名字由来。": "Arches, rock art, and areas such as Mystery Valley and Hunts Mesa beyond the Valley Drive are open only with a Navajo guide. Options include 1.5–3.5-hour Jeep tours, sunrise and sunset tours, and horseback rides, and guides share Navajo traditions and the stories behind the buttes' names.",
  "可以在游客中心的售票亭现场报名（6:00–20:00），也可以提前在纳瓦霍部落公园官网列出的授权导览公司订；价格按时长和路线不同，以各家为准，进园门票一般另付。": "Sign up on the spot at the tour booths at the visitor center (6 a.m.–8 p.m.), or book ahead with the authorized tour companies listed on the Navajo Nation Parks & Recreation website. Prices vary by length and route; check with each company. The park entrance fee is usually extra.",
  "The Wave 提前 4 个月的网上抽签": "Coyote Buttes North Advanced Lottery",
  "每天 64 个名额里的 48 人（最多 12 组）走网上抽签，哪里都能报；中签率很低，很多人连抽好几年。": "Of the 64 daily permits, 48 (for up to 12 groups) go through an online lottery that you can enter from anywhere. The odds are very low, and many people try for years.",
  "在 Recreation.gov 的 Coyote Buttes North Advanced Lottery 申请：徒步月份前第 4 个月的整个月都能报（比如 2027 年 2 月的名额在 2026 年 10 月报，11 月 1 日上午 9 点山地时间开奖），每份申请可选 3 个日期、最多 6 人，每人每次只能报一份，申请费 $6 不退；中签后当月 15 日前登录确认并付每人 $7（狗也算），许可证 4–6 周后邮寄。": "Apply on Recreation.gov under the Coyote Buttes North Advanced Lottery. Applications are open for the entire month four months before your hike month (for example, February 2027 permits are applied for in October 2026, with results November 1 at 9 a.m. Mountain Time). Each application can list three dates and up to six people; each person may submit only one application per lottery, and the $6 application fee is nonrefundable. If you win, log in by the 15th of that month to confirm and pay $7 per person (dogs count too); permits are mailed 4–6 weeks later.",
  "许可证不能改期、不能转让，没有任何年卡或优惠；中签者可以请授权向导带路，向导不占名额。": "Permits can't be rescheduled or transferred, and no passes or discounts apply. Winners may hire an authorized guide, and the guide doesn't count against the permit limit.",
  "The Wave 两天前的手机现场抽签": "Coyote Buttes North Daily Lottery",
  "没中网上抽签的话，人到了 Kanab、佩吉一带还能每天用手机抽两天后的名额，每天再发 16 人（最多 4 组）。": "If you miss out in the online lottery, once you're in the Kanab–Page area you can enter a daily mobile lottery for permits two days out; another 16 people (up to four groups) are chosen each day.",
  "徒步日前两天的 6:00–18:00（犹他时间）用 Recreation.gov 手机 App 申请，人必须在 Kanab 到佩吉之间 89 号公路一带的地理围栏里，电脑申请无效；当晚 19:15 出结果，中签后第二天早上 8 点前付费，并在 8:30 到 Kanab 游客中心或佩吉的 Lake Powell Hub 参加现场安全说明，再隔一天才是徒步日。申请费 $6，中签每人 $7。": "Apply in the Recreation.gov mobile app between 6 a.m. and 6 p.m. (Utah time) two days before your hike. You must be inside the geofence along Highway 89 between Kanab and Page; applications from a computer don't count. Results come out at 7:15 p.m. that evening. If you win, pay by 8 a.m. the next morning and attend an in-person safety briefing at 8:30 a.m. at the Kanab Visitor Center or the Lake Powell Hub in Page; your hike is the following day. The application fee is $6, and winners pay $7 per person.",
  "抽签按犹他时间：2026 年 3 月 8 日到 10 月 31 日夏令时期间，犹他比亚利桑那快 1 小时；2026 年 11 月 26 日、12 月 25 日和 2027 年 1 月 1 日领证点关闭。": "The lottery runs on Utah time: during daylight saving time, March 8–October 31, 2026, Utah is 1 hour ahead of Arizona. Permit offices are closed November 26 and December 25, 2026, and January 1, 2027.",
  "White Pocket 四驱一日团": "White Pocket 4x4 Tours",
  "自己开不了深沙路的话，Kanab 和佩吉有几家持 BLM 许可的越野团去 White Pocket，常和 Buckskin Gulch、Wire Pass 或 Coyote Buttes South 组合成一天，全程约 7–8 小时。": "If you can't drive deep sand yourself, several BLM-permitted outfitters in Kanab and Page run tours to White Pocket, often combined with Buckskin Gulch, Wire Pass, or Coyote Buttes South into one day of about 7–8 hours.",
  "向 Kanab 或佩吉的持证导览公司预订，例如佩吉 Antelope Canyon Tours 的 Vermilion Adventures 约 $225.50 起（另加税费），含接送；行程、午餐和价格以各家官网为准，雨后深沙路况差时可能改线或取消。": "Book with a permitted tour company in Kanab or Page; for example, Vermilion Adventures by Antelope Canyon Tours in Page starts at about $225.50 (plus taxes and fees), with pickup included. Check each company's website for itineraries, lunch, and prices. Trips may be rerouted or canceled when the sand roads are bad after rain.",
  "露易丝湖 / 梦莲湖 Parks Canada 班车": "Parks Canada Shuttle to Lake Louise & Moraine Lake",
  "梦莲湖全年不让私家车进，旺季露易丝湖也很难停车。Parks Canada 的预约班车从露易丝湖滑雪场的 Park and Ride 出发，一张票当天可以去两个湖，两湖之间有接驳车（Lake Connector）。": "Moraine Lake is closed to private vehicles year-round, and in peak season parking at Lake Louise is very hard to get. Parks Canada's reservable shuttle leaves from the Park and Ride at the Lake Louise Ski Resort; one ticket covers both lakes that day, with the Lake Connector shuttle running between them.",
  "在 reservation.pc.gc.ca（选 Day Use）预约：2026 年 4 月 15 日早上 8 点（山地时间）放出全季 40% 的座位，其余 60% 在出发前两天早上 8 点放出。往返成人 C$12.75、65 岁以上 C$6、17 岁及以下 C$4，网上订另收 C$3.50；要在预约的 1 小时时段内到 Park and Ride 签到上车。": "Reserve at reservation.pc.gc.ca (choose Day Use). On April 15, 2026, at 8 a.m. Mountain Time, 40% of the season's seats were released; the remaining 60% are released at 8 a.m. two days before each departure. Round trip is C$12.75 for adults, C$6 for 65 and up, and C$4 for 17 and under, plus a C$3.50 online booking fee. Check in and board at the Park and Ride within your reserved 1-hour window.",
  "2026 年露易丝湖线 5 月 15 日到 10 月 12 日、梦莲湖线 6 月 1 日到 10 月 12 日运行，每 30 分钟一班，末班回程 19:30；另有 4:00、5:00 从露易丝湖湖边发车的 Alpine Start 日出早班车。2027 年的开订日期还没公布。": "In 2026, the Lake Louise route runs May 15–October 12 and the Moraine Lake route June 1–October 12, every 30 minutes, with the last return at 7:30 p.m. There are also Alpine Start sunrise shuttles leaving the Lake Louise lakeshore at 4 and 5 a.m. Booking dates for 2027 haven't been announced.",
  "落叶松金秋": "Golden Larch Season",
  "9 月中下旬，高山落叶松（alpine larch）的针叶变成金黄色，只维持两三周；梦莲湖上方的落叶松谷和哨兵山口最出名，是班夫一年里最热门的徒步时段。": "In mid-to-late September, alpine larch needles turn gold for just two or three weeks. Larch Valley and Sentinel Pass above Moraine Lake are the most famous spots, and this is Banff's busiest hiking window of the year.",
  "徒步不用预约，但要订梦莲湖班车去步道口，落叶松季的周末班车很快订满；灰熊活动频繁时强制 4 人以上紧密结伴同行。": "The hike needs no reservation, but you'll need a Moraine Lake shuttle ticket to reach the trailhead, and weekend shuttles in larch season book up fast. When grizzly activity is high, hikers must travel in tight groups of four or more.",
  "每年变色时间差一两周，通常 9 月中旬到 9 月底最盛；这时 Parks Canada 常发布结伴限制，出发前看公园公告。": "Timing varies by a week or two each year; color usually peaks from mid- to late September. Parks Canada often puts group-hiking restrictions in place at this time, so check park notices before you go.",
  "明尼万卡湖游船": "Lake Minnewanka Cruise",
  "从明尼万卡湖码头出发约 1 小时的游船，开进湖深处的魔鬼峡口（Devil's Gap），讲解湖区历史和被淹没的老村落，是不徒步也能深入湖区的办法。": "A roughly 1-hour cruise from the Lake Minnewanka dock deep into the lake to Devil's Gap, with commentary on the area's history and the old village now underwater. A way to get far out on the lake without hiking.",
  "Pursuit 经营，在 banffjaspercollection.com 网上买票，票价随日期浮动，5 岁以下免费；可以坐 Roam 6 路公交到码头。": "Run by Pursuit; buy tickets online at banffjaspercollection.com. Prices vary by date, and kids under 5 ride free. Roam Transit Route 6 goes to the dock.",
  "2026 年 5 月 8 日到 10 月 12 日运行（看天气）。": "Runs May 8–October 12, 2026 (weather permitting).",
  "冬季冰湖溜冰和滑雪": "Winter Skating & Skiing",
  "冬天露易丝湖、朱砂湖等湖面结冰后可以溜冰，露易丝湖城堡酒店前会清出冰场，背景就是冰封的维多利亚冰川；班夫附近还有 Lake Louise、Sunshine Village、Mt. Norquay 三个滑雪场。": "In winter, once Lake Louise, the Vermilion Lakes, and other lakes freeze, you can skate on them. A rink is cleared in front of the Fairmont Chateau Lake Louise, with the frozen Victoria Glacier behind it. Near Banff there are also three ski areas: Lake Louise, Sunshine Village, and Mt. Norquay.",
  "湖面溜冰免费，镇上和酒店可以租冰鞋；三个滑雪场可以分别买票，也有通用的 SkiBig3 联票。": "Skating on the lakes is free; rent skates in town or at the hotels. Buy lift tickets for each ski area separately, or get a SkiBig3 pass good at all three.",
  "冰况每年不同，只在清过雪、测过冰厚的区域溜冰；冬季冰原大道和部分山路常临时封闭。": "Ice conditions vary each year; skate only in areas that have been cleared and tested for thickness. In winter, the Icefields Parkway and some mountain roads often close temporarily.",
  "玛琳湖游船（精灵岛）": "Maligne Lake Cruise to Spirit Island",
  "想亲眼看精灵岛只能坐这趟船：从玛琳湖北头的码头出发，往返约 1.5 小时，中途在精灵岛观景点上岸停留一会儿。": "This boat is the only way to see Spirit Island in person. It leaves the dock at the north end of Maligne Lake for a round trip of about 1.5 hours, with a short stop on shore at the Spirit Island viewpoint.",
  "Pursuit 经营，在 banffjaspercollection.com 提前订座，票价随日期浮动；错过船次不退款，当天改期名额很少。": "Run by Pursuit; reserve ahead at banffjaspercollection.com. Prices vary by date. Missed departures aren't refunded, and same-day changes are rarely available.",
  "2026 年 5 月 27 日到 10 月 11 日运行（看天气）；2027 年季节还没公布。": "Runs May 27–October 11, 2026 (weather permitting); the 2027 season hasn't been announced.",
  "冰原冰川车 + 冰川天空步道": "Columbia Icefield Adventure",
  "从哥伦比亚冰原探索中心坐巨型冰川车开上阿萨巴斯卡冰川，在冰面上走一走，回程去悬在峡谷上方的玻璃地板观景台 Glacier Skywalk。": "From the Columbia Icefield Discovery Centre, ride a giant Ice Explorer onto the Athabasca Glacier and walk around on the ice, then stop on the way back at the Glacier Skywalk, a glass-floored platform suspended over a canyon.",
  "Pursuit 经营，在 banffjaspercollection.com 买票，票价随日期浮动，旺季提前订。": "Run by Pursuit; buy tickets at banffjaspercollection.com. Prices vary by date; book ahead in peak season.",
  "2026 年 5 月 1 日到 10 月 12 日运营；Ice Odyssey 小团 2026 年剩下的季节停开。": "Operates May 1–October 12, 2026. Small-group Ice Odyssey tours are suspended for the rest of the 2026 season.",
  "贾斯珀暗夜节": "Jasper Dark Sky Festival",
  "贾斯珀是世界上最大的暗夜保护区之一，每年 10 月办十天的暗夜节，有天文讲座、望远镜观星、音乐会和天文摄影活动，主会场在贾斯珀镇。": "Jasper is one of the largest dark sky preserves in the world. Each October it holds a 10-day dark sky festival with astronomy talks, telescope stargazing, concerts, and astrophotography events, centered in the town of Jasper.",
  "部分活动免费，大型讲座、音乐会要在 jasperdarksky.travel 买票；10 月夜里常在零度以下，带厚衣服。": "Some events are free; major talks and concerts require tickets from jasperdarksky.travel. October nights often drop below freezing, so bring warm clothes.",
  "2026 年是 10 月 16–25 日。": "In 2026 it runs October 16–25.",
  "9 月到 10 月上旬，公马鹿在贾斯珀镇周边的草地、河滩高声鸣叫、争夺母鹿，开车在镇边和 16 号公路沿线常能看到。": "From September to early October, bull elk bugle and compete for cows in the meadows and river flats around the town of Jasper. You can often see them from your car on the edge of town and along Highway 16.",
  "免费；公鹿这时很凶，至少保持 30 米，最好在车里看，别在路中间停车。": "Free. Bulls are aggressive now; stay at least 100 feet (30 m) away, ideally in your car, and don't stop in the middle of the road.",
  "欧哈拉湖一日游巴士抽签": "Lake O'Hara Day-use Bus Random Draw",
  "去欧哈拉湖的 11 公里碎石路不对私家车开放，Parks Canada 的一日游巴士是进湖区最省力的办法，座位靠每年春天的抽签分配。": "The 7-mile (11 km) gravel road to Lake O'Hara is closed to private vehicles, so Parks Canada's day-use bus is the easiest way in. Seats are allocated by a random draw each spring.",
  "在 reservation.pc.gc.ca 申请抽签：2026 年是 3 月 2 日早上 8 点到 23 日 23:59（山地时间），每份申请费 C$10；抽签结束后剩下或退订的座位随时可以订，最晚到出发前一天 15:30。车票往返每人 C$25.50。": "Apply for the random draw at reservation.pc.gc.ca: in 2026 it ran from 8 a.m. March 2 to 11:59 p.m. March 23 (Mountain Time), with a C$10 application fee. After the draw, leftover or canceled seats can be booked anytime up to 3:30 p.m. the day before. The bus costs C$25.50 per person round trip.",
  "2026 年巴士 6 月 19 日到 10 月 4 日运行，每天 8:30、10:30 两班上山；2027 年的抽签日期还没公布。": "In 2026 the bus ran June 19–October 4, with two trips up daily, at 8:30 and 10:30 a.m. Draw dates for 2027 haven't been announced.",
  "伯吉斯页岩化石导览": "Burgess Shale Fossil Hikes",
  "跟 Parks Canada 的讲解员爬到 5 亿多年前的寒武纪化石层，边走边看化石：Walcott 采石场往返约 24 公里、Mount Stephen 三叶虫化石床往返约 8 公里，都是很费力的全天徒步。": "Hike with a Parks Canada interpreter up to Cambrian fossil beds more than 500 million years old, looking at fossils along the way. The Walcott Quarry is about 15 miles (24 km) round trip and the Mount Stephen trilobite beds about 5 miles (8 km) round trip; both are strenuous all-day hikes.",
  "在 Parks Canada 预订系统（reservation.pc.gc.ca）订，2026 年 1 月 20 日早上 8 点（山地时间）开订，热门日期很快订满；成人价 Walcott 采石场 C$131、Mount Stephen C$101.75。": "Book through the Parks Canada reservation system (reservation.pc.gc.ca). Booking for 2026 opened at 8 a.m. Mountain Time on January 20, and popular dates fill fast. Adult prices: Walcott Quarry C$131, Mount Stephen C$101.75.",
  "开团日期以预订系统为准；2027 年开订日期还没公布。": "Check the reservation system for hike dates; the 2027 booking date hasn't been announced.",
  "翡翠湖划独木舟": "Emerald Lake Canoe Rentals",
  "在翡翠湖上划独木舟，湖水颜色比在岸上看更绿，早上风小、人少的时候最好。": "Paddle a canoe on Emerald Lake, where the water looks even greener than it does from shore. Mornings are best, with less wind and fewer people.",
  "湖边租船点先到先得、不能预约，按小时收费；2027 年 3 月 31 日前幽鹤的湖泊河流禁止自带船只和钓鱼，只有这里的租船可以下水。": "The lakeside rental is first come, first served with no reservations, charged by the hour. Until March 31, 2027, private watercraft and fishing are banned on Yoho's lakes and rivers, so these rentals are the only boats allowed on the water.",
  "通常 5 月中到 10 月上旬营业，看天气。": "Usually open mid-May to early October, weather permitting.",
  "凯斯牧场护林员导览": "Keys Ranch Guided Tour",
  "Bill 和 Frances Keys 一家在偏僻石谷里经营了约 60 年的沙漠牧场，只能跟护林员进去：约 90 分钟、步行约 0.8 公里，看木屋、学校、商店、修车铺和满院子的老汽车、采矿机器，听他们怎么在沙漠里找水、种菜、养活一家人。": "Bill and Frances Keys ran this desert ranch in a remote rocky canyon for about 60 years, and you can visit only with a ranger. The 90-minute tour covers about half a mile on foot, past the house, schoolhouse, store, workshop, and a yard full of old cars and mining machinery, with stories of how the family found water, grew food, and made a living in the desert.",
  "只在 Recreation.gov 售票（Joshua Tree National Park Tours and Programs 里的 Keys Ranch Tour），最早提前 60 天、前一天午夜截止，没有现场票；12 岁以上 $10，6–11 岁 $5，6 岁以下免费，年长者卡、残障卡持有人 $5；每单最多 10 人。在 Keys Ranch 上锁的大门集合，从 Barker Dam Road 岔进约 1.6 公里土路。": "Tickets are sold only on Recreation.gov (Keys Ranch Tour, under Joshua Tree National Park Tours and Programs), from 60 days ahead until midnight the day before, with no walk-up tickets. $10 for ages 12 and up, $5 for ages 6–11, free under 6, and $5 for Senior and Access pass holders; up to 10 people per order. Meet at the locked Keys Ranch gate, about 1 mile down a dirt road off Barker Dam Road.",
  "高温季（5–8 月）通常不开团；2026–27 年冬春的场次以 Recreation.gov 放出的为准。": "Tours usually aren't offered in the hot season (May–August); check Recreation.gov for winter and spring 2026–27 tour dates.",
  "春季野花与约书亚树开花": "Spring Wildflowers & Joshua Tree Blooms",
  "秋冬雨水多的年份，2 月下旬起南部低处的 Cottonwood、平托盆地一带先开出沙漠金盏花、马鞭草等野花，3–4 月往北、往高处开到约书亚树林；约书亚树本身也常在 2–4 月开出奶白色的花簇。": "In years with plenty of fall and winter rain, wildflowers such as desert marigold and sand verbena start blooming in late February at lower elevations in the south, around Cottonwood and the Pinto Basin, then spread north and upslope to the Joshua tree woodlands in March–April. Joshua trees themselves often bloom in creamy white clusters in February–April.",
  "不用预约；出发前在游客中心问当周哪里开得好，别踩进花丛、不要摘花。": "No reservation needed. Before you go, ask at a visitor center where the flowers are best that week. Stay out of the flower patches and don't pick anything.",
  "花期和花量完全看当年雨水，干旱年份几乎没有；约书亚树也不是每年都开花。": "Bloom timing and abundance depend entirely on the year's rainfall, and dry years bring almost nothing. Joshua trees don't bloom every year either.",
  "观星与暗夜星空节": "Stargazing & Night Sky Festival",
  "公园是国际暗夜公园，晴朗无月的夜里在 Quail Springs、Hidden Valley、Cap Rock、Ryan Mountain 几个指定观星停车场就能看到银河；公园每年还办暗夜星空节（Night Sky Festival），露营地剧场常有护林员夜间讲座。": "Joshua Tree is an International Dark Sky Park. On clear, moonless nights you can see the Milky Way from the designated stargazing parking areas at Quail Springs, Hidden Valley, Cap Rock, and Ryan Mountain. The park also holds an annual Night Sky Festival, and campground amphitheaters often host ranger evening programs.",
  "自己观星不用预约；露营地的晚间讲座免费，Twentynine Palms 镇上 Sky's the Limit 天文台的护林员夜间活动要在 Recreation.gov 预约（和凯斯牧场导览在同一个页面）。": "Stargazing on your own needs no reservation. Campground evening programs are free; ranger night programs at the Sky's the Limit Observatory in Twentynine Palms require a Recreation.gov reservation (on the same page as the Keys Ranch tour).",
  "星空节和夜间活动的日期每年公布，看公园官网的日历。": "Dates for the festival and night programs are announced each year; check the calendar on the park website.",
  "攀岩与抱石": "Rock Climbing & Bouldering",
  "约书亚树是世界知名的攀岩地，隐谷、Intersection Rock、Echo T 和巴克水坝一带有几千条线路和抱石点，粗糙的花岗岩摩擦力很好；没经验的可以报公园授权向导的入门课。": "Joshua Tree is a world-famous climbing area, with thousands of routes and boulder problems around Hidden Valley, Intersection Rock, Echo T, and Barker Dam, all on coarse, grippy granite. Beginners can take an intro class with an authorized guide.",
  "自带装备不用许可证；新手找公园官网列出的授权商业向导，价格和时间各家不同。": "With your own gear, no permit is needed. Beginners can choose from the authorized commercial guides listed on the park website; prices and schedules vary.",
  "夏天岩面太烫，攀岩季基本是 10 月到次年 4 月；部分岩壁会因猛禽筑巢等原因临时关闭，出发前看攀岩页面。": "The rock gets too hot in summer, so climbing season is basically October to April. Some cliffs close temporarily for nesting raptors and other reasons; check the climbing page before you go.",
  "秋季麋鹿发情期": "Elk Rut",
  "9–10 月麋鹿（elk）从高山下到 Moraine Park、Horseshoe Park、Upper Beaver Meadows 和西侧 Kawuneeche 河谷的草甸，公鹿在清晨和傍晚发出尖锐的“吼叫”（bugling）、争夺母鹿群，是落基山最热门的季节。": "In September–October, elk come down from the high country to the meadows of Moraine Park, Horseshoe Park, Upper Beaver Meadows, and the Kawuneeche Valley on the west side. Bulls bugle in the early morning and evening and compete for herds of cows. It's Rocky Mountain's most popular season.",
  "不用预约，在路边停车处看，和麋鹿保持至少 23 米（75 英尺）。傍晚 18 点后开车进 Bear Lake 路（Moraine Park）不需要时段预约；白天进园的时段预约见公园页。": "No reservation needed. Watch from roadside pullouts and stay at least 75 feet from the elk. Driving onto Bear Lake Road (Moraine Park) after 6 p.m. requires no timed-entry reservation; see the park page for daytime timed-entry requirements.",
  "9 月 1 日到 10 月 31 日，Horseshoe Park、Moraine Park、Upper Beaver Meadows、Harbison Meadow 和 Holzwarth 草甸每天 17 点到次日上午禁止步行进入，只能在道路和步道上看；周末傍晚路边停车处很早就满。": "From September 1 to October 31, Horseshoe Park, Moraine Park, Upper Beaver Meadows, Harbison Meadow, and Holzwarth meadows are closed to foot travel daily from 5 p.m. until the next morning; watch only from roads and trails. Roadside pullouts fill early on weekend evenings.",
  "秋季山杨变黄": "Fall Aspen Colors",
  "9 月中下旬到 10 月初，成片的山杨变成金黄色，Bear Lake 路沿线（Glacier Gorge、Bierstadt Lake 一带）和西侧 Kawuneeche 河谷最集中，和麋鹿发情期同一时间，周末非常拥挤。": "From mid-to-late September to early October, groves of aspen turn gold, most densely along Bear Lake Road (around Glacier Gorge and Bierstadt Lake) and in the Kawuneeche Valley on the west side. It coincides with the elk rut, and weekends are very crowded.",
  "不用预约；但 2026 年 10 月 18 日前 5:00–18:00 开车进 Bear Lake 路要预约含 Bear Lake 路的时段，停车场一早就满，可以停 Park & Ride 坐免费班车。": "No reservation needed to see the color, but until October 18, 2026, driving onto Bear Lake Road between 5 a.m. and 6 p.m. requires a timed-entry reservation that includes Bear Lake Road. Parking lots fill early; park at the Park & Ride and take the free shuttle.",
  "高处约 9 月中旬开始变色，低处晚一两周，每年随天气提前或推后。": "Higher elevations start turning around mid-September and lower ones a week or two later; timing shifts earlier or later each year with the weather.",
  "大角羊下山舔盐": "Bighorn Sheep at Sheep Lakes",
  "初夏大角羊成群从 Mummy Range 山上下到 Horseshoe Park 的 Sheep Lakes，舔食湖边泥土里的矿物盐，常要横穿 34 号公路，护林员和志愿者会临时拦车让它们过去。": "In early summer, bighorn sheep come down in groups from the Mummy Range to Sheep Lakes in Horseshoe Park to lick minerals from the mud around the lakes. They often cross Highway 34, and rangers and volunteers temporarily stop traffic to let them pass.",
  "不用预约；上午在 Sheep Lakes 停车场等，别靠近、别挡住羊群的路线。9:00–14:00 进园要时段预约（到 10 月 12 日）。": "No reservation needed. Wait in the Sheep Lakes parking area in the morning; don't approach the sheep or block their path. Entering the park 9 a.m.–2 p.m. requires a timed-entry reservation (through October 12).",
  "5 月到 8 月中旬最常见，每天来不来、几点来都不一定。": "Most often seen from May to mid-August, but whether and when they show up on a given day is unpredictable.",
  "高山苔原野花": "Alpine Tundra Wildflowers",
  "林线以上的苔原生长季只有 6–12 周，6 月下旬到 7 月，Trail Ridge Road 两边的苔原上开满贴地的高山勿忘我、高山金莲花和虎耳草，Rock Cut 的苔原步道和 Forest Canyon Overlook 旁最方便看。": "Above treeline, the tundra growing season lasts only 6–12 weeks. From late June through July, the tundra along Trail Ridge Road is covered with low-growing alpine forget-me-nots, globeflowers, and saxifrage. The Tundra Communities Trail at Rock Cut and the area around Forest Canyon Overlook are the easiest places to see them.",
  "不用预约；只走铺装步道，别踩进苔原、不要摘花。9:00–14:00 进园要时段预约。": "No reservation needed. Stay on paved trails, keep off the tundra, and don't pick flowers. Entering the park 9 a.m.–2 p.m. requires a timed-entry reservation.",
  "Trail Ridge Road 通车时间和花期都看当年积雪，雪大的年份花期推迟到 7 月中下旬。": "Trail Ridge Road's opening and the bloom both depend on the year's snowpack; in big snow years the bloom is pushed back to mid-to-late July.",
  "1930 年代的红色敞篷老巴士（Red Jammer）载着游客走向阳大道，司机兼导游一路讲解，车顶帆布卷起来能仰头看峭壁；不想自己开山路，或者车太长上不了向阳大道时最省心。": "Red 1930s open-top buses (the Red Jammers) carry visitors over Going-to-the-Sun Road while the driver-guide narrates, and with the canvas top rolled back you can look straight up at the cliffs. The easiest option if you'd rather not drive the mountain road or your vehicle is too long for Going-to-the-Sun Road.",
  "在 glaciernationalparklodges.com 预订，旺季常提前卖完。2026 年成人价：西侧 Lake McDonald Lodge 出发的 Western Alpine（3–4 小时）$80、全天的 Crown of the Continent（8–9.5 小时）$130；东侧 Rising Sun 出发的 Eastern Alpine（2.5–3.5 小时）$66 起，East Glacier 出发的 Big Sky Circle（8 小时）$136。": "Book at glaciernationalparklodges.com; tours often sell out in peak season. 2026 adult prices: from Lake McDonald Lodge on the west side, Western Alpine (3–4 hours) $80 and the full-day Crown of the Continent (8–9.5 hours) $130; on the east side, Eastern Alpine from Rising Sun (2.5–3.5 hours) from $66, and Big Sky Circle from East Glacier (8 hours) $136.",
  "2026 年 Western Alpine 6 月 20 日到 10 月 2 日（Lake McDonald Lodge 出发的班次到 9 月 27 日）、Crown of the Continent 6 月 21 日到 9 月 28 日，东侧各团 6 月上中旬到 9 月下旬；翻越洛根山口的线路要等向阳大道全线通车。": "In 2026, Western Alpine runs June 20–October 2 (departures from Lake McDonald Lodge through September 27) and Crown of the Continent June 21–September 28; east-side tours run from early or mid-June to late September. Routes over Logan Pass wait until Going-to-the-Sun Road is fully open.",
  "Many Glacier 游船": "Many Glacier Boat Tour",
  "坐两段历史木船横渡急流湖和约瑟芬湖，往返约 1.5 小时；可以在上游码头下船走到格林内尔湖，或者接格林内尔冰川步道，省掉一段平路。": "Two historic wooden boats carry you across Swiftcurrent Lake and Lake Josephine, about 1.5 hours round trip. You can get off at the upper dock and walk to Grinnell Lake, or connect to the Grinnell Glacier Trail and skip a flat stretch.",
  "在 glacierparkboats.com 预订，旺季提前几个月订满；2026 年成人 $41.70、4–12 岁 $20.85，每天 8:30–17:00 约 7 班；7 月 1 日起有给徒步的人只坐回程的单程票。": "Book at glacierparkboats.com; peak season fills months ahead. 2026 prices: $41.70 for adults and $20.85 for ages 4–12, with about seven departures daily, 8:30 a.m.–5 p.m. From July 1, hikers can buy one-way tickets for the return trip only.",
  "2026 年 6 月 10 日到 9 月 19 日运营（部分班次 7 月 1 日起），船公司不再带队徒步。": "Runs June 10–September 19, 2026 (some departures from July 1). The boat company no longer leads guided hikes.",
  "圣玛丽湖、麦克唐纳湖、双药湖游船": "St. Mary, Lake McDonald & Two Medicine Boat Tours",
  "同一家船公司在另外三个湖也开历史木船：圣玛丽湖从 Rising Sun 出发，停靠巴林瀑布，可以跟导游走到圣玛丽瀑布；麦克唐纳湖从 Lake McDonald Lodge 出发，1 小时，傍晚那班看日落；双药湖 45 分钟，到对岸走约 1.4 公里看 Twin Falls。": "The same company runs historic wooden boats on three other lakes. On St. Mary Lake, boats leave from Rising Sun and stop at Baring Falls, where you can walk with a guide to St. Mary Falls. On Lake McDonald, 1-hour cruises leave from Lake McDonald Lodge, with an evening sunset departure. On Two Medicine Lake, a 45-minute ride takes you to the far shore, where a walk of about 0.9 mile leads to Twin Falls.",
  "在 glacierparkboats.com 预订。2026 年成人价：圣玛丽湖 $41.70（游湖 1.5 小时，加徒步约 3.5 小时）、麦克唐纳湖 $27.80、双药湖 $20.85；双药湖只坐回程的单程票只在现场售票处卖。": "Book at glacierparkboats.com. 2026 adult prices: St. Mary Lake $41.70 (1.5 hours on the lake, about 3.5 hours with the hike), Lake McDonald $27.80, and Two Medicine $20.85. One-way return tickets on Two Medicine are sold only at the ticket office on site.",
  "2026 年圣玛丽湖 6 月 5 日到 9 月 12 日、麦克唐纳湖 5 月 20 日到 9 月 26 日、双药湖 6 月 1 日到 9 月 7 日；双药湖一带 9 月起因道路施工封闭。": "In 2026: St. Mary Lake June 5–September 12, Lake McDonald May 20–September 26, and Two Medicine June 1–September 7. The Two Medicine area has been closed since September for road construction.",
  "Granite Park / Sperry 高山木屋": "Granite Park & Sperry Chalets",
  "铁路公司在 1910 年代建的两座石头高山木屋，只能徒步上去：Granite Park 在高线步道上，Sperry 从 Lake McDonald Lodge 爬约 10 公里、爬升约 1,000 米。住一晚可以在山上看日落和日出，第二天再走下山。": "Two stone backcountry chalets built by the railroad in the 1910s, reachable only on foot. Granite Park sits along the Highline Trail; Sperry is about 6 miles from Lake McDonald Lodge, with about 3,300 feet of elevation gain. Stay a night to watch sunset and sunrise in the mountains, then hike down the next day.",
  "各自官网预订（graniteparkchalet.com、sperrychalet.com），名额很少、一放出就订满。": "Book on each chalet's website (graniteparkchalet.com, sperrychalet.com). Space is very limited and fills as soon as dates open.",
  "2026 年 Granite Park 6 月 29 日到 9 月 12 日、Sperry 7 月 10 日到 9 月 12 日营业；2027 年起改为试行抽签，细则和日期还没公布（2026 年 9 月 1 日公告）。": "In 2026, Granite Park was open June 29–September 12 and Sperry July 10–September 12. Starting in 2027, bookings move to a pilot lottery; details and dates haven't been released (announced September 1, 2026).",
  "春季骑车走向阳大道": "Going-to-the-Sun Road Spring Biking",
  "每年春天扫雪期间，向阳大道高处还没对汽车开放，可以骑车或步行进入封闭路段，在没有车的山路上看雪墙和瀑布，是当地人最喜欢的季节活动之一。": "Each spring while plows clear Going-to-the-Sun Road, the upper road is still closed to cars, but you can bike or walk into the closed section, past snow walls and waterfalls with no traffic. It's one of the locals' favorite seasonal outings.",
  "不用预约；从西侧的车辆关卡（Lake McDonald Lodge 或 Avalanche）往里骑，West Glacier、Apgar 一带能租自行车。扫雪作业区不能进，开放到哪里每天在 NPS 的路况页（Hiker/Biker Status）更新，午后山上有雪崩风险。": "No reservation needed. Ride in from the west-side vehicle closure (at Lake McDonald Lodge or Avalanche); you can rent bikes around West Glacier and Apgar. Active plowing zones are off-limits, and how far you can go is updated daily on the NPS road status page (Hiker/Biker Status). Avalanche risk rises on the upper road in the afternoon.",
  "2026 年 6 月 22 日全线通车后结束；通车后到劳动节，西侧 Apgar 到 Sprague Creek 一段 11:00–16:00 禁止自行车。": "Ended June 22, 2026, when the road fully opened. From full opening until Labor Day, bikes are prohibited 11 a.m.–4 p.m. on the west side between Apgar and Sprague Creek.",
  "峡湾游船季": "Kenai Fjords boat tour season",
  "峡湾和潮水冰川大多只能坐船看。夏季每天有好几家公司从 Seward 小船港开船：3–4 小时的短线在复活湾里看野生动物，6–7.5 小时的航线到 Aialik 或 Holgate 湾的潮水冰川，8.5–9 小时的全天航线开到西北峡湾。": "Most of the fjords and tidewater glaciers can be seen only by boat. In summer, several companies sail daily from the Seward small boat harbor: 3–4-hour trips look for wildlife in Resurrection Bay, 6–7.5-hour trips reach the tidewater glaciers of Aialik or Holgate Bay, and 8.5–9-hour full-day trips go out to Northwestern Fjord.",
  "在 Kenai Fjords Tours、Major Marine Tours 等公司官网预订，夏季提前订；公园本身不开船。": "Book on the websites of Kenai Fjords Tours, Major Marine Tours, and other companies; book ahead in summer. The park itself doesn't run boats.",
  "Kenai Fjords Tours 2026 年的航季是 3 月 12 日到 9 月 27 日（3–5 月只有复活湾里的短线）；2027 年的日期以各家公布为准。": "Kenai Fjords Tours' 2026 season runs March 12–September 27 (March–May, only short trips within Resurrection Bay). For 2027 dates, check with each company.",
  "春季灰鲸迁徙": "Spring gray whale migration",
  "每年春天灰鲸从墨西哥往北迁徙，经过复活湾口；这时各家公司开 3–4 小时的春季看鲸游船，船少人少。": "Each spring, gray whales migrating north from Mexico pass the mouth of Resurrection Bay. Companies run 3–4-hour spring whale-watching cruises then, with fewer boats and smaller crowds.",
  "向 Seward 的游船公司预订春季航次（Spring Wildlife Cruise）。": "Book a spring departure (Spring Wildlife Cruise) with a Seward tour boat company.",
  "Mount Marathon 登山赛": "Mount Marathon Race",
  "每年 7 月 4 日在 Seward 举行、始于 1915 年的登山赛：选手从镇上直冲到 Mount Marathon 约 920 米高的折返点再冲下来，下坡几乎是滑下来的，全镇都出来看。": "A mountain race held in Seward every July 4 since 1915. Runners charge from town straight up Mount Marathon to a turnaround at about 3,000 feet and race back down, half sliding on the descent, while the whole town turns out to watch.",
  "观赛免费，不用预约；当天 Seward 人非常多，住宿和停车都要很早安排。": "Watching is free, no reservation needed. Seward is packed that day, so arrange lodging and parking well in advance.",
  "Exit Glacier 护林员讲解": "Ranger programs at Exit Glacier",
  "夏季每天都有护林员在 Exit Glacier 带队讲解，讲冰川怎么退缩、植物怎么在冰川退出的地面上重新长出来。": "Every day in summer, rangers lead programs at Exit Glacier on how the glacier is retreating and how plants take hold again on the ground it leaves behind.",
  "不用预约，时间看自然中心的公告。": "No reservation needed; check the notices at the nature center for times.",
  "唯一能走进 14 层高的选矿厂的方式：跟向导沿楼梯和梯子一层层往下走，看当年碾碎、分选铜矿石的机器。": "The only way into the 14-story concentration mill: follow a guide down stairs and ladders floor by floor, past the machinery that once crushed and sorted copper ore.",
  "只由 St. Elias Alpine Guides（NPS 独家特许）经营，2 小时，成人 $36、12 岁以下 $18，在官网预订；下午 3:30 那场最常见，7 月 1 日到 8 月 15 日加开 11:30。": "Offered only by St. Elias Alpine Guides (the exclusive NPS concessioner): 2 hours, $36 for adults and $18 for kids under 12; book on its website. The 3:30 p.m. tour is the standard one, with an added 11:30 a.m. tour July 1–August 15.",
  "2027 年导览季是 5 月 28 日到 9 月 12 日，已经开订。": "The 2027 tour season runs May 28–September 12, and booking is already open.",
  "Root 冰川徒步和攀冰": "Root Glacier hikes and ice climbing",
  "Kennecott 的向导公司夏季每天带团上 Root 冰川：半日冰川徒步不需要经验，还有攀冰、冰洞探险和在冰川上露营的多日团。": "Kennecott guide companies take groups onto the Root Glacier every day in summer. Half-day glacier hikes need no experience, and there are also ice climbing, ice cave trips, and multiday glacier camping trips.",
  "向 St. Elias Alpine Guides、Kennicott Wilderness Guides 等公司预订，冰爪和装备由公司提供。": "Book with St. Elias Alpine Guides, Kennicott Wilderness Guides, or another company; crampons and other gear are provided.",
  "McCarthy 观光飞行": "Flightseeing from McCarthy",
  "从 McCarthy 的小机场起飞，飞过冰川、冰瀑和高山，是看清这座公园有多大的唯一办法。": "Take off from the small McCarthy airstrip and fly over glaciers, icefalls, and peaks. It's the only way to grasp how huge this park is.",
  "向 Wrangell Mountain Air 等航空公司预订，通常两人起飞；这家公司也有 McCarthy 和 Chitina 之间每天三班的定期航班。": "Book with Wrangell Mountain Air or another air service; flights usually need at least two passengers. Wrangell Mountain Air also runs three scheduled flights a day between McCarthy and Chitina.",
  "铜河鲑鱼洄游": "Copper River salmon run at Chitina",
  "夏季铜河的红鲑和帝王鲑逆流而上，Chitina 一带的河岸架满捕鱼水车，常看到有人站在急流边用长柄抄网捞鱼。": "In summer, sockeye and king salmon run up the Copper River. Around Chitina, fish wheels line the riverbanks, and you'll often see people standing at the edge of the rapids scooping fish with long-handled dip nets.",
  "看不用预约；Chitina 的抄网捕鱼是只限阿拉斯加居民的个人用渔业，游客不能参加。": "No reservation needed to watch. Chitina dip netting is a personal-use fishery for Alaska residents only; visitors can't take part.",
  "满月之夜": "Full Moon Night",
  "5–10 月每个满月的晚上，公园比平时晚关约 2 小时，可以在月光照亮的白沙里自己走走；有几个满月夜会在沙丘中心的露天剧场办音乐会或讲座。": "On each full moon night from May to October, the park stays open about 2 hours later than usual so you can wander the moonlit white sand on your own. On some full moon nights there are concerts or talks at the amphitheater in the heart of the dunes.",
  "不用买票也不用预约，交公园门票就行。露天剧场停车场在活动开始前 1.5 小时开放，停满就封，从收费站开过去要多留 30 分钟；剧场不提供座位，自带折叠椅或毯子。": "No tickets or reservations needed; just pay the park entrance fee. The amphitheater parking lot opens 1.5 hours before the event and closes when full; allow an extra 30 minutes to drive there from the fee booth. There's no seating, so bring a folding chair or blanket.",
  "2026 年的满月之夜是 5/1、5/31、6/29、7/29、8/27、9/26、10/25；最后一场 10 月 25 日有护林员 David Bustos 讲化石脚印（庆祝国家化石日），当天公园开到 20:00。2027 年的日期还没公布。": "Full Moon Nights in 2026: May 1, May 31, June 29, July 29, August 27, September 26, and October 25. On the last one, October 25, ranger David Bustos talks about fossil footprints (for National Fossil Day), and the park stays open until 8 p.m. 2027 dates haven't been announced.",
  "满月前后的晚上跟护林员走沙丘生命自然步道，全程不开手电，月光下的白沙亮得能看见自己的影子。": "On nights around the full moon, walk the Dune Life Nature Trail with a ranger, with no flashlights at all. Under the moon, the white sand is bright enough to see your own shadow.",
  "Recreation.gov 买票，16 岁以上 $8、15 岁以下 $4，另收公园门票；活动前一个月早上 8 点（山地时间）开售，每团 50 人，常几分钟卖完，每单最多 6 张。": "Buy tickets on Recreation.gov: $8 for ages 16 and up and $4 for 15 and under, plus the park entrance fee. Tickets go on sale one month ahead at 8 a.m. Mountain Time, 50 per hike, and often sell out in minutes; up to six per order.",
  "2026 年还剩 10 月 26 日 18:00、11 月 24 日 16:30 两场（7 月 30 日那场已取消）；2027 年的日期还没公布。": "Two hikes remain in 2026: October 26 at 6 p.m. and November 24 at 4:30 p.m. (the July 30 hike was canceled). 2027 dates haven't been announced.",
  "每月一次跟护林员车队开进导弹靶场，下到白沙的“源头”卢塞罗湖湖床，看露出地面的透石膏晶体，听白沙是怎么形成的。": "Once a month, join a ranger-led car caravan onto the missile range and down to the bed of Lake Lucero, the source of the white sand, to see selenite crystals at the surface and learn how the sand forms.",
  "Recreation.gov 买票，16 岁以上 $8、15 岁以下 $4，不另收公园门票；导览前一个月开售，每团 50 人，一张票只能开一辆车。": "Buy tickets on Recreation.gov: $8 for ages 16 and up and $4 for 15 and under; no park entrance fee. Tickets go on sale one month ahead, 50 per tour, and each ticket is good for one vehicle only.",
  "2026–27 年冬季：2026 年 11 月 21 日、12 月 19 日，2027 年 1 月 9 日、2 月 13 日、3 月 13 日，都是周六 10:00 出发。": "Winter 2026–27: November 21 and December 19, 2026, and January 9, February 13, and March 13, 2027, all Saturdays at 10 a.m.",
  "护林员日落漫步": "Sunset Stroll",
  "护林员带着在沙丘里慢慢走约 800 米，讲石膏沙和沙丘里的动植物，正好在日落时结束。": "A ranger leads a slow walk of about half a mile through the dunes, talking about the gypsum sand and the plants and animals that live there, timed to end at sunset.",
  "免费，不用也不能预约，交公园门票就行；在沙丘大道尽头的“Sunset Stroll Meets Here”牌子下集合。": "Free; no reservations needed or accepted, just the park entrance fee. Meet at the “Sunset Stroll Meets Here” sign at the end of Dunes Drive.",
  "2026 年只在周五、周六、周日举行，开始时间随日落从 16:00 到 19:00 不等，高温警报时取消。": "In 2026, held only on Fridays, Saturdays, and Sundays. Start times shift with sunset, from 4 p.m. to 7 p.m., and strolls are canceled during heat warnings.",
  "白沙热气球节": "White Sands Balloon Invitational",
  "每年 9 月的一个周末，成群的热气球一早在白色沙丘上空升起，是园里一年中最热闹的早晨。": "One weekend each September, fleets of hot air balloons rise over the white dunes at dawn. It's the liveliest morning of the year in the park.",
  "不用买票，交公园门票（每车 $25）就行；最好 5:30–6:30 到，7:00 飞行员简报，7:30–8:00 升空，天气不好会取消。": "No tickets needed; just pay the park entrance fee ($25 per vehicle). Arrive between 5:30 and 6:30 a.m.; the pilot briefing is at 7 a.m. and launch is 7:30–8 a.m. Canceled in bad weather.",
  "2026 年是第 34 届：9 月 19 日（周六）在公园里升空，9 月 20 日在 Alamogordo 的 Ed Brabson 热气球公园（免费）；今年没有夜间灯光秀和摊位。2027 年的日期还没公布。": "The 34th event was held in 2026: balloons launched in the park on Saturday, September 19, and at Ed Brabson Balloon Park in Alamogordo (free) on September 20. There was no evening balloon glow or vendors this year. 2027 dates haven't been announced.",
  "蝙蝠出洞讲解": "Bat Flight Program",
  "每天傍晚在天然入口的露天剧场听护林员讲蝙蝠，然后看几十万只巴西犬吻蝠盘旋着飞出洞口觅食；8–9 月小蝙蝠加入、北方的蝙蝠迁徙路过，数量最多。": "Every evening, listen to a ranger talk about bats at the Natural Entrance amphitheater, then watch hundreds of thousands of Brazilian free-tailed bats spiral out of the cave to feed. Numbers peak in August–September, when the young join the flights and bats migrating from the north pass through.",
  "免费，不用预约，也不需要洞穴门票，座位先到先得；为保护蝙蝠，剧场一带禁止一切电子设备（手机、相机都不行）。": "Free, with no reservation or cave ticket needed; seating is first come, first served. To protect the bats, all electronic devices (phones and cameras included) are banned in the amphitheater area.",
  "2026 年 4–10 月每晚举行，开始时间随日落变，当天在游客中心问；打雷闪电时取消。": "In 2026, held every night April–October. Start times change with sunset; ask at the visitor center that day. Canceled during thunder and lightning.",
  "护林员带着走进 Big Room 旁边装饰最密集的四个洞厅，下到游客能到的最深处，中途关灯体验洞里的漆黑。": "A ranger leads you through four of the most highly decorated chambers next to the Big Room, down to the deepest point open to visitors, and turns off the lights partway to show you total cave darkness.",
  "2026 年只在游客中心卖当天的现场票：成人 $10，儿童（6–15 岁）和老人卡、残障卡持有者 $5，另要分时段入场预约和洞穴门票；每团 12 人。": "In 2026, tickets are sold only same-day at the visitor center: $10 for adults and $5 for children (ages 6–15) and Senior and Access pass holders. You also need a timed-entry reservation and a cave entrance ticket. 12 people per tour.",
  "2026 年周四到周二 10:30、13:30 两场（周三不开），只在当天人手够时开。": "In 2026, two tours daily, Thursday through Tuesday, at 10:30 a.m. and 1:30 p.m. (none on Wednesdays), offered only when staffing allows that day.",
  "戴头盔头灯，下绳坡、爬梯子进入没有电灯和步道的下层洞穴，看洞穴珍珠和 1924 年探险队留下的痕迹。": "Wearing a helmet and headlamp, descend a rope-assisted slope and climb ladders into the lower cave, with no electric lights or paved trails, to see cave pearls and traces left by the 1924 expedition.",
  "Recreation.gov 提前 30 天放票，成人 $30，儿童和老人卡、残障卡持有者 $15，另要分时段入场预约和洞穴门票；12 岁以上，每团 12 人。": "Tickets are released on Recreation.gov 30 days ahead: $30 for adults and $15 for children and Senior and Access pass holders. You also need a timed-entry reservation and a cave entrance ticket. Ages 12 and up; 12 people per tour.",
  "2026 年每周三 9:30 一场，约 3 小时。": "In 2026, one tour every Wednesday at 9:30 a.m., about 3 hours.",
  "观星和夜间徒步": "Night Sky Programs",
  "公园远离城市灯光，夏秋的部分周末，蝙蝠讲解结束后有护林员带的观星（在游客中心东停车场用望远镜看）和夜间徒步。": "Far from city lights, the park offers ranger-led stargazing (with telescopes in the visitor center's east parking lot) and night hikes after the bat flight program on some summer and fall weekends.",
  "免费；夜间徒步每场最多 25 人，当天在游客中心服务台登记，观星不用登记。": "Free. Night hikes are limited to 25 people each; sign up at the visitor center information desk that day. No sign-up is needed for stargazing.",
  "NPS 的活动介绍页还写着暂停，但 2026 年的公园日历上有：9 月 11–13 日、10 月 9–11 日观星，9 月 25–27 日、10 月 23–25 日夜间徒步；以公园日历为准。": "The NPS program page still says these are suspended, but the 2026 park calendar lists stargazing on September 11–13 and October 9–11 and night hikes on September 25–27 and October 23–25; go by the park calendar.",
  "崖居护林员导览": "Ranger-Guided Cliff Dwelling Tours",
  "进悬崖宫殿、阳台屋、长屋这几处大崖居只能跟护林员导览：悬崖宫殿约 45 分钟、要爬 4 段梯子；阳台屋 1 小时，要爬 10 米木梯、钻岩缝隧道；长屋在 Wetherill Mesa，连走路约 2 小时。": "The large cliff dwellings of Cliff Palace, Balcony House, and Long House can be entered only on ranger-guided tours. Cliff Palace takes about 45 minutes and involves climbing four ladders; Balcony House takes 1 hour, with a 32-foot wooden ladder and a crawl through a rock tunnel; Long House, on Wetherill Mesa, takes about 2 hours including the walk.",
  "只在 Recreation.gov（或电话 1-877-444-6777）卖票，按滚动窗口提前 14 天、山地时间早上 8 点开放，每人 $8（3 岁以上）；旺季当天就会订满，有人退票会放回网上，开团前 2 小时都能捡漏。园内不卖票，也没有候补名单。": "Tickets are sold only on Recreation.gov (or by phone at 1-877-444-6777), on a rolling window 14 days ahead, opening at 8 a.m. Mountain Time; $8 per person (ages 3 and up). In peak season tours sell out the day they open. Canceled tickets go back online, so you can grab a spot up to 2 hours before a tour. No tickets are sold in the park, and there's no waitlist.",
  "2026 年导览季 5 月 4 日到 10 月 21 日，Wetherill Mesa 的长屋 5 月 22 日起；2027 年的日期还没公布。": "The 2026 tour season runs May 4–October 21, with Long House on Wetherill Mesa from May 22. 2027 dates haven't been announced.",
  "700 Years Tour 大巴导览团": "700 Years Tour",
  "特许经营商 Aramark 的半日大巴团，从 Far View Lodge 出发，导游沿途讲台地顶的半地穴屋和村落遗址，最后跟护林员下到悬崖宫殿，不用自己抢导览票、开山路。": "A half-day bus tour run by the concessioner Aramark, departing from Far View Lodge. The guide explains the pithouses and village sites on the mesa top along the way, and the tour ends with a ranger-led visit to Cliff Palace. No need to compete for tour tickets or drive the mountain roads yourself.",
  "在 visitmesaverde.com 网上订，或在 Far View Lodge、Far View Terrace、Morefield 营地现场订；8:00–12:00、13:00–17:00 两团，成人 $129、5–11 岁 $99、4 岁以下免费，订票时全额付款，出发 72 小时前取消才能全额退款。": "Book online at visitmesaverde.com or in person at Far View Lodge, Far View Terrace, or Morefield Campground. Two tours daily, 8 a.m.–noon and 1–5 p.m.: $129 for adults, $99 for ages 5–11, and free for 4 and under. Full payment is due at booking, and you get a full refund only if you cancel at least 72 hours ahead.",
  "2026 年 5 月 4 日到 10 月 18 日运营；Far View Lodge 离入口约 30 分钟车程，按时到。": "Runs May 4–October 18, 2026. Far View Lodge is about 30 minutes' drive from the entrance, so arrive on time.",
  "护林员荒野徒步团（方塔屋、马克杯屋）": "Backcountry Tours: Square Tower House & Mug House",
  "每天只有一团、限 10 人的小团，下到平时只能远看的崖居：方塔屋有全园最高的四层方塔和保存完整的地穴屋顶；马克杯屋在 Wetherill Mesa，沿途还有岩画和石峡谷风景。都要攀石、爬梯子、走崖边，适合体力好的人。": "Small tours, just one a day with 10 people each, go down to cliff dwellings you'd otherwise see only from a distance. Square Tower House has the tallest structure in the park, a four-story tower, and an intact original kiva roof. Mug House is on Wetherill Mesa, with rock art and canyon scenery along the way. Both involve scrambling over rocks, climbing ladders, and walking along cliff edges, so they suit fit hikers.",
  "Recreation.gov 提前 14 天、山地时间早上 8 点开票，每人 $25（3 岁以上）。方塔屋 8:30 在步道口集合、8:45 出发；马克杯屋 8:45 在 Wetherill Mesa 游客亭集合、9:00 出发，都是约 2 小时。": "Tickets open on Recreation.gov 14 days ahead at 8 a.m. Mountain Time, $25 per person (ages 3 and up). For Square Tower House, meet at the trailhead at 8:30 a.m. for an 8:45 a.m. start; for Mug House, meet at the Wetherill Mesa kiosk at 8:45 a.m. for a 9 a.m. start. Both take about 2 hours.",
  "2026 年方塔屋 5 月 4 日到 10 月 21 日、马克杯屋 5 月 22 日到 9 月 7 日每天一团。": "In 2026, one tour daily: Square Tower House May 4–October 21, Mug House May 22–September 7.",
  "周三星空讲解": "Wednesday Night Sky Programs",
  "梅萨维德是国际暗夜公园。每周三晚上护林员在 Morefield 营地露天剧场先讲 30 分钟，再用激光笔认星座、架望远镜看星星（天气好时）；阴天也照常讲。": "Mesa Verde is an International Dark Sky Park. Every Wednesday evening at the Morefield Campground amphitheater, a ranger gives a 30-minute talk, then points out constellations with a laser pointer and sets up telescopes (weather permitting). The talk goes on even when it's cloudy.",
  "免费、不用预约；带保暖衣服和手电（最好是红光）。": "Free, no reservation needed. Bring warm clothes and a flashlight (red light is best).",
  "2026 年 5 月 27 日–9 月 2 日 21:00、9 月 9–23 日 20:30、9 月 30 日–10 月 14 日 20:00 开始。": "2026 start times: 9 p.m. May 27–September 2, 8:30 p.m. September 9–23, and 8 p.m. September 30–October 14.",
  "冬季越野滑雪和雪鞋": "Cross-Country Skiing & Snowshoeing",
  "积雪够厚时，冬天封闭的 Cliff Palace Loop 和 Morefield 营地的环路会压出越野滑雪、雪鞋道，沿途能看到雪中的崖居，几乎遇不到别人。": "When the snow is deep enough, the Cliff Palace Loop, closed to cars in winter, and the Morefield Campground loops are groomed for cross-country skiing and snowshoeing. You'll see cliff dwellings in the snow and hardly anyone else.",
  "免费；游客与研究中心每天中午前免费借雪鞋（大人小孩尺码都有），15:30 前还回。": "Free. The Visitor and Research Center lends snowshoes for free (adult and kids' sizes) every day before noon; return them by 3:30 p.m.",
  "要看当年积雪，NPS 会在 Winter Activities 页面更新压雪情况。": "Depends on the year's snow; NPS posts grooming conditions on its Winter Activities page.",
  "彩绘沙漠旅馆的纳瓦霍手工艺展示": "Cultural Demonstrations at the Painted Desert Inn",
  "公园有 30 多个关系密切的部落。有些日子会有纳瓦霍等部落的艺人在彩绘沙漠旅馆现场做银饰、串珠、陶器、织毯或讲故事，可以边看边聊，有的作品当场出售。": "The park has close ties to more than 30 tribes. On some days, Navajo and other Native artists demonstrate silversmithing, beadwork, pottery, weaving, or storytelling at the Painted Desert Inn. You can watch and chat, and some work is for sale.",
  "免费、不用预约；在彩绘沙漠旅馆，通常 10:00–15:00。": "Free, no reservation needed. At the Painted Desert Inn, usually 10 a.m.–3 p.m.",
  "日程按月公布在官网（例如 2026 年 8 月几乎每天都有安排），随时可能调整，出发前看一眼。": "The schedule is posted monthly on the park website (in August 2026, for example, there were demonstrations almost every day) and can change at any time, so check before you go.",
  "石化林野外学院向导游": "Petrified Forest Field Institute Guided Trips",
  "公园官方合作的非营利博物馆协会开的小团，你开自己的车跟着向导走：3–4 小时的 Insider's Tour 把主要景点串起来；Ancient Wonders 从彩虹森林博物馆出发，去岩画峡谷（Petroglyph Canyon）和玛瑙屋；还有蓝台地、观鸟植物和要开四驱车去的冰淇淋岩（Ice Cream Rocks）。": "Small-group trips run by the nonprofit museum association that partners with the park; you drive your own car and follow the guide. The 3–4-hour Insider's Tour links the main sights, and Ancient Wonders starts at the Rainbow Forest Museum and visits Petroglyph Canyon and Agate House. Other trips cover Blue Mesa, birds and plants, and the Ice Cream Rocks, which require four-wheel drive.",
  "至少提前 7 天打电话（928-524-1286）或在官网留言约时间；每人 $69–$89，不含门票。": "Call at least 7 days ahead (928-524-1286) or leave a message on the website to schedule; $69–89 per person, entrance fee not included.",
  "按预约安排，没有固定班次。": "Scheduled by appointment; there are no regular departures.",
  "普埃科村落的夏至光斑": "Summer Solstice Solar Marker at Puerco Pueblo",
  "普埃科村落步道旁一块巨石上刻着一个小螺旋。夏至那几天的早上，一道光斑投到石面上，慢慢往下移，正好碰到螺旋的中心，是古普韦布洛人用来记录节令的“太阳历”。": "A small spiral is carved into a boulder beside the Puerco Pueblo trail. On mornings around the summer solstice, a spot of sunlight falls on the rock and slowly moves down until it touches the center of the spiral, a solar calendar the ancestral Puebloans used to mark the seasons.",
  "免费；6 月 21 日前后早上去普埃科村落。": "Free. Go to Puerco Pueblo in the morning around June 21.",
  "公园 8:00 才开门，有没有护林员带的观看活动、几点开始，以 NPS 活动日历为准。": "The park doesn't open until 8 a.m.; check the NPS events calendar to see whether rangers host a viewing and when it starts.",
  "季风雷雨季": "Monsoon Season",
  "亚利桑那的季风季从 6 月 15 日到 9 月 30 日，石化林通常 7 月初才下第一场雨，之后午后常常积起雷雨云。雨后的荒地和化石木颜色特别鲜艳，草原也会变绿。": "Arizona's monsoon season runs June 15–September 30. Petrified Forest usually gets its first rain in early July, and after that thunderheads often build in the afternoon. After rain, the badlands and petrified wood look especially vivid, and the grasslands turn green.",
  "不用预约。把户外活动排在上午，下午听到雷声就回车里（遮阳棚是金属顶，不安全）；不要穿越有水的冲沟和路面。": "No reservation needed. Plan outdoor time for the morning, and when you hear thunder in the afternoon, get back in your car (the shade shelters have metal roofs and aren't safe). Don't cross washes or roads with water flowing over them.",
  "暴雨可能让步道、支路临时关闭，看公园 Alerts。": "Heavy storms can temporarily close trails and side roads; check the park alerts.",
  "魔鬼游乐场许可证徒步": "Devil's Playground Permit Hike",
  "北区荒野里一片偏远的荒地，被侵蚀成各种奇形怪状的石柱，带着灰、紫、蓝色条纹；没有步道，要走一段土路再自己找路。": "A remote stretch of badlands in the north wilderness, eroded into strange pinnacles striped gray, purple, and blue. There's no trail: you drive a dirt road, then find your own way.",
  "每周只有 3 张免费许可证，从周三开始在游客中心先到先得，必须在徒步当天中午前领到，不能电话预留（可以先打 928-524-6228 分机 236 问还剩几张）。": "Only three free permits are issued per week, first come, first served at the visitor center starting Wednesday. You must pick yours up by noon on the day of your hike, and you can't hold one by phone (call 928-524-6228, ext. 236, to ask how many are left).",
  "官网写的是只在彩绘沙漠游客中心发放，2026 年那里施工关闭，北区的咨询暂时在彩绘沙漠旅馆，去之前打电话确认在哪领。进去的土路风险自负，雨后不要开。": "The website says permits are issued only at the Painted Desert Visitor Center, which is closed for construction in 2026; north-end visitor information is temporarily at the Painted Desert Inn. Call ahead to confirm where to pick up your permit. The dirt access road is driven at your own risk; stay off it after rain.",
  "梅达诺溪春季涌浪": "Medano Creek Surge Flow",
  "雪大的年份，5 月下旬到 6 月初融水最多，沙丘脚下的梅达诺溪漫开成一片宽浅的“沙滩”：水流把河床的沙堆成一道道小沙坝，冲垮时就涌下一波浪，大约 20 秒一波，水大时浪高 30 厘米以上。": "In big snow years, snowmelt peaks from late May to early June, and Medano Creek spreads into a wide, shallow beach at the foot of the dunes. The current piles sand on the creekbed into small dams, and each time one breaks, a wave surges down, about every 20 seconds, over a foot high when the water is high.",
  "不用预约，交公园门票就行；周末入口排长队、停车场爆满，尽量工作日去。可以给小孩带个扁平的充气垫，水大时能顺浪漂一小段。": "No reservation needed, just the park entrance fee. On weekends there's a long line at the entrance and the parking lot overflows, so go on a weekday if you can. Bring a flat inflatable pad for the kids; when the water is high they can ride a wave a short way.",
  "2026 年积雪接近历史最低，溪水整个春天都没流到主停车场，只在东边的 Sand Pit、城堡溪一带有细流；2027 年的流量预测 NPS 一般在 4 月发布。": "Snowpack in 2026 was near a record low, and the creek never reached the main parking area all spring, with only a trickle to the east around the Sand Pit and Castle Creek. NPS usually releases its flow forecast for 2027 in April.",
  "护林员晚间讲座和看星星": "Ranger Evening Programs & Night Sky",
  "夏秋的部分晚上，护林员在 Piñon Flats 营地下方的露天剧场讲公园里的动物、地质和夜空；散场后正好去沙丘上看星星，7 月下旬到 9 月银河入夜后就高挂天上。": "On some summer and fall evenings, rangers give talks on the park's wildlife, geology, and night sky at the amphitheater below Piñon Flats Campground. Afterward, head out onto the dunes to stargaze; from late July to September, the Milky Way is high overhead after dark.",
  "免费、不用预约，交公园门票就行；开车停露天剧场（Amphitheater）停车场。": "Free, no reservation needed, just the park entrance fee. Park in the Amphitheater parking lot.",
  "2026 年只在 7 月下旬到 10 月初的部分周六举行（7 月底周五也有），开始时间随日落从 21:00 提前到 19:30；2027 年的安排以公园日历为准。": "In 2026, held only on some Saturdays from late July to early October (plus Fridays in late July), with start times moving earlier with sunset, from 9 p.m. to 7:30 p.m. Check the park calendar for 2027.",
  "秋季山杨和棉白杨变黄": "Fall Aspen & Cottonwood Colors",
  "9 月下旬到 10 月初，沙丘上方山坡的山杨林变成金黄色，莫斯卡山口步道和梅达诺山口四驱路一路都是；10 月中旬轮到沙丘脚下沿溪的棉白杨，黄叶衬着沙丘和刚落雪的山顶。": "From late September to early October, aspen groves on the slopes above the dunes turn gold all along the Mosca Pass Trail and Medano Pass Primitive Road. In mid-October it's the turn of the cottonwoods along the creek at the foot of the dunes, yellow leaves against the sand and freshly snowcapped peaks.",
  "不用预约；9 月是全年天气最好的时候，下午沙丘也不太烫，周末人比 5–6 月少。": "No reservation needed. September has the best weather of the year, the dunes aren't too hot in the afternoon, and weekends are less crowded than in May–June.",
  "高处先变色、低处晚一两周，每年随天气提前或推后；秋天上面的国家保护区是打猎区，进山穿颜色鲜艳的衣服。": "Higher elevations change first and lower ones a week or two later, earlier or later each year with the weather. In fall, the national preserve upslope is open to hunting, so wear bright colors in the mountains.",
  "沙丘边的草原向日葵": "Prairie Sunflower Bloom",
  "夏天雨水多的年份，8 月下半月沙丘边缘和草原上会开出成片的草原向日葵，黄花一直铺到沙丘脚下，背后是雪山。": "In summers with plenty of rain, prairie sunflowers bloom in sheets along the edges of the dunes and across the grasslands in the second half of August, yellow flowers right up to the foot of the dunes with snowy peaks behind.",
  "不用预约；进园公路两边和沙丘停车场附近就能看到，清早或傍晚光线最好，也避开午后雷暴。": "No reservation needed. You can see them along the park entrance road and near the dunes parking lot. Early morning and evening have the best light and avoid afternoon thunderstorms.",
  "要看 7–8 月的季风雨，干旱的年份几乎不开，花期每年可能前后差一两周。": "Depends on the July–August monsoon rains; in dry years there's almost no bloom, and timing can shift by a week or two.",
  "圣路易斯谷沙丘鹤迁徙": "Sandhill Crane Migration (San Luis Valley)",
  "每年春秋两季，两万多只大沙丘鹤在圣路易斯谷的农田和湿地停留几个星期补充体力，早晚成群起落、跳求偶舞，3 月上旬数量最多。看鹤最集中的是公园西南约 1 小时 15 分车程的 Monte Vista 国家野生动物保护区。": "Each spring and fall, more than 20,000 greater sandhill cranes stop for a few weeks in the farm fields and wetlands of the San Luis Valley to refuel, rising and landing in flocks and dancing in the morning and evening. Numbers peak in early March. The biggest concentration is at Monte Vista National Wildlife Refuge, about 1 hour 15 minutes' drive southwest of the park.",
  "看鹤不用预约，在 Monte Vista 保护区周边的公路旁停车看，别进私人农田；每年 3 月上旬 Monte Vista 镇有沙丘鹤节（2026 年是 3 月 6–8 日），部分观鹤巴士团和讲座要在鹤节官网提前报名。": "No reservation needed to watch. Park along the roads around the Monte Vista refuge, and stay out of private fields. Each year in early March, the town of Monte Vista holds a crane festival (March 6–8 in 2026); some crane-viewing bus tours and talks require advance registration on the festival website.",
  "春季约 2 月初到 3 月底，秋季约 9 月下旬到 11 月中下旬（秋天比较分散）；2027 年鹤节的日期还没公布。": "Spring: about early February to late March; fall: about late September to mid-to-late November (more spread out). 2027 festival dates haven't been announced.",
  "梅达诺山口四驱路吉普团": "Medano Pass 4WD Tours",
  "没有四驱车也能走梅达诺山口四驱路：本地向导开吉普带你穿过深沙、在峡谷里涉水过溪，一路讲沙丘东侧的地质和动物，秋天山杨变黄时最受欢迎。": "No four-wheel-drive vehicle? A local guide can drive you over Medano Pass Primitive Road in a Jeep, through deep sand and across the creek in the canyon, explaining the geology and wildlife on the east side of the dunes. Most popular in fall, when the aspens turn.",
  "NPS 列出的几家（Dunes 4x4、Mountain Master Off-Road Tours、Pathfinders 4x4）都要提前打电话或网上订；Mountain Master 的团约 3.5 小时、从游客中心出发，2026 年 1–2 人一车 $410，3–4 人另加价。": "The outfitters NPS lists (Dunes 4x4, Mountain Master Off-Road Tours, and Pathfinders 4x4) all require booking ahead by phone or online. Mountain Master's tour runs about 3.5 hours from the visitor center; in 2026, $410 per vehicle for one or two people, with an extra charge for three or four.",
  "四驱路全线通常 5 月中下旬到 11 月底开放，冬天只能开到城堡溪野餐区；暴雨后溪水上涨可能临时封路。": "The full road is usually open from mid-to-late May to late November; in winter you can drive only to the Castle Creek Picnic Area. The road may close temporarily when the creek rises after storms.",
  "护林员观景台讲解": "Ranger Talks at Pulpit Rock",
  "夏天每天上午 10 点在讲坛岩观景台有 20–30 分钟的地质讲解（峡谷为什么这么深、这么陡、岩石有多老），下午 2 点是护林员选题讲解（历史、植物或动物），站在崖边听，适合第一次来的人。": "Every summer morning at 10 a.m., there's a 20–30-minute geology talk at the Pulpit Rock Overlook (why the canyon is so deep and steep, and how old the rock is), and at 2 p.m. a ranger's-choice talk (history, plants, or animals). You stand at the rim and listen; a good introduction on a first visit.",
  "免费、不用预约，交了公园门票就能参加；准时到讲坛岩观景台集合。": "Free, no reservation needed with park admission. Be at the Pulpit Rock Overlook on time.",
  "2026 年两场讲解每天都有，日历排到 10 月 14 日；黄昏讲座和营地晚间节目 2026 年不办，人手不够或天气不好时会取消。": "In 2026, both talks are given daily, with the calendar running through October 14. Twilight talks and campground evening programs aren't offered in 2026, and talks are canceled when staffing is short or the weather is bad.",
  "天文观星活动与 AstroFest 天文节": "Astronomy Programs & Black Canyon Curecanti AstroFest",
  "公园是国际暗夜公园，夏天护林员、志愿者和当地的黑峡谷天文学会常架望远镜带大家看星星、认星座，白天也有太阳望远镜观测；每年 9 月还有两天的 AstroFest 天文节。": "The park is an International Dark Sky Park. In summer, rangers, volunteers, and the local Black Canyon Astronomical Society often set up telescopes to show you stars and constellations, plus solar telescopes by day. Each September there's also a two-day AstroFest.",
  "免费、不用预约，交公园门票即可；日期和地点不固定，看公园日历或到南缘游客中心问。带保暖衣服和红光手电。": "Free, no reservation needed with park admission. Dates and places vary; check the park calendar or ask at the South Rim Visitor Center. Bring warm clothes and a red flashlight.",
  "2026 年的 AstroFest 已在 9 月 11–12 日办完（11 日晚上在南缘游客中心，12 日在 Curecanti 的 Elk Creek 露天剧场），2027 年的日期还没公布。": "The 2026 AstroFest took place September 11–12 (the evening of the 11th at the South Rim Visitor Center, the 12th at the Elk Creek amphitheater in Curecanti). 2027 dates haven't been announced.",
  "冬天游客中心以西的南缘公路不通车，积雪够时公园把路面压成越野滑雪（传统式和自由式）和雪鞋道，到高点单程约 9.7 公里，能到平时开车去的观景台；1 月到 3 月上旬积雪好时，周末还有护林员带队的雪鞋徒步。": "In winter, South Rim Road west of the visitor center is closed to cars. When there's enough snow, the park grooms it for cross-country skiing (classic and skate) and snowshoeing, about 6 miles one way to High Point, reaching overlooks you'd normally drive to. When the snow is good from January to early March, rangers also lead snowshoe walks on weekends.",
  "自己滑、自己走都免费（交公园门票），园内不租装备，在 Montrose 等镇上租；护林员雪鞋徒步周六、日 11:00 出发，约 90 分钟、1.6 公里左右，免费借雪鞋，名额有限，活动前一周开始发邮件到 BLCA_info@nps.gov 预约，提前 15 分钟到游客中心旁的滑雪道起点集合。": "Skiing and snowshoeing on your own are free (with park admission). There are no rentals in the park; rent gear in Montrose or other nearby towns. Ranger snowshoe walks start at 11 a.m. on Saturdays and Sundays and last about 90 minutes over roughly 1 mile, with free snowshoes. Space is limited: starting a week before, email BLCA_info@nps.gov to reserve, and meet 15 minutes early at the start of the ski trail next to the visitor center.",
  "要看当年积雪，压道情况在公园 Current Conditions 页面更新；2026/27 季的雪鞋徒步日期还没公布。": "Depends on the year's snow; grooming conditions are posted on the park's Current Conditions page. Snowshoe walk dates for 2026–27 haven't been announced.",
  "Kīlauea 山顶间歇喷发": "Kīlauea summit eruption (episodic lava fountaining)",
  "2024 年 12 月 23 日起，Halemaʻumaʻu 火山口里的喷口时喷时停：每次熔岩喷泉持续几个小时到十来个小时，最高时几百米高，两次之间停几天到几周。喷发全在公园的封闭区里，在火山口边的观景台就能看，天黑后最壮观；停的时候夜里也常能看到喷口的红光。": "Since December 23, 2024, vents inside Halemaʻumaʻu crater have erupted on and off. Each episode of lava fountaining lasts from a few hours to more than 10, with fountains at times more than 1,000 feet high, and pauses between episodes last days to weeks. The eruption is entirely within a closed area of the park, but you can watch from overlooks on the crater rim; it's most dramatic after dark. Between episodes, the vents often glow red at night.",
  "不用预约，付公园门票就行；出发前看 USGS 夏威夷火山观测站的每日公告和直播摄像头，喷发开始后 NPS 会在官网公布观景点和停车建议。": "No reservation needed, just the park entrance fee. Before you go, check the USGS Hawaiian Volcano Observatory's daily updates and live webcams; once an episode starts, NPS posts viewing areas and parking advice on its website.",
  "到 2026 年 8 月 25 日已喷发 54 次；9 月 7 日起第 55 次的前兆活动（喷口溢流、新喷口）断断续续，10 月 3 日 USGS 说还没开始喷泉、预测不了时间，警戒级别 WATCH / ORANGE。10 月 1 日起 Keanakākoʻi 一侧因地震增多临时关闭。": "As of August 25, 2026, there had been 54 episodes. Precursor activity for episode 55 (vent overflows and new vents) has come and gone since September 7. On October 3, USGS said fountaining had not begun and its timing couldn't be forecast; the alert level is WATCH/ORANGE. Since October 1, the Keanakākoʻi area has been temporarily closed because of increased earthquakes.",
  "山顶护林员讲解": "Ranger-guided programs at Kīlauea summit",
  "公园几乎每天都有免费的护林员活动，比如在 Uēkahuna 讲火山和夏威夷文化的“Life on the Edge”、带着走山顶的“Explore the Summit”，喷发期间护林员也常在观景台回答问题。": "The park has free ranger programs almost every day, such as “Life on the Edge” at Uēkahuna, on volcanoes and Hawaiian culture, and “Explore the Summit,” a walk around the summit. During eruptions, rangers are often at the overlooks to answer questions.",
  "免费、不用预约（门票另付）；时间看公园日历，或到欢迎中心门口的公告板查。": "Free, no reservation needed (entrance fee applies). Check the park calendar or the bulletin board outside the visitor center for times.",
  "Kahuku 周六导览和讲座": "Kahuku guided hikes and Coffee Talks",
  "Kahuku 园区周四到周日开放，周六上午常有护林员带队的轻松徒步（比如看古代夏威夷人田地遗迹的“Farming the Rock”、认识 ʻōhiʻa 树的“ʻŌhiʻa Lehua Hike”），每月还有一次“Coffee Talk”讲座，讲当地的鸟、牧场史和手工艺。": "The Kahuku Unit is open Thursday through Sunday. Saturday mornings often bring easy ranger-led hikes (such as “Farming the Rock,” to the remains of ancient Hawaiian fields, and the “ʻŌhiʻa Lehua Hike,” about the ʻōhiʻa tree), and once a month there's a “Coffee Talk” on local birds, ranching history, or crafts.",
  "免费、不用预约，在 Kahuku 游客接待站集合（11 号公路 70.5 英里路标附近）；具体日期看公园每月的活动公告。": "Free, no reservation needed. Meet at the Kahuku visitor contact station (near mile marker 70.5 on Highway 11); see the park's monthly events listing for dates.",
  "Kahuku“七月圣诞”市集": "Christmas in July at Kahuku",
  "每年夏天在 Kahuku 游客接待站旁草地上办的家庭市集：夏威夷手工艺品、音乐表演和本地小吃，小朋友有免费的脸部彩绘和刨冰，由公园之友和夏威夷太平洋公园协会主办。": "A family fair held each summer on the lawn beside the Kahuku visitor contact station, with Hawaiian crafts, music, and local food, plus free face painting and shave ice for kids. Hosted by Friends of Hawaiʻi Volcanoes National Park and Hawaiʻi Pacific Parks Association.",
  "免费，门口不收门票。": "Free; no entrance fee is charged at the gate.",
  "2026 年是 7 月 18 日（周六）9:00–15:00；2027 年的日期还没公布。": "In 2026 it was Saturday, July 18, 9 a.m.–3 p.m.; 2027 dates haven't been announced.",
  "山顶雨林志愿清理": "Stewardship at the Summit (rainforest restoration)",
  "志愿者跟着项目负责人在山顶雨林里拔除入侵植物，给夏威夷本地植物腾地方；穿结实的鞋和长裤，手套、工具都提供，大约半天。": "Volunteers work with a project leader to pull invasive plants in the summit rainforest, making room for native Hawaiian plants. Wear sturdy shoes and long pants; gloves and tools are provided. About half a day.",
  "免费、不用预约，活动日早上 8:45 在 Kīlauea 游客中心停车场集合；18 岁以下要家长陪同并签同意书。每月 3–4 次，日期看公园每月的活动公告。": "Free, no reservation needed. Meet at 8:45 a.m. on the event day in the Kīlauea Visitor Center parking lot. Volunteers under 18 must be with a parent and have a signed consent form. Held three or four times a month; see the park's monthly events listing for dates.",
  "梅里君王节（希洛）": "Merrie Monarch Festival (Hilo)",
  "世界上最有名的草裙舞（hula）比赛，每年复活节那一周在希洛举行，纪念推动夏威夷文化复兴的卡拉卡瓦国王；周四到周六晚上是古典和现代草裙舞比赛，周六上午有皇家巡游，一整周还有免费的手工艺市集和表演。这一周希洛酒店往往提前很久订满，来公园的人也多。": "The world's best-known hula competition, held in Hilo every year during Easter week in honor of King Kalākaua, who championed the revival of Hawaiian culture. Thursday through Saturday nights bring the ancient and modern hula competitions, Saturday morning has a royal parade, and free craft fairs and performances run all week. Hilo hotels often book up far in advance that week, and the park gets busier too.",
  "比赛门票只能寄纸质申请表抽签，每人最多 2 张，国际申请抽中后会发邮件联系付款；比赛也有电视和网络直播。手工艺市集、巡游免费。": "Competition tickets are available only through a lottery by mailed paper application, up to two per person; international applicants who win are contacted by email to pay. The competition is also broadcast on TV and streamed online. The craft fairs and parade are free.",
  "2027 年是 3 月 28 日到 4 月 3 日，门票申请要在 2026 年 11 月 16 日或以后寄出（邮戳为准）。": "In 2027 it runs March 28–April 3; ticket applications must be mailed (postmarked) on or after November 16, 2026.",
  "银剑草开花": "Haleakalā silversword (ʻāhinahina) bloom",
  "银剑草只长在哈莱阿卡拉的高山火山砂坡上，长几年到几十年才开一次花：从银色的叶球里抽出一人多高的花茎，开满紫红色的小花，开完整株就死去。多在夏天开花，风小的下午能闻到淡淡的香味，每年开花的株数差别很大。": "Silverswords grow only on the alpine cinder slopes of Haleakalā, and each plant blooms just once, after several years to several decades: a flower stalk taller than a person shoots up from the silver rosette, covered in small purplish-red flowers, and then the whole plant dies. Most bloom in summer; on calm afternoons you can catch a faint scent. The number of plants blooming varies widely from year to year.",
  "不用预约。Kalahaku 观景台、山顶停车场边和 Sliding Sands 步道上都能看到，只能远观，不要走下步道靠近。": "No reservation needed. You can see them at Kalahaku Overlook, beside the summit parking area, and along the Sliding Sands Trail. View them only from a distance; don't step off the trail to get closer.",
  "护林员活动和 Kīpahulu 文化示范": "Ranger programs & Kīpahulu cultural demonstrations",
  "护林员不定期在山顶游客中心和 Kīpahulu 讲火山、银剑草、夏威夷雁和星空；Kīpahulu 游客中心旁的传统草屋 Hale Hālāwai 有时有夏威夷文化示范，比如编织、做芋泥（poi）、织渔网和草裙舞。": "Rangers give occasional talks at the summit visitor center and at Kīpahulu on volcanoes, silverswords, nēnē, and the night sky. At Hale Hālāwai, the traditional thatched house next to the Kīpahulu Visitor Center, there are sometimes Hawaiian cultural demonstrations such as weaving, poi making, net making, and hula.",
  "免费、不用预约（门票另付）；时间看公园日历或到游客中心问。": "Free, no reservation needed (entrance fee applies). Check the park calendar or ask at a visitor center for times.",
  "Cycle to the Sun 自行车爬坡赛": "Cycle to the Sun",
  "每年 8 月初一个周六举行的自行车爬坡赛：从海边的 Paia 一路骑到 3,055 米的山顶，约 58 公里、爬升 3,000 多米的连续上坡。比赛期间公园里的山顶公路车速很慢。": "A hill climb bike race held on a Saturday in early August: riders climb from Paia by the ocean to the 10,023-foot summit, about 36 miles and roughly 10,000 feet of nonstop climbing. During the race, traffic on the summit road in the park moves very slowly.",
  "观赛不用预约；比赛那天上午开车上山要预留更多时间，注意路上的车手。": "No reservation needed to watch. On race morning, allow extra time to drive up, and watch for riders on the road.",
  "2025 年是 8 月 2 日 8:00–13:30；2026 年和 2027 年的日期没查到 NPS 的公告。": "In 2025 it was August 2, 8 a.m.–1:30 p.m. No NPS announcement of the 2026 or 2027 dates could be found.",
  "进湾游船季": "Glacier Bay day boat season",
  "夏季每天早上一班双体船从 Bartlett Cove 开到湾底的 Margerie、Grand Pacific 冰川再开回来，全程约 8 小时，NPS 护林员随船讲解，是不坐邮轮的人进湾的主要方式。": "Every summer morning, a catamaran leaves Bartlett Cove for Margerie and Grand Pacific glaciers at the head of the bay and comes back, about 8 hours in all, with an NPS ranger narrating on board. It's the main way into the bay if you're not on a cruise ship.",
  "向 Glacier Bay Lodge & Tours 预订（官网或 888-229-8687），2026 年成人 $273.57、3–12 岁 $142.92，含午餐；也可以订酒店的“住宿 + 早餐 + 游船”套餐。": "Book with Glacier Bay Lodge & Tours (online or at 888-229-8687). In 2026, $273.57 for adults and $142.92 for ages 3–12, lunch included. You can also book the lodge's package of lodging, breakfast, and the boat.",
  "2026 年是 5 月 22 日到 9 月 7 日，每天 6:50 登船、7:15 开、约 15:30 回来；2027 年的日期和价格以官网公布为准。": "In 2026 the boat ran May 22–September 7, boarding daily at 6:50 a.m., departing at 7:15 a.m., and returning around 3:30 p.m. Check the website for 2027 dates and prices.",
  "Bartlett Cove 护林员活动": "Bartlett Cove ranger programs",
  "夏季每天 13:30 护林员从 Glacier Bay Lodge 门口带 90 分钟的森林步道讲解，跟着冰川留下的“脚印”认识雨林和海岸；11:00 在酒店放映厅放公园影片，18:00 有约 30 分钟的晚间讲座，每晚题目不同。": "Every summer day at 1:30 p.m., a ranger leads a 90-minute forest walk from the front of Glacier Bay Lodge, following the glacier's “footprints” to learn about the rainforest and the shore. At 11 a.m. the park film shows in the lodge auditorium, and at 6 p.m. there's an evening talk of about 30 minutes on a different topic each night.",
  "免费，不用预约；当天的节目表贴在酒店里，也能在 NPS App 的活动日历查。": "Free, no reservation needed. The day's schedule is posted in the lodge and on the events calendar in the NPS App.",
  "2026 年是 5 月 22 日到 9 月 7 日。": "In 2026, programs ran May 22–September 7.",
  "Huna 部落屋开放日": "Open house at Xunaa Shuká Hít",
  "夏季 Huna 特林吉特部落的讲解员在部落屋接待游客，讲特林吉特人在冰川湾的生活、冰川怎样把他们赶出家园，以及部落和国家公园管理局后来怎样和解；下午还放两部关于部落屋和这段历史的影片。": "In summer, Huna Tlingit interpreters welcome visitors at the tribal house, sharing Tlingit life in Glacier Bay, how the glaciers drove them from their homeland, and how the tribe and the National Park Service later reconciled. In the afternoon, two films about the tribal house and this history are shown.",
  "免费，不用预约，开门时间内随时进去。": "Free, no reservation needed; drop in anytime it's open.",
  "2026 年 5 月 26 日到 8 月 29 日的周二到周六 13:00–17:30 开门（15:45、16:30 放影片），时间可能因部落活动调整。": "In 2026, open Tuesday through Saturday, 1–5:30 p.m., May 26–August 29 (films at 3:45 and 4:30 p.m.); hours may change for tribal events.",
  "座头鲸季": "Humpback whale season",
  "座头鲸每年夏天到冰川湾和湾口的 Icy Strait 觅食，6 月中以后明显多起来，7–8 月最多；坐进湾的游船、在 Bartlett Cove 划皮划艇或坐 Gustavus 出发的看鲸船都常能看到，游客中心的水听器还能听到它们的叫声。鲸多的时候 NPS 会划出“鲸鱼水域”限制船速。": "Humpback whales come to feed in Glacier Bay and in Icy Strait at its mouth every summer, becoming noticeably more common after mid-June and peaking in July–August. You'll often see them from the day boat, while kayaking at Bartlett Cove, or on whale-watching boats from Gustavus, and the hydrophone at the visitor center lets you hear their calls. When whales are plentiful, NPS designates whale waters with boat speed limits.",
  "在湾里看鲸跟进湾游船；专门看鲸可以订 Gustavus 出发去 Point Adolphus 的看鲸船。": "To see whales in the bay, take the day boat; for a dedicated trip, book a whale-watching boat from Gustavus to Point Adolphus.",
  "坐邮轮游冰川湾": "Cruising Glacier Bay by cruise ship",
  "多数游客是坐内湾航道（Inside Passage）的邮轮来的：船在湾里待一整天（约 9–10 小时），开到湾底的潮水冰川前停几个小时；NPS 护林员和 Huna 部落的讲解员在湾口上船，全程广播讲解。湾里每天最多只放两艘大邮轮进来，乘客不下船，所以不用排进这里的行程。": "Most visitors arrive on Inside Passage cruise ships. Ships spend a full day in the bay (about 9–10 hours) and stop for a few hours in front of the tidewater glaciers at its head, while NPS rangers and Huna Tlingit interpreters board at the mouth of the bay and narrate over the PA system. No more than two large cruise ships enter the bay each day, and passengers don't go ashore, so this doesn't need a place in an on-land itinerary.",
  "不是每条阿拉斯加邮轮航线都进冰川湾（有的去 Hubbard 冰川等别的地方），订邮轮时看清行程里有没有 Glacier Bay。": "Not every Alaska cruise goes into Glacier Bay (some go to Hubbard Glacier or elsewhere instead), so when you book, check that Glacier Bay is on the itinerary.",
  "午夜太阳": "Midnight sun",
  "Coldfoot 在北极圈以北约 75 公里，6 月初到 7 月中旬太阳整夜不落，只是山谷里半夜太阳会躲到山后。想看太阳贴着北边地平线转一圈，夏至前后可以在 Dalton 公路 132 英里处的 Gobblers Knob 爬上路东的小山，或者翻过 Atigun 山口到北坡，那里 5 月下旬到 7 月中旬 24 小时都是白天。": "Coldfoot is about 47 miles north of the Arctic Circle, and from early June to mid-July the sun never sets, though in the valley it dips behind the mountains around midnight. To watch the sun circle along the northern horizon, around the summer solstice climb the hill east of the road at Gobblers Knob (Dalton Highway mile 132), or cross Atigun Pass to the North Slope, where it's light 24 hours a day from late May to mid-July.",
  "不用预约。半夜也很亮，带眼罩睡觉；6 月中旬到 7 月也是蚊子最多的时候。": "No reservation needed. It's bright even at midnight, so bring an eye mask for sleeping. Mid-June through July is also peak mosquito season.",
  "极光季": "Northern lights season",
  "8 月下旬到次年 4 月中旬夜里够黑就有机会看到极光。Coldfoot、Wiseman 和 Bettles 都在极光带正下方，北边的山谷几乎没有灯光，晴夜大多看得到；BLM 说 9 月和 3 月最好，9 月还不太冷、Dalton 公路也好开。": "From late August to mid-April, you can see the northern lights whenever the night is dark enough. Coldfoot, Wiseman, and Bettles sit right under the auroral oval, the valleys to the north have almost no lights, and on most clear nights there's a show. BLM says September and March are best; in September it isn't too cold yet and the Dalton Highway is easier to drive.",
  "9 月到 10 月上旬自驾去 Coldfoot 住两三晚最划算，Coldfoot Camp 的 Wiseman 极光团每人 $89（8 月 21 日到次年 4 月 21 日）。冬天别自己开 Dalton 公路：北阿拉斯加旅游公司有在 Coldfoot 住两晚的极光团（坐车去、坐小飞机回，2026–27 冬季每人 $1,019–1,169，按两人一间算），Bettles Lodge 也有坐飞机去的极光套餐。": "The best value is driving to Coldfoot in September or early October and staying two or three nights; Coldfoot Camp's Wiseman aurora tour is $89 per person (August 21–April 21). Don't drive the Dalton Highway yourself in winter: Northern Alaska Tour Company runs aurora tours with two nights in Coldfoot (up by road, back by small plane; $1,019–1,169 per person for winter 2026–27, based on double occupancy), and Bettles Lodge has fly-in aurora packages.",
  "布鲁克斯山脉秋色": "Fall colors in the Brooks Range",
  "秋色先从北坡开始（8 月中旬），布鲁克斯山脉 8 月下旬最盛，育空河以南要到 9 月初：苔原和灌丛变成一片红、橙、金，山顶开始落新雪，蚊子也少了，晚上还能碰上第一批极光。": "Fall color starts on the North Slope (mid-August), peaks in the Brooks Range in late August, and reaches south of the Yukon River in early September. The tundra and brush turn red, orange, and gold, fresh snow starts dusting the peaks, the mosquitoes thin out, and at night you may catch the first auroras of the season.",
  "不用预约；这段时间去 Coldfoot 的人多，住宿早订，带好保暖衣物，9 月起随时可能下雪。": "No reservation needed. Coldfoot is busy at this time, so book lodging early and pack warm layers; snow is possible any time from September on.",
  "Coldfoot 游客中心晚间讲座": "Evening programs at the Arctic Interagency Visitor Center",
  "游客中心夏季开放期间每晚 8 点有护林员讲座，讲北极的动物、原住民、淘金和输油管的故事；要进公园徒步、漂流的人也在这里听行前说明、借防熊食物桶。": "While the visitor center is open in summer, rangers give talks every night at 8 p.m. on Arctic wildlife, Alaska Native peoples, the gold rush, and the pipeline. Anyone heading into the park to backpack or float also gets a trip briefing and borrows bear-resistant food containers here.",
  "免费，不用预约。": "Free, no reservation needed.",
  "Arctic Mountain Safari（Coldfoot 往北的向导车）": "Arctic Mountain Safari from Coldfoot",
  "不想自己开 Coldfoot 以北的山路，可以坐 Coldfoot Camp 的向导车往北，经过 Sukakpak 山、Chandalar Shelf，天气允许时开到 Atigun 山口，路上讲当地的地质、动物和冻土。": "If you'd rather not drive the mountain road north of Coldfoot yourself, take Coldfoot Camp's guided van north past Sukakpak Mountain and Chandalar Shelf to Atigun Pass (weather permitting), with commentary on local geology, wildlife, and permafrost along the way.",
  "打 Coldfoot Camp 的电话（907-474-3500）预订，2026 年每人 $129，不含餐，可以在营地买盒饭带上。": "Book by calling Coldfoot Camp (907-474-3500). In 2026 it's $129 per person, meals not included; you can buy a boxed lunch at the camp to take along.",
  "Wiseman 村探访": "Wiseman Village Visit",
  "向导带着从 Coldfoot 开到 Wiseman，看村里的小博物馆、进当地人的木屋，听他们讲在北极圈以北打猎、设陷阱、种菜过冬的日子。": "A guide drives you from Coldfoot to Wiseman to see the village's small museum and step inside a local cabin, where residents talk about hunting, trapping, and growing food to get through the winter north of the Arctic Circle.",
  "打 Coldfoot Camp 的电话（907-474-3500）预订，2026 年每人 $69；北阿拉斯加旅游公司的 Coldfoot 过夜团也能加买。": "Book by calling Coldfoot Camp (907-474-3500); $69 per person in 2026. It can also be added to Northern Alaska Tour Company's overnight Coldfoot tours.",
  "Koyukuk 河中叉漂流": "Koyukuk River Float",
  "在 Coldfoot 附近的 Koyukuk 河中叉跟向导坐橡皮艇顺流漂一段，水流平缓，看河谷两岸的山和夏天的北极植物。": "Float a stretch of the Middle Fork of the Koyukuk River near Coldfoot in a raft with a guide. The water is gentle, with mountains on both sides of the valley and Arctic plants in summer.",
  "打 Coldfoot Camp 的电话（907-474-3500）预订，2026 年每人 $149，大约 5 月中到 9 月中营业。": "Book by calling Coldfoot Camp (907-474-3500); $149 per person in 2026. Operates from about mid-May to mid-September.",
  "费尔班克斯出发的北极圈团": "Arctic Circle tours from Fairbanks",
  "不租车也能去北极圈：北阿拉斯加旅游公司夏季每天有坐车往返的一日团（早上 9:45 出发、半夜 1–2 点回，在育空河吃饭、在北极圈拍照拿证书），也有一程坐车、一程坐小飞机的团，或在 Coldfoot 住一两晚、再加买观光飞行和漂流。": "You can reach the Arctic Circle without a rental car. In summer, Northern Alaska Tour Company runs daily round-trip day tours by road (leaving at 9:45 a.m. and returning around 1–2 a.m., with a meal at the Yukon River and a photo and certificate at the Arctic Circle). There are also tours with one leg by road and one by small plane, or with one or two nights in Coldfoot, where you can add flightseeing and rafting.",
  "在 northernalaska.com 预订，订的时候全额付款，出发前 7 天内取消不退。2027 年夏季坐车一日团每人 $239–259，坐车去、在 Coldfoot 住一晚、坐飞机回的团 $509–559（按两人一间算）。": "Book at northernalaska.com; full payment is due at booking, and cancellations within 7 days of departure aren't refunded. For summer 2027, the road day tour is $239–259 per person, and the tour up by road with one night in Coldfoot and a flight back is $509–559 (based on double occupancy).",
  "荒野背包和漂流（多日）": "Backpacking and river trips",
  "真正走进公园要靠多日的荒野行程：坐小飞机降落在湖上或河滩，背包穿越没有路的山谷，或者坐橡皮艇、充气独木舟漂流 Alatna、John、Noatak、Koyukuk 河北叉这些国家荒野河流（公园里有 6 条）。一路几乎碰不到人，没有手机信号，要完全自给自足。": "Really getting into the park takes a multiday wilderness trip: fly in by small plane to land on a lake or gravel bar, then backpack through trailless valleys, or float a national wild river (the park has six) such as the Alatna, John, Noatak, or North Fork Koyukuk by raft or packraft. You'll see almost no one, there's no cell service, and you must be completely self-sufficient.",
  "没有经验的跟 NPS 许可的向导公司去（Arctic Wild、Expeditions Alaska、Indigo Alpine Guides 等，多日团每人几千到上万美元）；自己去的提前几个月订好包机，过夜必须用防熊食物桶，一队最多 10 人，带卫星通讯设备。": "Without experience, go with an NPS-permitted guide company (such as Arctic Wild, Expeditions Alaska, or Indigo Alpine Guides; multiday trips run from several thousand to more than $10,000 per person). On your own, book your charter flight months ahead. Bear-resistant food containers are required overnight, groups are limited to 10, and you should carry a satellite communicator.",
  "Bettles 护林站的行前说明": "Bettles Ranger Station and Visitor Center",
  "Bettles 是公园南界外约 30 公里、只能坐飞机去的小村，NPS 的护林站兼游客中心就在机场对面：进园背包、漂流的人在这里听行前说明、借防熊食物桶、问河水情况，也有展览、影片和护林员讲解，可以盖国家公园护照章。": "Bettles is a fly-in village about 19 miles outside the park's southern boundary, and the NPS ranger station and visitor center is right across from the airstrip. Backpackers and river runners heading into the park get trip briefings, borrow bear-resistant food containers, and ask about river conditions here. There are also exhibits, films, and ranger talks, and you can get your national park passport stamped.",
  "不用预约。护林站大约 6 月 10 日到 9 月 15 日开，周一到周六 14:00–18:00，冬季关闭。Wright Air 从费尔班克斯有定期航班（2026 年 8 月时刻表周一到周五 13:15 起飞），当天来回不现实，一般住一晚 Bettles Lodge。": "No reservation needed. The ranger station is open about June 10–September 15, Monday through Saturday, 2–6 p.m., and closed in winter. Wright Air has scheduled flights from Fairbanks (on the August 2026 schedule, departing at 1:15 p.m. Monday through Friday). A same-day round trip isn't realistic, so most people spend a night at Bettles Lodge.",
  "西部北极驯鹿群秋季渡河": "Western Arctic caribou fall migration",
  "西部北极驯鹿群每年春天往北穿过科伯克谷，到布鲁克斯山脉以北产仔，秋天再往南回来，很多在 Onion Portage 一带游过 Kobuk 河，沙丘上留下密密麻麻的蹄印。这是当地 Iñupiat 人最重要的猎季，也是公园最壮观的景象，但时间越来越难预测：NPS 说 2000 年以前多在 8 月中旬开始南迁，之后推迟到 9 月，最近几年常到 10 月底、11 月才过河；驯鹿群也减到 2025 年的约 12 万头，是 1970 年代以来最少的。": "Each spring the Western Arctic caribou herd heads north through the Kobuk Valley to calve beyond the Brooks Range, then returns south in fall, with many animals swimming the Kobuk River around Onion Portage and leaving the dunes covered in hoofprints. It's the most important hunting season for the local Iñupiat and the park's most spectacular sight, but the timing is getting harder to predict. NPS says that before 2000 the southbound migration usually began in mid-August, later shifting to September, and in recent years the caribou often haven't crossed the river until late October or November. The herd has also shrunk to about 120,000 animals in 2025, the smallest since the 1970s.",
  "没有专门的观驯鹿团；想碰运气就在 9 月包机去 Onion Portage 或沙丘一带，出发前问空中出租车和遗产中心驯鹿最近走到哪了。猎季里尊重打猎的村民，别靠近猎人和营地。": "There are no dedicated caribou-viewing tours. To try your luck, charter a flight to Onion Portage or the dunes in September, and before you go ask the air taxis and the heritage center where the caribou were last seen. During hunting season, respect the villagers who are hunting and keep away from hunters and their camps.",
  "大沙丘的飞行季": "Great Kobuk Sand Dunes flight season",
  "夏秋两季 Kotzebue 的空中出租车可以把人送到科伯克大沙丘上降落，待几个小时再接回来；背包客也可以在沙丘上扎营住几天。7 月最暖，6、7 月蚊子最多，8、9 月虫子少很多。": "In summer and fall, air taxis from Kotzebue can land you on the Great Kobuk Sand Dunes for a few hours and pick you up later; backpackers can also camp on the dunes for a few days. July is warmest, mosquitoes are worst in June and July, and there are far fewer bugs in August and September.",
  "向 Arctic Backcountry Flying Service（907-442-3200）或 Golden Eagle Outfitters（907-388-5968）包机，按飞机和飞行时间报价，几个人合包。参考 Arctic Backcountry 2026 年 7 月公布的村庄包机价：Kotzebue 到 Kiana 村 $1,000、到 Ambler 村 $2,000（按架次）。": "Charter with Arctic Backcountry Flying Service (907-442-3200) or Golden Eagle Outfitters (907-388-5968); prices depend on the plane and flight time, so a few people often share a charter. For reference, Arctic Backcountry's village charter rates posted in July 2026: Kotzebue to Kiana $1,000 and to Ambler $2,000 (per flight).",
  "Kobuk 河漂流（5–7 天）": "Floating the Kobuk River",
  "Kobuk 河坡缓水慢，从上游的 Ambler 村漂到下游的 Kiana 村，穿过整个公园约 5–7 天，可以上岸走到大沙丘、在 Onion Portage 停一停。适合有野外露营经验、会划船的人；河上常有当地人的摩托艇，逆风有时大到要顺着水流使劲划才能前进。": "The Kobuk River has a gentle grade and slow current. Floating from the village of Ambler upstream to Kiana downstream, through the whole park, takes about 5–7 days, with time to hike up to the Great Kobuk Sand Dunes and stop at Onion Portage. Best for paddlers with backcountry camping experience. Locals' motorboats often use the river, and headwinds can be strong enough that you have to paddle hard even going downstream.",
  "自己去的把可折叠的船当行李，坐定期航班飞到 Ambler（或 Shungnak、Kobuk 村）下水，从 Kiana 或 Noorvik 村坐定期航班回 Kotzebue；也可以找 NPS 许可的向导公司。7 月到 9 月上旬最好，6 月河上可能还有冰，9 月中下旬开始结冰。": "On your own, check a folding boat as luggage and take a scheduled flight to Ambler (or the villages of Shungnak or Kobuk) to put in; from Kiana or Noorvik, take a scheduled flight back to Kotzebue. You can also go with an NPS-permitted guide company. July to early September is best; there may still be ice on the river in June, and it starts freezing in mid-to-late September.",
  "Kotzebue 的午夜太阳": "Midnight sun in Kotzebue",
  "Kotzebue 在北极圈以北约 40 公里，6 月初到 7 月上旬太阳整夜不落，半夜还能在海边散步。": "Kotzebue is about 25 miles north of the Arctic Circle, and from early June to early July the sun never sets. You can still walk along the shore at midnight.",
  "不用预约；带个眼罩睡觉。": "No reservation needed; bring an eye mask for sleeping.",
  "遗产中心的讲座和社区活动": "Programs at the Northwest Arctic Heritage Center",
  "遗产中心全年不定期办讲座、工作坊和儿童活动，讲公园的自然、历史、当地的科研和 Iñupiat 文化；夏天也有护林员带的活动。": "Year-round, the heritage center holds occasional talks, workshops, and kids' programs on the parks' nature and history, local research, and Iñupiat culture; there are also ranger-led programs in summer.",
  "免费；时间不固定，去之前打电话（907-442-3890）或看 NPS 的活动日历。": "Free. Schedules vary, so call before you go (907-442-3890) or check the NPS events calendar.",
  "向导带的多日荒野行程": "Guided multi-day trips",
  "想在沙丘上扎营、又没有荒野经验，可以跟 NPS 许可的向导公司去：通常和北极之门或诺阿塔克河连在一起，5 到 12 天，全程露营，包机、装备、伙食都由公司安排。": "To camp on the dunes without backcountry experience, go with an NPS-permitted guide company. Trips usually combine Kobuk Valley with Gates of the Arctic or the Noatak River, last 5–12 days, and are fully camped, with the company handling charter flights, gear, and food.",
  "例如 Arctic Wild 的“北极之门和科伯克谷”5 天营地团，2027 年 7 月 17–21 日、每人 $9,100，从 Kotzebue 出发，沙丘上住两天、北极之门住两天；Indigo Alpine Guides、Alaska Alpine Adventures 也有带沙丘的多日团。名额很少，尽早订。": "For example, Arctic Wild's 5-day Gates of the Arctic and Kobuk Valley basecamp trip runs July 17–21, 2027, for $9,100 per person, starting in Kotzebue, with two nights on the dunes and two in Gates of the Arctic. Indigo Alpine Guides and Alaska Alpine Adventures also run multiday trips that include the dunes. Space is very limited, so book early.",
  "Brooks 瀑布的熊季": "Bear season at Brooks Falls",
  "红鲑 6 月底开始洄游，熊跟着来到 Brooks 河：7 月熊在瀑布上抓跳起来的鱼，7 月中旬最多；7 月底熊散去，8 月有时一整天看不到；8 月底以后鲑鱼产完卵死去，9 月熊又成群回来，在下游河段捞死鱼，个个养得又肥又换了新毛。": "Sockeye salmon start running in late June, and the bears follow them to the Brooks River. In July, bears at the falls catch leaping fish, with numbers peaking in mid-July. By late July the bears disperse, and in August you may go a whole day without seeing one. After late August, the salmon spawn and die, and in September the bears gather again to scoop dead fish from the lower river, fat and in fresh coats.",
  "坐看熊一日游或在 Brooks Lodge、营地过夜；7 月人最多，瀑布观景台常要排队。": "Come on a bear-viewing day trip or stay overnight at Brooks Lodge or the campground. July is the busiest month, and there's often a wait for the falls platform.",
  "2026 年 Brooks Camp 的服务是 6 月 1 日到 9 月 17 日，Brooks Lodge 和 Katmai Air 到 9 月 18 日；2027 年的日期以官网为准。": "In 2026, Brooks Camp services ran June 1–September 17, with Brooks Lodge and Katmai Air through September 18. Check the official websites for 2027 dates.",
  "胖熊周（Fat Bear Week）": "Fat Bear Week",
  "每年秋天公园和 explore.org 办的网上投票：把 Brooks 河上的熊夏初、秋末的照片放在一起，比谁冬眠前吃得最胖，淘汰赛进行一周，2025 年收到 170 多万票、来自 100 多个国家。夏秋两季 explore.org 还在网上直播 Brooks 瀑布的熊。": "An online vote held each fall by the park and explore.org: photos of the Brooks River bears from early summer and late fall are posted side by side, and people vote for the bear that fattened up best before hibernation. The bracket runs for a week; in 2025 it drew more than 1.7 million votes from more than 100 countries. In summer and fall, explore.org also livestreams the bears at Brooks Falls.",
  "在 fatbearweek.org 网上投票，免费；直播在 explore.org 的 Brooks Falls bearcam。": "Vote free online at fatbearweek.org; the livestream is on explore.org's Brooks Falls bearcam.",
  "2026 年是 9 月 22–29 日（9 月 18 日公布对阵表，周末不投票），2027 年的日期一般 9 月公布。": "In 2026 it ran September 22–29 (the bracket was posted September 18, with no voting on the weekend). Dates for 2027 are usually announced in September.",
  "海岸看熊季": "Coastal bear viewing season",
  "6 月到 7 月初，海岸的熊在草甸吃刚长出的莎草、退潮时在泥滩挖蛤蜊，也是交配、母熊带小熊出来的时候；7–8 月鲑鱼进溪，熊转到溪口抓鱼，看得更稳定。": "In June and early July, coastal bears graze on fresh sedge in the meadows and dig clams on the mudflats at low tide. It's also mating season and when sows bring out their cubs. In July–August, salmon enter the streams and the bears move to the creek mouths to fish, making viewing more reliable.",
  "向 Homer（或 Kodiak）的航空公司订带向导的一日游。": "Book a guided day trip with an air service in Homer (or Kodiak).",
  "万烟谷巴士导览季": "Valley of Ten Thousand Smokes tour season",
  "每天一班巴士从 Brooks Camp 开到万烟谷边的观景小屋，护林员随车讲解 1912 年的 Novarupta 大爆发，可以跟着下到谷底。": "A daily bus runs from Brooks Camp to an overlook cabin at the edge of the Valley of Ten Thousand Smokes. A ranger on board explains the great 1912 Novarupta eruption, and you can follow along down to the valley floor.",
  "向 Brooks Lodge（Katmailand）预订，2026 年含午餐 $115。": "Book with Brooks Lodge (Katmailand); $115 in 2026, lunch included.",
  "2026 年是 6 月 5 日到 9 月 17 日，每天 9:00–16:00；2027 年以官网为准。": "In 2026 the tour ran June 5–September 17, daily 9 a.m.–4 p.m. Check the official website for 2027.",
  "Brooks Camp 文化遗址讲解": "Brooks Camp cultural site walk",
  "Brooks 河口一带几千年来都是人们捕鱼、居住的地方：游客中心旁有一条约 160 米的自导步道，通到复原的半地下竖穴屋；有护林员时每天 14:00 带约 1 小时的讲解。": "People have fished and lived around the mouth of the Brooks River for thousands of years. A self-guided trail of about 500 feet next to the visitor center leads to a reconstructed semi-subterranean pit house, and when a ranger is available there's a 1-hour talk daily at 2 p.m.",
  "免费，不用预约，在游客中心问当天有没有。": "Free, no reservation needed. Ask at the visitor center whether there's a talk that day.",
  "5 月底到 7 月，Cook 湾海岸的熊在盐沼吃新长出的莎草，退潮时到泥滩挖蛤蜊，6 月也是交配季；夏末鲑鱼进溪，熊转到河口和溪边，Silver Salmon Creek 8 月以后还有银鲑洄游，看熊、钓鱼都好。": "From late May through July, bears along the Cook Inlet coast graze on fresh sedge in the salt marshes and dig clams on the mudflats at low tide, and June is mating season too. In late summer, salmon enter the streams and the bears move to river mouths and creeks. Silver Salmon Creek also gets a coho run from August on, good for both bear viewing and fishing.",
  "向安克雷奇、Homer、Soldotna 的航空公司订带向导的一日游，或住 Silver Salmon Creek、Chinitna 湾的看熊度假屋（只能飞进去）。": "Book a guided day trip with an air service in Anchorage, Homer, or Soldotna, or stay at a bear-viewing lodge at Silver Salmon Creek or Chinitna Bay (fly-in only).",
  "Crescent 湖红鲑季": "Crescent Lake salmon & bear season",
  "夏末红鲑游进 Crescent 湖，在湖岸和入湖的溪流产卵，棕熊沿岸捉鱼；Redoubt 火山下的湖边秋色也在 9 月。": "In late summer, sockeye salmon swim into Crescent Lake to spawn along the shore and in its inlet streams, and brown bears fish along the banks. Fall color on the lakeshore beneath Redoubt Volcano also comes in September.",
  "坐 Lake Hood 出发的一日游（Rust's，8 月 1 日到 9 月 25 日），或住湖边的 Redoubt Mountain Lodge。": "Take a day trip from Lake Hood (Rust's, August 1–September 25), or stay at Redoubt Mountain Lodge on the lake.",
  "Proenneke 小屋开放季": "Proenneke's Cabin open season",
  "Upper Twin Lake 化冰后，NPS 的护林员和志愿者在 Dick Proenneke 的小木屋值守、带游客参观，讲他怎样用自己做的工具盖房子、在荒野里独自生活 30 年。": "Once the ice goes out on Upper Twin Lakes, NPS rangers and volunteers staff Dick Proenneke's cabin and show visitors around, telling how he built it with tools he made himself and lived alone in the wilderness for 30 years.",
  "不用预约，也不收费；坐水上飞机去（安克雷奇约 1 小时多，Port Alsworth 约 30 分钟）。": "No reservation and no fee. Get there by floatplane (a little over 1 hour from Anchorage, about 30 minutes from Port Alsworth).",
  "2026 年大约 5 月底开到 9 月底，每天 10:00–16:00（开门日期看湖面化冰）。": "In 2026, open from about late May to late September, daily 10 a.m.–4 p.m. (opening depends on ice-out).",
  "春季野花和溪水": "Spring wildflowers",
  "冬雨过后山坡转绿，2 月起野花陆续开放，3–4 月最盛：步道两边是加州罂粟、羽扇豆和各种小野花，Chalone 溪、Bear 溪有水，Sycamore 步道雨后偶尔有小瀑布。这也是全年游客最多的时候。": "After winter rains the hills turn green, wildflowers start blooming in February, and they peak in March–April: California poppies, lupine, and many smaller flowers line the trails, Chalone and Bear creeks run, and after rain the Sycamore Trail sometimes has small waterfalls. It's also the busiest time of year.",
  "不用预约；周末和节假日早上 8 点前到，或者平日来。": "No reservation needed. On weekends and holidays, arrive before 8 a.m., or come on a weekday.",
  "看加州神鹫": "California condor viewing",
  "加州神鹫是北美最大的陆地鸟类，1987 年全世界只剩 27 只，尖峰石阵是全美几个人工繁育放归点之一，如今在园里筑巢繁殖。最容易看到的是 High Peaks 一带和 Condor Gulch 上空，清早和傍晚乘着上升气流盘旋。": "The California condor is North America's largest land bird. In 1987 only 27 were left in the world. Pinnacles is one of a handful of captive-breeding release sites in the U.S., and condors now nest in the park. The best places to see them are around the High Peaks and over Condor Gulch, where they soar on rising air in the early morning and evening.",
  "不用预约；带望远镜，保持距离、不要喂食。": "No reservation needed. Bring binoculars, keep your distance, and don't feed them.",
  "Bear Gulch 洞穴整洞开放": "Bear Gulch Cave fully open",
  "Bear Gulch 洞穴的上半段是汤森大耳蝠的栖息地，一年里大多关着；只有 3 月和 10 月蝙蝠不在时整洞开放，一般是月底那一周，蝙蝠少的年份能开一整个月，可以从下洞一路钻到上洞再出到水库边。5 月中到 7 月中蝙蝠育幼，整个洞都关。": "The upper part of Bear Gulch Cave is home to Townsend's big-eared bats and stays closed most of the year. It opens fully only in March and October, when the bats are away, usually for the last week of the month, or the whole month in years with few bats. You can then squeeze from the lower cave all the way through the upper cave and out by the reservoir. From mid-May to mid-July, when the bats are raising young, the whole cave is closed.",
  "不用预约，带手电；具体哪几天开看 NPS 洞穴状态页。": "No reservation needed; bring a flashlight. Check the NPS cave status page for exact open dates.",
  "2026 年 10 月 1 日起上、下洞都开着。": "Since October 1, 2026, both the upper and lower cave have been open.",
  "春季周末接驳车（东侧）": "East Side weekend shuttle",
  "冬末到春天的周五到周日，东侧有接驳车从营地开到 Bear Gulch 日间区，8:00–17:30 运行，末班 17:30 从 Bear Gulch 开回；Bear Gulch 一带停满时可以把车停在营地再坐车上去。": "Fridays through Sundays from late winter through spring, an east-side shuttle runs between the campground and the Bear Gulch Day Use Area, 8 a.m.–5:30 p.m., with the last return from Bear Gulch at 5:30 p.m. When Bear Gulch parking fills, leave your car at the campground and ride up.",
  "不用预约；具体开始、结束的日期 NPS 每年公布。": "No reservation needed; NPS announces the start and end dates each year.",
  "2026 年的接驳车季已经结束。": "The 2026 shuttle season has ended.",
  "猛禽育雏期（攀岩限制）": "Raptor advisory season",
  "每年 1 月到 6、7 月游隼、金雕等猛禽在岩壁上筑巢，公园会把有巢的岩峰划为敏感区，请攀岩者和离开步道的人避开；正式步道不受影响。": "From January to June or July each year, peregrine falcons, golden eagles, and other raptors nest on the cliffs. The park designates rock formations with nests as sensitive areas and asks climbers and off-trail hikers to avoid them; official trails aren't affected.",
  "攀岩前看 NPS 的猛禽公告或两侧的攀岩公告板。": "Before climbing, check the NPS raptor advisory or the climbing bulletin boards on either side of the park.",
  "2026 年的限制 7 月 6 日已全部解除。": "All 2026 restrictions were lifted on July 6.",
  "大盆地天文节": "Great Basin Astronomy Festival",
  "每年 9 月新月前后的周末举行，一连几晚在 Lehman Caves 游客中心旁的天文剧场开星空派对：志愿者摆出几十台望远镜，护林员讲星座，白天有天文学家讲座、太阳望远镜、天文摄影工作坊，还能参观全美唯一建在国家公园里的研究级天文台 Great Basin Observatory。": "Held each September on a weekend near the new moon, with star parties several nights running at the astronomy amphitheater next to the Lehman Caves Visitor Center: volunteers set up dozens of telescopes and rangers talk about constellations. By day there are talks by astronomers, solar telescopes, and astrophotography workshops, and you can tour the Great Basin Observatory, the only research-grade observatory in a U.S. national park.",
  "活动免费，大多不用预约；天文台参观当天在游客中心先到先得、每团 15 人，摄影工作坊要在 Great Basin National Park Foundation 报名。营地和 Baker 的住宿很早订满。": "Events are free, and most need no reservation. Observatory tours are first come, first served at the visitor center that day, 15 people per group; photography workshops require registration with the Great Basin National Park Foundation. Campgrounds and lodging in Baker fill very early.",
  "2026 年是 9 月 10–13 日；2027 年的日期等公园公布（一般在夏天）。": "In 2026 it was September 10–13; 2027 dates will come from the park (usually in summer).",
  "夏季护林员观星": "Ranger-led astronomy programs",
  "大约阵亡将士纪念日到劳动节，每周四到周日晚上在天文剧场：护林员先讲 30 分钟，再用望远镜带大家看 1.5 小时；夏天周三晚上另有在 Baker 镇 Great Basin 游客中心对面的星座讲解。天文节以后场次变少，10 月结束。": "From about Memorial Day to Labor Day, Thursday through Sunday nights at the astronomy amphitheater, a ranger gives a 30-minute talk followed by 1.5 hours at the telescopes. On summer Wednesday nights there's also a constellation tour across from the Great Basin Visitor Center in Baker. After the astronomy festival, programs become less frequent and end in October.",
  "免费、不用预约，但人数有上限，游客中心停车场停满就不再放人；开始时间随日落变，看公园日历。下雨打雷取消。": "Free, no reservation needed, but attendance is capped: once the visitor center parking lot is full, no more people are admitted. Start times change with sunset; check the park calendar. Canceled in rain or thunder.",
  "山杨秋色": "Fall aspen colors",
  "一般 9 月第二、三周开始变色：惠勒峰景观道两边的山杨林最方便看，Baker Creek 环线有特别高大的山杨林，Snake Creek 沿路是金黄的三叶杨；初雪落下时白、黄、绿三色叠在一起最好看。": "Color usually starts in the second or third week of September. The aspen groves along Wheeler Peak Scenic Drive are the easiest to see, the Baker Creek loop has especially tall aspens, and the Snake Creek road is lined with golden cottonwoods. When the first snow falls, the white, gold, and green together look their best.",
  "不用预约；景观道一般 11 月 1 日前第一场大雪后关上段，10 月去之前看路况。": "No reservation needed. The upper scenic drive usually closes after the first big snow, before November 1; check road conditions before an October visit.",
  "公园 40 周年庆典（2026 年 10 月 23 日）": "Great Basin 40th Anniversary Celebration",
  "大盆地 1986 年 10 月 27 日成为国家公园。2026 年 10 月 23 日庆祝 40 周年和 Lehman Caves 新照明完工：Baker 礼堂有讲洞穴成因、换灯工程和建园历史的讲座，14:00 在游客中心后面剪彩，当天 Grand Palace 洞穴导览全天免费。": "Great Basin became a national park on October 27, 1986. On October 23, 2026, the park celebrates its 40th anniversary and the completion of new lighting in Lehman Caves, with talks in the Baker auditorium on how the cave formed, the lighting project, and the park's founding, a ribbon cutting behind the visitor center at 2 p.m., and free Grand Palace cave tours all day.",
  "免费；洞穴导览票早上 8 点起在 Lehman Caves 游客中心现场先到先得，不在网上卖。停车位很少，尽量拼车。": "Free. Cave tour tickets are first come, first served at the Lehman Caves Visitor Center starting at 8 a.m., not sold online. Parking is very limited, so carpool if you can.",
  "只在 2026 年 10 月 23 日。": "October 23, 2026, only.",
  "夏至日出（Baker 考古遗址）": "Summer solstice at Baker Archeological Site",
  "Baker 镇外的 Baker 考古遗址是约 800 年前弗里蒙特人（Fremont）村落的遗迹，NPS 说夏至那天日出和遗址的布局会对成一线；这里平时也是看星星、拍星空的地方。": "Baker Archeological Site, outside the town of Baker, preserves the remains of a Fremont village from about 800 years ago. NPS says the summer solstice sunrise lines up with the site's layout. It's also a popular spot for stargazing and night sky photography.",
  "不用预约，遗址归 BLM 管，在公园外。": "No reservation needed. The site is managed by BLM and lies outside the park.",
  "冬季雪鞋和越野滑雪": "Winter snowshoeing & cross-country skiing",
  "冬天惠勒峰景观道从 Upper Lehman Creek 营地往上不通车，积雪的公路和步道就成了雪鞋、越野滑雪的路线，一路几乎遇不到人，能看到雪地里的动物脚印。Lehman Caves 和游客中心冬天照常开。": "In winter, Wheeler Peak Scenic Drive is closed to cars above Upper Lehman Creek Campground, and the snow-covered road and trails become snowshoe and cross-country ski routes. You'll see almost no one, but you will see animal tracks in the snow. Lehman Caves and the visitor center stay open in winter.",
  "不用预约，装备自己带。天气变化快，出发前到 Lehman Caves 游客中心问雪况和雪崩风险。": "No reservation needed; bring your own gear. The weather changes fast, so ask about snow conditions and avalanche risk at the Lehman Caves Visitor Center before you go.",
  "春季沙漠花季": "Spring desert bloom",
  "雨水好的年份，2 月起低处沙漠开出一片片蓝紫色的大弯羽扇豆（Big Bend bluebonnet，比得州别处的更高大），3–4 月接着是仙人掌、丝兰、刺木（ocotillo）的花，Ross Maxwell 观景道和河路两边最多；山上的花要等夏末雨季。每年差别很大，冬天干旱的年份可能几乎不开。": "In years with good rain, from February on, the low desert fills with patches of blue-purple Big Bend bluebonnets (taller than the bluebonnets elsewhere in Texas), followed in March–April by blooming cactus, yucca, and ocotillo, especially along the Ross Maxwell Scenic Drive and River Road. Flowers in the mountains wait for the late-summer rains. It varies widely from year to year, and after a dry winter there may be almost no bloom.",
  "不用预约；花况看游客中心的公告或 NPS 社交媒体。春假前后人最多，住宿要早订。": "No reservation needed; check visitor center notices or NPS social media for bloom reports. Spring break is the busiest time, so book lodging early.",
  "格兰德河漂流（圣埃伦娜峡谷等）": "Rio Grande river trips",
  "坐皮划艇、独木舟或橡皮艇顺着格兰德河漂进最深约 450 米的峡谷：圣埃伦娜峡谷可以一天来回或两三天，Boquillas 峡谷约 53 公里、适合新手的多日行程，Mariscal 峡谷最短但最偏远。河道中线就是国界，除了安全原因不能上墨西哥那边的岸。": "Float the Rio Grande by kayak, canoe, or raft into canyons up to about 1,500 feet deep. Santa Elena Canyon works as a day trip or a two- to three-day trip, Boquillas Canyon is a roughly 33-mile multiday trip suited to beginners, and Mariscal Canyon is the shortest but most remote. The middle of the river is the international border, and you can't land on the Mexican side except for safety reasons.",
  "Terlingua、Lajitas 的漂流公司（如 Far Flung Outdoor Center、Big Bend River Tours）有半天到多日的团，包许可证、装备和接送；自己划要到游客中心办漂流许可证。": "Outfitters in Terlingua and Lajitas (such as Far Flung Outdoor Center and Big Bend River Tours) run trips from half a day to several days, including permits, gear, and shuttles. To paddle on your own, get a river use permit at a visitor center.",
  "能不能漂、漂哪段要看水位，干旱时圣埃伦娜峡谷常常水太浅；2026 年 8 月 12 日起圣埃伦娜船只下水点一带因国土安全部的边境工程封闭，10 月初往峡谷的路又因山洪封着，出发前问漂流公司。": "Whether you can float, and which stretch, depends on water levels; in drought, Santa Elena Canyon is often too shallow. Since August 12, 2026, the area around the Santa Elena boat launch has been closed for Department of Homeland Security border construction, and in early October the road to the canyon was also closed by flash flooding. Check with an outfitter before you go.",
  "护林员讲解和星空活动": "Ranger programs & night sky programs",
  "旺季护林员和志愿者每周有免费的讲解、带队徒步和星空活动（观星会、月光漫步、认星座），地点在 Panther Junction、盆地、格兰德河村等处。大弯是国际暗夜公园，没有活动的晚上自己找个远离营地的路边也能看银河。": "In peak season, rangers and volunteers lead free talks, guided hikes, and night sky programs (star parties, moonlight walks, constellation tours) each week at Panther Junction, the Chisos Basin, Rio Grande Village, and elsewhere. Big Bend is an International Dark Sky Park; on nights with no program, find a roadside spot away from the campgrounds and you can still see the Milky Way.",
  "免费、一般不用预约；每周的活动表贴在游客中心和 NPS 网站上。": "Free, usually no reservation needed. The weekly schedule is posted at visitor centers and on the NPS website.",
  "隔壁大弯牧场州立公园 2026 年秋天另有“边境星空派对”（10 月 10 日、11 月 7 日、12 月 5 日），要在 Texas Parks & Wildlife 网站报名。": "Next door, Big Bend Ranch State Park has its own “Border Star Parties” in fall 2026 (October 10, November 7, and December 5); register on the Texas Parks & Wildlife website.",
  "观鸟：Colima 林莺和春季迁徙": "Birding: Colima Warbler & spring migration",
  "大弯记录到的鸟约 450 种，是全美国家公园里最多的之一。4–5 月候鸟北迁经过格兰德河村的棉白杨林；Colima 林莺在美国只在奇索斯山繁殖，4 月中到 9 月在 Boot 峡谷一带能听到、看到，是观鸟的人专程上山的目标。": "About 450 bird species have been recorded at Big Bend, one of the highest counts of any U.S. national park. In April–May, migrants pass through the cottonwoods at Rio Grande Village on their way north. The Colima warbler nests in the U.S. only in the Chisos Mountains, and from mid-April to September you can hear and see it around Boot Canyon; birders hike up specifically to find it.",
  "不用预约；去 Boot 峡谷要走南缘一带的长步道，一早出发。": "No reservation needed. Reaching Boot Canyon means a long hike in the South Rim area, so start early.",
  "Terlingua 辣椒大赛": "Terlingua International Chili Championship",
  "从 1967 年开始的辣椒炖肉（chili）比赛，每年 11 月第一个周六前后在 Terlingua 举行，现在分成两个比赛（CASI 的锦标赛和 “Original” 的那一个），几天里有音乐、营地派对，几千人涌进这个小镇。": "A chili cook-off dating to 1967, held each year around the first Saturday of November in Terlingua. It's now split into two competitions (the CASI championship and the “Original”), with several days of music and campground parties that bring thousands of people to this small town.",
  "要在两个比赛的官网买门票或营地票；那几天 Terlingua、Study Butte 一带的住宿很早就订满。": "Buy admission or camping passes on each competition's website. Lodging in Terlingua and Study Butte books up very early for those days.",
  "2026 年是 11 月 4–7 日（CASI 写 11 月 3–7 日）。": "In 2026 it's November 4–7 (CASI lists November 3–7).",
  "Terlingua 亡灵节": "Día de los Muertos in Terlingua",
  "每年 11 月 2 日晚上，Terlingua 老墓地里的家人和镇民来扫墓，在坟头摆上照片、花和食物，点满蜡烛，是墨西哥传统的亡灵节；游客可以安静地在旁边看。": "On the night of November 2 each year, families and townspeople gather in the old Terlingua cemetery to tend the graves, setting out photos, flowers, and food and lighting candles everywhere for the Mexican tradition of Día de los Muertos. Visitors are welcome to watch quietly.",
  "不用预约；墓地里的坟大多有人祭扫，别踩、别动供品，拍照先问。": "No reservation needed. Most graves are tended by families: don't step on them or touch the offerings, and ask before taking photos.",
  "从 1965 年演到现在的夏季露天歌舞秀，在 Medora 镇西山坡上能坐 2,800 人的 Burning Hills 露天剧场，背后就是恶地；乡村和流行歌舞、杂技、真马上台，穿插罗斯福和北达科他的故事，最后放烟花。周二到周日晚上 7:30 开演、约 2 小时，周一停演。": "An outdoor summer musical show running since 1965 at the 2,800-seat Burning Hills Amphitheatre on the hillside west of Medora, with the badlands as a backdrop. Country and pop song and dance, acrobats, and live horses onstage are mixed with stories of Theodore Roosevelt and North Dakota, and it ends with fireworks. Shows start at 7:30 p.m. Tuesday through Sunday and last about 2 hours; there's no show on Mondays.",
  "在 medora.com、etix.com 或打 1-800-MEDORA-1 订票，成人约 $63–86，6 岁以下免费；夏季周末和 7 月初很早卖完。只认官方渠道，第三方转卖常有加价和假票。": "Book at medora.com or etix.com, or call 1-800-MEDORA-1. Adults pay about $63–86, and kids under 6 are free. Summer weekends and early July sell out early. Buy only through official channels; third-party resellers often charge markups or sell fake tickets.",
  "2026 年演出季是 6 月 3 日到 9 月 12 日；2027 年 6 月重开，具体日期还没公布。": "The 2026 season ran June 3–September 12. It reopens in June 2027; exact dates haven't been announced.",
  "叉子烤牛排（Pitchfork Steak Fondue）": "Pitchfork Steak Fondue",
  "音乐剧开演前在剧场旁的山顶露台吃的西部晚餐：厨师把整块纽约客牛排插在干草叉上，放进大油桶里炸熟，配自助的烤豆子、土豆和沙拉，一边吃一边看恶地日落。傍晚 5 点多开餐（和音乐剧一样周一不开），吃完直接走去看演出。": "A Western dinner on the hilltop terrace next to the amphitheater before the musical: cooks spear whole New York strip steaks on pitchforks and fry them in big oil drums, served with a buffet of baked beans, potatoes, and salad while you watch the sun set over the badlands. Dinner starts a little after 5 p.m. (like the musical, it's closed Mondays), and afterward you walk straight over to the show.",
  "和音乐剧一起在 medora.com 订，成人约 $58 以内（官方说高于这个价的多半是假票），12 岁以下儿童热狗餐免费。": "Book with the musical at medora.com. Adults pay up to about $58 (the official site says higher prices usually mean fake tickets), and hot dog meals for kids under 12 are free.",
  "2026 年和音乐剧同季（6 月 3 日到 9 月 12 日），6 月 28 日到 7 月 1 日因总统到访停了几天；2027 年日期未公布。": "In 2026 it ran the same season as the musical (June 3–September 12), with a few days off June 28–July 1 for a presidential visit. 2027 dates haven't been announced.",
  "Dakota Nights 天文节": "Dakota Nights Astronomy Festival",
  "公园每年 8 月办的两天天文节：下午在 South Unit 游客中心草坪用太阳望远镜看太阳黑子、给小朋友做火箭，傍晚有讲座；晚上 20:45 到 23:30 志愿者在 Peaceful Valley Ranch 架起望远镜看行星、星云和银河。": "The park's two-day astronomy festival each August. In the afternoon, look at sunspots through solar telescopes on the South Unit visitor center lawn and build rockets with the kids; early evening brings talks. From 8:45 to 11:30 p.m., volunteers set up telescopes at Peaceful Valley Ranch to show planets, nebulae, and the Milky Way.",
  "免费，不用预约；晚上看星星不能用白光手电，带红光灯，穿保暖外套。": "Free, no reservation needed. No white flashlights during night viewing: bring a red light and a warm jacket.",
  "2026 年是 8 月 14–15 日（2025 年是 8 月 22–23 日），每年日期不同，以公园公布为准。": "In 2026 it was August 14–15 (in 2025, August 22–23). Dates change every year; go by what the park announces.",
  "护林员讲解、马耳他十字小屋导览": "Ranger programs & Maltese Cross Cabin tours",
  "夏天护林员带着看罗斯福的第一间牧场小屋、讲野牛，也带短途徒步；小屋全年在游客中心开放时间里都能自己进去看，夏天才有讲解。": "In summer, rangers show visitors Theodore Roosevelt's first ranch cabin, talk about bison, and lead short hikes. You can see the cabin on your own year-round whenever the visitor center is open; talks are offered only in summer.",
  "不用预约，时间看游客中心的公告或公园日历。": "No reservation needed. Check visitor center notices or the park calendar for times.",
  "春天的小野马": "Feral horse foaling season",
  "South Unit 有大约 200 匹野马，是当年附近牧场跑出来的马的后代，公园当作历史文化资源保留。春天是小马出生的季节，常能在景观环路边、Painted Canyon 一带甚至 I-94 上看到一群一群带着小马的马群。": "The South Unit has about 200 wild horses, descendants of horses that escaped from nearby ranches long ago, kept by the park as a historic and cultural resource. Spring is foaling season, and you'll often see bands with foals along the Scenic Loop Drive, around Painted Canyon, and even along I-94.",
  "不用预约。至少离 25 码（约 23 米）远，用长焦或望远镜看，不要喂。": "No reservation needed. Stay at least 25 yards away, use a telephoto lens or binoculars, and don't feed them.",
  "2026 年公园给 72 匹母马打避孕针，逐步减少数量、不再清走马群；国会还在讨论要求至少保留 150 匹的法案，以后的数量看最终决定。": "In 2026 the park gave contraceptive shots to 72 mares to reduce the herd gradually rather than remove the horses. Congress is still debating a bill requiring at least 150 horses to be kept; future numbers depend on the final decision.",
  "7–8 月公野牛会追着母牛跑、互相顶撞，在土坑里打滚、低吼，两个园区的公路边都常见；这时公牛脾气最差，比平时更危险。": "In July–August, bull bison chase cows, butt heads, wallow in dirt pits, and bellow, often right beside the roads in both units. Bulls are at their most short-tempered now and more dangerous than usual.",
  "不用预约。待在车里看最安全，下车至少离 25 码（约 23 米），被野牛盯住就慢慢退开。": "No reservation needed. Watching from your car is safest; if you get out, stay at least 25 yards away, and if a bison stares you down, back away slowly.",
  "秋天的麋鹿鸣叫和三叶杨变黄": "Elk bugling & fall color",
  "9 月中到 10 月是 South Unit 麋鹿的发情季，清早和傍晚 Buck Hill 一带的草原上能听到公鹿高亢的叫声；9 月下旬到 10 月初，小密苏里河两岸的三叶杨和草原一起变黄，游客也少了很多。": "Mid-September through October is the elk rut in the South Unit. Early morning and evening, you can hear bulls' high-pitched bugles across the prairie around Buck Hill. From late September to early October, the cottonwoods along the Little Missouri River turn gold along with the grasslands, and the crowds thin out.",
  "不用预约。清早或傍晚去 Buck Hill、Boicourt 一带，带望远镜。": "No reservation needed. Go to the Buck Hill and Boicourt area in the early morning or evening, and bring binoculars.",
  "恶地天文节": "Badlands Astronomy Festival",
  "每年 7 月中下旬办三天：白天有缩尺太阳系步行、太阳望远镜观测和讲座，晚上请来天文学家演讲，再由业余天文爱好者摆出几十台望远镜带大家看星空。2012 年起每年举办，恶地 2026 年获得国际暗夜公园认证。": "A three-day festival in mid-to-late July: by day, a scale-model solar system walk, solar telescope viewing, and talks; at night, a talk by a visiting astronomer, then amateur astronomers set up dozens of telescopes to show you the sky. It has been held every year since 2012, and Badlands was certified as an International Dark Sky Park in 2026.",
  "免费、不用报名和门票（入园费另付）；日程到 Ben Reifel 游客中心领，或看 NPS 天文节页面。": "Free, with no registration or tickets needed (the park entrance fee is separate). Pick up a schedule at the Ben Reifel Visitor Center or see the NPS festival page.",
  "2026 年是 7 月 17–19 日；2027 年的日期还没公布，一般也在 7 月中下旬。": "In 2026 it was July 17–19. 2027 dates haven't been announced but are usually in mid-to-late July as well.",
  "夏夜讲解和星空观测": "Evening Program & Night Sky Program",
  "夏天每晚在 Cedar Pass 营地露天剧场，先是 30 分钟的护林员讲解（野牛、化石、拉科塔文化……每天不同），接着是星空观测：认星座、用望远镜看行星和星团，晴天能看到 7500 多颗星和清楚的银河。": "Every summer night at the Cedar Pass Campground amphitheater, there's a 30-minute ranger talk (bison, fossils, Lakota culture, and other topics that change nightly), followed by a night sky program: learn the constellations and look at planets and star clusters through telescopes. On clear nights you can see more than 7,500 stars and a sharp Milky Way.",
  "免费、不用预约；开始时间跟着日落变（2026 年 6–7 月 21:00、8 月 20:30、9 月 20:00），当天到游客中心确认。": "Free, no reservation needed. Start times follow sunset (in 2026, 9 p.m. in June–July, 8:30 p.m. in August, and 8 p.m. in September); confirm at the visitor center that day.",
  "护林员地质散步和化石讲解": "Geology Walk & Fossil Talks",
  "夏季每天的免费护林员活动：8:30 在 Door 步道带 30–45 分钟的地质散步，讲恶地的岩层怎么来的；10:30 和 14:00 在化石展示步道讲 20–30 分钟化石；17:30 从游客中心出发走一段草原。": "Free daily ranger programs in summer: at 8:30 a.m., a 30–45-minute geology walk on the Door Trail about how the badlands' rock layers formed; at 10:30 a.m. and 2 p.m., a 20–30-minute fossil talk on the Fossil Exhibit Trail; and at 5:30 p.m., a prairie walk from the visitor center.",
  "不用预约，到集合地点就行。": "No reservation needed; just show up at the meeting spot.",
  "2026 年是 5 月 17 日到 9 月 26 日。": "In 2026, offered May 17–September 26.",
  "化石修复室开放": "Fossil Preparation Lab",
  "Ben Reifel 游客中心里有一间对外开放的化石修复室，隔着玻璃看古生物学家和实习生清理、鉴定、编号园里刚挖出的化石，还能直接问他们问题，是美国国家公园里少有的。": "The Ben Reifel Visitor Center has a fossil preparation lab open to the public. Through the glass, watch paleontologists and interns clean, identify, and catalog fossils just dug up in the park, and ask them questions directly. Labs like this are rare in U.S. national parks.",
  "免费、不用预约。": "Free, no reservation needed.",
  "2026 年 5 月 23 日到 10 月 31 日开放，9:00–16:00。": "Open May 23–October 31, 2026, 9 a.m.–4 p.m.",
  "Sturgis 摩托车集会": "Sturgis Motorcycle Rally",
  "每年 8 月第一个周五起在黑山北边的 Sturgis 办 10 天，几十万骑手涌进南达科他西部，很多人会骑到恶地和黑山兜风。这几天 Loop Road 上摩托车成群，Wall、拉皮德城和黑山一带的旅馆价格翻倍、很早订满。": "A 10-day rally that starts the first Friday of August in Sturgis, north of the Black Hills, bringing hundreds of thousands of riders into western South Dakota, many of whom ride out to the Badlands and the Black Hills. During the rally, the Loop Road fills with motorcycles, and hotel prices in Wall, Rapid City, and the Black Hills double and sell out early.",
  "不是公园的活动；赶上这段时间的话住宿要提前很久订，开车多留意摩托车。": "This isn't a park event. If your trip overlaps with it, book lodging far in advance and watch for motorcycles on the road.",
  "2026 年是 8 月 7–16 日，2027 年是 8 月 6–15 日。": "In 2026 it's August 7–16; in 2027, August 6–15.",
  "马鹿求偶鸣叫和护林员听鹿活动": "Elk bugling programs",
  "秋天是马鹿的发情季，公鹿在黄昏到清晨发出高亢的“吹哨”一样的叫声争夺母鹿，在 Elk Mountain 营地、Boland Ridge 一带最容易听到。公园这时有护林员带的听鹿活动：先在游客中心草坪讲马鹿，再一起开车到园里的停车点静静地听。": "Fall is the elk rut. From dusk to dawn, bulls make high-pitched, whistle-like bugles as they compete for cows, easiest to hear around Elk Mountain Campground and Boland Ridge. During the rut, rangers lead elk bugling programs: a talk about elk on the visitor center lawn, then a drive together to a pullout in the park to listen quietly.",
  "免费、不用预约；带手电、椅子或垫子，穿暖和。": "Free, no reservation needed. Bring a flashlight and a chair or pad, and dress warmly.",
  "2026 年 9 月 14 日到 10 月 10 日的每周一、三、六晚上 7 点在游客中心前草坪集合；2027 年的日期还没公布。": "In 2026, the program met at 7 p.m. on the lawn in front of the visitor center every Monday, Wednesday, and Saturday from September 14 to October 10. 2027 dates haven't been announced.",
  "夏季烛光导览和野洞探险": "Candlelight & Wild Cave tours (summer only)",
  "只在夏天开的两种特别导览：提着蜡烛桶在没有灯的洞段里走的烛光导览（约 2 小时，8 岁以上），和戴头盔、头灯在没开发的洞里爬行的野洞探险（最长约 4 小时，16 岁以上）。名额很少，比常规导览难订得多。": "Two special tours offered only in summer: the Candlelight Tour, carrying candle buckets through an unlit section of the cave (about 2 hours, ages 8 and up), and the Wild Cave Tour, crawling through undeveloped cave with a helmet and headlamp (up to about 4 hours, ages 16 and up). Spots are very limited and much harder to get than on the regular tours.",
  "只能打电话预约（605-745-4600），最早提前 1 个月；烛光 $16、野洞 $45。": "Reservations by phone only (605-745-4600), up to 1 month ahead; Candlelight $16, Wild Cave $45.",
  "2026 年烛光导览 6 月 7 日到 8 月 22 日、野洞探险 6 月 7 日到 9 月 7 日。": "In 2026, Candlelight Tours ran June 7–August 22 and Wild Cave Tours June 7–September 7.",
  "卡斯特州立公园野牛围赶": "Custer State Park Buffalo Roundup",
  "园外：每年 9 月最后一个周五，牛仔和护林员骑马、开车把卡斯特州立公园约 1300 头野牛赶进围栏，做体检、打疫苗、挑出要拍卖的，最多两万多人站在山坡上看野牛群奔过草原，是黑山一年里最有名的活动之一；前后几天还有艺术节。": "Outside the park: on the last Friday of September each year, cowboys and rangers on horseback and in trucks drive Custer State Park's roughly 1,300 bison into corrals for health checks, vaccinations, and sorting out animals for auction. Up to 20,000-plus people line the hillsides to watch the herd thunder across the prairie. It's one of the best-known events of the year in the Black Hills, with an arts festival in the days around it.",
  "免费；停车场 6:15 开放、9:30 开始赶，野牛进围栏（一般到中午）之前不能离开观看区，要很早到；附近旅馆提前很久订满。": "Free. Parking opens at 6:15 a.m. and the roundup starts at 9:30 a.m.; you can't leave the viewing areas until the bison are in the corrals (usually around noon), so arrive very early. Nearby hotels book up far in advance.",
  "2026 年是 9 月 25 日（第 61 届），2027 年是 9 月 24 日。": "In 2026 it was September 25 (the 61st roundup); in 2027 it's September 24.",
  "园外：夏天每晚在拉什莫尔山的露天剧场，护林员讲解、放短片，最后点亮四座总统头像，约 45 分钟。": "Outside the park: every summer night in the Mount Rushmore amphitheater, a ranger talk and short film end with the lighting of the four presidents' faces, about 45 minutes in all.",
  "免费、不用预约，停车费另付；提前半小时到。": "Free, no reservation needed; the parking fee is separate. Arrive half an hour early.",
  "2026 年 5 月 23 日到 8 月 9 日 21:00 开始，8 月 10 日到 9 月 30 日 20:00 开始。": "In 2026, the program started at 9 p.m. from May 23 to August 9 and at 8 p.m. from August 10 to September 30.",
  "每年 8 月第一个周五起在黑山北边的 Sturgis 办 10 天，几十万骑手涌进黑山，Needles 公路、Iron Mountain 路和野生动物环线上摩托车成群，整个黑山和拉皮德城的旅馆价格翻倍、很早订满。": "A 10-day rally that starts the first Friday of August in Sturgis, north of the Black Hills, bringing hundreds of thousands of riders into the region. Needles Highway, Iron Mountain Road, and the Wildlife Loop fill with motorcycles, and hotel prices across the Black Hills and Rapid City double and sell out early.",
  "不是公园的活动；赶上这段时间住宿要很早订，热门山路早上去。": "This isn't a park event. If your trip overlaps with it, book lodging very early and drive the popular mountain roads in the morning.",
  "巨人柱开花": "Saguaro bloom",
  "巨人柱一年只开一次花：5 月底到 6 月，蜡白色的大花一簇簇开在枝头顶端，夜里开、第二天下午就谢，白天早上看得最清楚；蝙蝠、白翅鸽和蜜蜂都来采蜜。6 月底到 7 月花谢后结出红色的果子，裂开时像枝头又开了一朵红花。": "Saguaros bloom just once a year: from late May into June, clusters of large waxy white flowers open at the tips of the arms. They open at night and wilt by the next afternoon, so morning is the best time to see them, when bats, white-winged doves, and bees come to feed. After the flowers fade, red fruit forms in late June and July; when it splits open, it looks like a second red bloom on the arms.",
  "不用预约。花开在最高处，带望远镜或长焦镜头；这时候白天常到 40°C 以上，只在清早出门。": "No reservation needed. The flowers are at the very top, so bring binoculars or a telephoto lens. Daytime temperatures this time of year often top 104°F, so go out only in the early morning.",
  "季风雷暴季": "Monsoon season",
  "6 月中到 9 月底是索诺兰沙漠的夏季季风，午后山上常有雷暴，干河床几分钟内就会涨成山洪，雨后沙漠一下子转绿，傍晚的云和闪电很壮观。动物在这时交配、繁殖，傍晚能看到的野生动物也多。": "From mid-June to late September, the Sonoran Desert's summer monsoon brings frequent afternoon thunderstorms to the mountains, and dry washes can flash-flood within minutes. After rain the desert turns green almost overnight, and evening clouds and lightning put on a dramatic show. Animals mate and raise young now, so you'll see more wildlife in the evening.",
  "不用预约。下雨时远离峡谷和干河床，不要开车涉水；西区的砂石环线雨后常被冲坏封路。": "No reservation needed. In rain, stay out of canyons and washes, and don't drive through flowing water. The gravel loop on the west side is often washed out and closed after storms.",
  "2026 年 9 月的暴雨冲坏了西区 Bajada 环线，9 月 11 日起陆续封路，到 10 月初仍关闭。": "Heavy rain in September 2026 damaged the Bajada Loop Drive in the west district; sections began closing on September 11, and it was still closed in early October.",
  "冬季护林员讲座和导览": "Ranger and naturalist programs",
  "天气凉快的半年两个游客中心每天都有免费的讲座和短导览：讲巨人柱怎么长大、啄木鸟怎么在仙人掌里做窝、美洲狮和响尾蛇，西区还有带着走仙人掌园、去 Signal Hill 看岩画的导览；夏天太热，只有零星几场。": "During the cooler half of the year, both visitor centers offer free talks and short guided walks every day: how saguaros grow, how woodpeckers nest inside the cactus, mountain lions, and rattlesnakes. The west district also has guided walks through the cactus garden and to the petroglyphs at Signal Hill. Summer is too hot, so there are only a few scattered programs.",
  "免费、一般不用预约，门票照付；具体场次看 NPS 活动日历。": "Free and usually no reservation needed, though the entrance fee still applies. Check the NPS events calendar for specific programs.",
  "2026 年 10 月西区每天上午、中午、下午各有几场（如 9:15 仙人掌园导览、11:15 巨人柱讲座），10 月 16–30 日下午 2:15 有 Signal Hill 岩画导览，但 Bajada 环线封路期间可能取消。": "In October 2026 the west district has several programs every morning, midday, and afternoon (such as a 9:15 a.m. cactus garden walk and an 11:15 a.m. saguaro talk), and a Signal Hill petroglyph walk at 2:15 p.m. October 16–30, though it may be canceled while the Bajada Loop is closed.",
  "东区星空晚会": "Star Party (Rincon Mountain District)",
  "公园和图森业余天文协会在东区一起办的观星晚会：天文爱好者架好望远镜带大家看行星、星云，护林员还带小朋友拿紫外线手电在仙人掌间找会发荧光的蝎子。图森是全美最注意控制光污染的城市之一，东区夜空相当暗。": "A star party held in the east district by the park and the Tucson Amateur Astronomy Association. Amateur astronomers set up telescopes to show you planets and nebulae, and rangers take kids out among the cacti with UV flashlights to find scorpions that glow. Tucson is one of the most light-pollution-conscious cities in the U.S., and the east district's night sky is quite dark.",
  "免费，不用预约，晚会时间内随时来。": "Free, no reservation needed; drop in anytime during the event.",
  "2026 年这一场在 11 月 27 日晚上；12 月 20 日下午还有一场用太阳望远镜看太阳黑子的“Sun Party”。": "In 2026 this star party is on the evening of November 27. There's also a “Sun Party” on the afternoon of December 20 to look at sunspots through solar telescopes.",
  "图森宝石矿物展": "Tucson Gem and Mineral Show",
  "每年 1 月底到 2 月中旬，全世界的矿物、化石和宝石商人涌进图森，几十个展场遍布全城，是世界上最大的这类展会之一，不懂矿物逛逛也很有意思。": "From late January to mid-February each year, mineral, fossil, and gem dealers from around the world pour into Tucson, filling dozens of venues across the city. It's one of the largest shows of its kind in the world, and fun to browse even if you know nothing about minerals.",
  "大部分展场免费进；主展（Tucson Gem and Mineral Society Show）要买票。": "Most venues are free; the main show (the Tucson Gem and Mineral Society Show) requires a ticket.",
  "展期全城酒店大涨价、很难订，这几周去巨人柱的话住宿要很早订。": "Hotel prices across the city jump during the show and rooms are hard to find, so if you're visiting Saguaro in those weeks, book lodging very early.",
  "沙漠博物馆夏夜开放": "Cool Summer Nights at the Desert Museum",
  "6–8 月每个周六，亚利桑那–索诺拉沙漠博物馆开到晚上 10 点，天黑后能看到夜行动物出来活动，还有用紫外线灯找蝎子、看星星等主题活动，比白天凉快得多。": "Every Saturday in June–August, the Arizona-Sonora Desert Museum stays open until 10 p.m. After dark you can see nocturnal animals out and about, with themed activities such as hunting for scorpions with UV lights and stargazing. It's much cooler than during the day.",
  "买普通门票就能进；官网买票。": "A regular admission ticket gets you in; buy tickets on the museum's website.",
  "Sabino Canyon 夜游接驳车": "Sabino Canyon Night Tours",
  "夏秋的周六晚上，Sabino Canyon 的电动接驳车加开约 90 分钟的夜游：一路开到峡谷最里面，在上方观景点停 10 分钟看星星，再绕到 Bear Canyon 观景点看图森夜景。": "On summer and fall Saturday nights, the Sabino Canyon electric shuttle adds a roughly 90-minute night tour: it drives to the far end of the canyon, stops for 10 minutes at the upper overlook for stargazing, then swings by the Bear Canyon overlook for a view of Tucson's lights.",
  "每人 $15，在 sabinocanyoncrawler.com 订票，夜游场次在发车时间列表的最后一行。": "$15 per person; book at sabinocanyoncrawler.com. The night tour is the last line in the list of departure times.",
  "官网的说明写的是 6 月 28 日到 10 月 25 日每周六，7 点半发车、之后每月提前半小时（这是 2025 年的日期，2026 年的季节以官网为准）。": "The website lists Saturdays from June 28 to October 25, with a 7:30 p.m. departure that moves half an hour earlier each month (these are 2025 dates; check the website for the 2026 season).",
  "McKittrick 峡谷红叶": "Fall colors in McKittrick Canyon",
  "得州西部少有的秋色：海拔高、有泉水的峡谷里长着大齿枫、橡树和得州马德隆，一般 10 月中开始变色，10 月最后一周到 11 月第一周最盛，红、黄、褐色衬着灰白的石灰岩壁。McKittrick 峡谷最有名，Smith Spring、Devil's Hall 和北边的 Dog Canyon 也能看到，都要走进去才看得到。": "Fall color that's rare for West Texas: high, spring-fed canyons hold bigtooth maples, oaks, and Texas madrones that usually start turning in mid-October and peak from the last week of October through the first week of November, red, yellow, and brown against pale limestone walls. McKittrick Canyon is the most famous, and you can also see color at Smith Spring, Devil's Hall, and Dog Canyon to the north; in every case you have to hike in to see it.",
  "不用预约，但红叶季周末全园停车场常满，McKittrick 和 Pine Springs 会限流“出一辆进一辆”；尽量平日去，McKittrick 8:00 开门就到。": "No reservation needed, but on fall color weekends parking lots fill throughout the park, and McKittrick and Pine Springs switch to one car out, one car in. Go on a weekday if you can, and be at McKittrick when it opens at 8 a.m.",
  "每年变色时间随降雨和气温不同，出发前看公园的社交媒体或打电话问；Dog Canyon 常比东边早一两周。": "Timing varies each year with rainfall and temperature; check the park's social media or call before you go. Dog Canyon often turns a week or two earlier than the east side.",
  "春秋登山旺季": "Spring and fall hiking season",
  "3–5 月和 9–12 月气温最适合爬瓜达卢佩峰，也是公园一年里人最多的时候（春假、感恩节前后尤其多）。这个“最少人去的国家公园之一”的停车场和营地是按很少的游客设计的，旺季周末上午就会停满。": "March–May and September–December bring the best temperatures for climbing Guadalupe Peak, and this is also the park's busiest time of year (especially spring break and the days around Thanksgiving). Parking lots and campgrounds at one of the least-visited national parks were built for very few visitors, and on peak-season weekends they fill by midmorning.",
  "营地和背包营地都提前在 Recreation.gov 订；当天没有营位的话，最近的露营地在 1 小时外。": "Reserve campsites and backcountry sites ahead on Recreation.gov; if you arrive without a site, the nearest campground is an hour away.",
  "泉水边观鸟": "Birding at the springs",
  "山脚下的 Frijole、Manzanita 和 Smith 几处泉水是沙漠里少有的水源，一年四季都吸引鸟类和鹿、狐狸来喝水，春秋迁徙季种类最多；清早和傍晚在 Frijole 牧场的大树下、Manzanita 泉边安静地等最好。": "The Frijole, Manzanita, and Smith springs at the foot of the mountains are rare water sources in the desert, drawing birds, deer, and foxes to drink year-round, with the greatest variety during spring and fall migration. Wait quietly under the big trees at Frijole Ranch or by Manzanita Spring in the early morning or evening.",
  "不用预约，带望远镜；游客中心有鸟类名录。": "No reservation needed; bring binoculars. The visitor center has a bird checklist.",
  "沙漠星空": "Night skies",
  "公园周围上百公里几乎没有城镇，空气干燥，是得州看星星最好的地方之一：在 Pine Springs 营地、Salt Basin 沙丘的停车场（日落后 30 分钟内要离开）或 62/180 号公路边的停车点，没有月亮的晚上银河很清楚。": "With almost no towns for more than 60 miles around and dry air, this is one of the best places in Texas to see stars. On moonless nights the Milky Way is sharp from Pine Springs Campground, the Salt Basin Dunes parking area (you must leave within 30 minutes after sunset), or pullouts along US 62/180.",
  "不用预约；公园目前没有固定的观星活动，想在暗处待到深夜就订 Pine Springs 营地。": "No reservation needed. The park has no regular stargazing programs right now; to stay out late in the dark, reserve a site at Pine Springs Campground.",
  "蓝岭山脊上的橡树、枫树、山核桃一般 10 月中下旬变色，高处先红、再一路红到山脚和河谷；每年早晚随天气差一两个星期，干旱、暖秋的年份颜色偏淡。整条天际线公路就是赏叶路线，Stony Man、Hawksbill 和公路边的西侧观景台最好看。": "Oaks, maples, and hickories on the Blue Ridge usually turn in mid-to-late October, starting at the top and working down to the foothills and valleys. Timing shifts by a week or two each year with the weather, and colors are duller in dry or warm autumns. All of Skyline Drive is a leaf-peeping route, with the best views at Stony Man, Hawksbill, and the west-facing overlooks along the road.",
  "不用预约，但这是全年最挤的时候：周末入口排长队、热门步道口一早就停满，园内住宿和营地提前几个月就订满。尽量平日去，或者早上 8 点前进园；周末可以先玩人少的南区。": "No reservation needed, but this is the busiest time of year: weekend lines at the entrances are long, popular trailheads fill early, and in-park lodging and campgrounds book up months ahead. Go on a weekday if you can, or enter before 8 a.m.; on weekends, start in the less crowded South District.",
  "野花周末": "Wildflower Weekend",
  "公园每年 5 月初的周末办的野花活动（2026 年是 5 月 2–3 日）：护林员和志愿者带队认野花，有讲座和儿童活动，正赶上野杜鹃、延龄草和山茱萸开花。": "The park's wildflower event on a weekend in early May (May 2–3 in 2026): rangers and volunteers lead wildflower walks, with talks and kids' activities, right when wild azaleas, trilliums, and dogwoods are blooming.",
  "免费，大部分活动不用预约，日程在公园官网的特别活动页公布；门票照付。": "Free, and most events need no reservation; the schedule is posted on the special events page of the park website. The entrance fee still applies.",
  "2027 年的日期还没公布，往年都在 5 月上旬。": "2027 dates haven't been announced; in past years it has been in early May.",
  "Rapidan 营地导览季": "Rapidan Camp tours",
  "胡佛总统的夏季营地只能跟护林员坐面包车进去，5 月下旬到 10 月下旬的周四到周一开，每天两班，参观复原的总统小屋和展览。": "President Hoover's summer camp can be visited only by ranger-led van tour, Thursday through Monday from late May to late October, twice a day. You'll see the restored presidential cabin and exhibits.",
  "只能在 Recreation.gov 预约，最早提前 6 个月、最晚开团前 4 小时，现场不卖票。": "Reservations only on Recreation.gov, from 6 months to 4 hours before the tour; no tickets are sold on site.",
  "Big Meadows 看星空": "Stargazing at Big Meadows",
  "Big Meadows 地势高、四周是开阔的草甸，是美国东海岸大城市附近少有的暗夜观星点，晴朗无月的夏夜能看到银河。山上夜里比河谷冷 5–10°C，带厚外套。": "High up and surrounded by open meadow, Big Meadows is one of the few truly dark stargazing spots near the big cities of the East Coast, and on clear, moonless summer nights you can see the Milky Way. Nights on the mountain are 9–18°F colder than in the valley, so bring a warm jacket.",
  "自己去不用预约，挑新月前后的晴夜。夏秋偶有公园或 Big Meadows Lodge 办的观星活动，日程看公园和 Delaware North 官网。": "No reservation needed on your own; pick a clear night near the new moon. In summer and fall the park or Big Meadows Lodge occasionally holds stargazing programs; check the park and Delaware North websites for schedules.",
  "山月桂花期": "Mountain laurel bloom",
  "6 月初到中旬，山月桂在步道两边开满粉白色的小花，Limberlost 环线、Stony Man 和 Hawksbill 一带最集中；5 月中下旬的野杜鹃（pinxter）在 Mary's Rock 一带常见。": "From early to mid-June, mountain laurel covers the trailsides with small pinkish-white flowers, most densely around the Limberlost loop, Stony Man, and Hawksbill. In mid-to-late May, wild pinxter azaleas are common around Mary's Rock.",
  "不用预约；花期每年随海拔和气温前后差一两个星期。": "No reservation needed. Bloom timing shifts by a week or two each year with elevation and temperature.",
  "Skyland 骑马": "Horseback rides at Skyland Stables",
  "Skyland 马场带向导骑马走林间马道，适合不想走太多路的人；年龄、体重有限制，预约时问清楚。": "Skyland Stables offers guided rides on wooded horse trails, a good option if you don't want to walk much. Age and weight limits apply; ask when you book.",
  "提前打电话 540-999-2213 预约（Delaware North 经营），2026 年 5 月 1 日到 10 月 25 日营业。": "Call ahead to reserve at 540-999-2213 (run by Delaware North). Open May 1–October 25, 2026.",
  "护林员讲解": "Ranger programs",
  "春、夏、秋季在两个游客中心、Big Meadows 和各营地的露天剧场有护林员讲解和带队短走，讲黑熊、山里人家的历史和夜空。": "In spring, summer, and fall, rangers give talks and lead short walks at the two visitor centers, Big Meadows, and the campground amphitheaters, on black bears, the history of mountain families, and the night sky.",
  "不用预约，日程在游客中心公布。": "No reservation needed; schedules are posted at the visitor centers.",
  "桥日（Bridge Day）": "Bridge Day",
  "每年 10 月第三个周六，为纪念 1977 年大桥建成，US-19 大桥封路一天给行人走：一年里只有这一天能合法从桥上跳伞（BASE），几百名跳伞者从约 267 米高的桥面跳向峡谷，还有人从桥下的检修走道绳降。西弗吉尼亚最大的一日节庆，桥上桥头都是小吃摊，常有约 10 万人。": "On the third Saturday of every October, the US 19 bridge closes to traffic for a day and opens to pedestrians, marking its completion in 1977. It's the only day of the year you can legally BASE jump from the bridge: hundreds of jumpers leap from the deck, about 876 feet above the gorge, and others rappel from the catwalk beneath. It's the largest one-day festival in West Virginia, with food stands all over the bridge and both ends, and crowds that often reach about 100,000.",
  "免费、不用买票。大桥 9:00–15:00 对行人开放，7:00–17:00 封闭车辆；桥头附近不能停车，要在 Fayetteville、Oak Hill 一带的指定停车点坐接驳车（2026 年每人 $5，只收现金）。桥上不许带普通背包和手提袋（透明包可以）、宠物、自行车、婴儿车和冷藏箱。想从桥下看可以订 Bridge Walk 的桥日团（$125），下到谷底的大巴（Into the Gorge）要提前买票。": "Free, no tickets needed. The bridge is open to pedestrians 9 a.m.–3 p.m. and closed to vehicles 7 a.m.–5 p.m. There's no parking near the bridge; park at designated lots around Fayetteville and Oak Hill and take the shuttle ($5 per person in 2026, cash only). Regular backpacks and bags (clear bags are fine), pets, bikes, strollers, and coolers aren't allowed on the bridge. To watch from below, book a Bridge Walk Bridge Day tour ($125); buses down to the gorge floor (Into the Gorge) require advance tickets.",
  "2026 年是 10 月 17 日（前一天晚上在 Adventures on the Gorge 有收费的 Taste of Bridge Day）；当天 US-19 绕行 US-60 和 US-16 约多 45 分钟，Canyon Rim 游客中心停车场前一天 17:30 起关闭、当天上午才重开，Fayette Station Road 前一天 18:00 到当天 18:00 封路。2027 年按惯例是 10 月 16 日。Fayetteville 一带的住宿要提前几个月订。": "In 2026 it's October 17 (the paid Taste of Bridge Day takes place the night before at Adventures on the Gorge). That day, US 19 traffic detours via US 60 and US 16, adding about 45 minutes. The Canyon Rim Visitor Center parking lot closes from 5:30 p.m. the day before until the morning after, and Fayette Station Road is closed from 6 p.m. the day before to 6 p.m. on Bridge Day. Following tradition, 2027's Bridge Day is October 16. Book lodging around Fayetteville months ahead.",
  "新河漂流季": "New River whitewater rafting season",
  "4 月到 10 月是商业漂流的旺季：下游峡谷（Lower New）III–IV 级激流、最后从大桥下漂过，一般 12 岁以上；上游（Upper New）水缓、I–III 级，适合带小孩的家庭。6–8 月水温最舒服，春天水量最大、浪最猛。": "April to October is peak commercial rafting season. The Lower New gorge has Class III–IV rapids and ends by floating under the bridge, usually for ages 12 and up. The Upper New is calmer, Class I–III, and good for families with kids. Water temperatures are most comfortable in June–August, and spring brings the highest water and biggest waves.",
  "向西弗州政府许可的漂流公司预订（ACE Adventure Resort、Adventures on the Gorge、River Expeditions、New and Gauley River Adventures 等），全天团含午餐和接送，下游峡谷每人约 $140 起；夏季周末提前订。": "Book with a state-licensed outfitter (such as ACE Adventure Resort, Adventures on the Gorge, River Expeditions, or New and Gauley River Adventures). Full-day trips include lunch and shuttles, with Lower New trips starting at about $140 per person. Book ahead for summer weekends.",
  "Gauley 河放水季": "Gauley Season",
  "每年秋天上游的 Summersville 水库按计划放水，旁边 Gauley River 国家休闲区（NPS 另一个单位，在大桥北边约 40 分钟）的 Gauley 河变成美国最难的商业漂流河段之一，V 级激流一个接一个，主要在 9 月初到 10 月中的周末。只适合身体好、有漂流经验的成年人。": "Each fall, scheduled releases from Summersville Lake upstream turn the Gauley River in nearby Gauley River National Recreation Area (a separate NPS unit, about 40 minutes north of the bridge) into one of the most difficult commercially rafted rivers in the U.S., with one Class V rapid after another, mostly on weekends from early September to mid-October. Only for fit adults with rafting experience.",
  "向同一批漂流公司预订 Upper Gauley / Lower Gauley 团；放水日按陆军工程兵团公布的日程，周末最先订满。": "Book Upper Gauley or Lower Gauley trips with the same outfitters. Release days follow the schedule published by the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers, and weekends fill first.",
  "红叶季": "Fall foliage",
  "一般 10 月中下旬峡谷两岸的枫树、橡树和山核桃变成红、橙、黄，从 Long Point、Grandview、Canyon Rim 看大桥和马蹄弯都是一年里最好看的时候；清晨谷里常起雾。": "In mid-to-late October, the maples, oaks, and hickories on both sides of the gorge usually turn red, orange, and yellow. It's the best time of year to look out at the bridge and the horseshoe bend from Long Point, Grandview, and Canyon Rim. Fog often fills the gorge in the early morning.",
  "不用预约。红叶季周末（尤其赶上桥日那个周末）步道口很早停满、Fayetteville 住宿紧张，尽量平日去、一早出发。": "No reservation needed. On fall color weekends (especially Bridge Day weekend), trailheads fill early and Fayetteville lodging is tight; go on a weekday if you can, and start early.",
  "杜鹃花季": "Rhododendron bloom",
  "Grandview 崖边的紫色卡托巴杜鹃大约 5 月中开，林下大片白色的大杜鹃（西弗吉尼亚州花）7 月开；Endless Wall、Long Point 步道两旁也有。每年花期前后差一两个星期。": "Purple Catawba rhododendron on the cliffs at Grandview blooms around mid-May, and great masses of white great rhododendron (the West Virginia state flower) bloom in the understory in July. You'll also find them along the Endless Wall and Long Point trails. Bloom timing shifts by a week or two each year.",
  "不用预约，花期可以问护林员或看公园的 Facebook。": "No reservation needed. Ask a ranger or check the park's Facebook page for bloom updates.",
  "Grandview 夏季露天剧（Theatre West Virginia）": "Theatre West Virginia outdoor dramas",
  "夏天在 Grandview 崖边的 Cliffside 露天剧场演出，招牌剧目是讲西弗吉尼亚从弗吉尼亚分出来建州的《Honey in the Rock》，也演音乐剧。": "Summer performances at the Cliffside Amphitheatre on the cliffs at Grandview. The signature show is Honey in the Rock, about West Virginia splitting from Virginia to become a state, and there are musicals too.",
  "在 Theatre West Virginia 官网买票，晚上开演。": "Buy tickets on the Theatre West Virginia website; shows are in the evening.",
  "2026 年是《Honey in the Rock》首演 65 周年，和《Shrek the Musical》轮流上演；2027 年的剧目还没公布。": "2026 is the 65th anniversary of Honey in the Rock's premiere, and it runs in rotation with Shrek the Musical. The 2027 lineup hasn't been announced.",
  "护林员导览和讲解": "Ranger programs",
  "阵亡将士纪念日到劳动节之间，护林员在 Canyon Rim、Grandview、Thurmond、Sandstone 等处带徒步、讲煤矿小镇和峡谷地质，Thurmond 还有小镇历史导览。": "Between Memorial Day and Labor Day, rangers lead hikes and give talks on coal towns and the geology of the gorge at Canyon Rim, Grandview, Thurmond, Sandstone, and other spots, and Thurmond also has guided tours of the town's history.",
  "免费、一般不用预约，日程看游客中心的公告和 NPS 官网的活动日历。": "Free, usually no reservation needed. Check visitor center notices and the events calendar on the NPS website for schedules.",
  "9 月下旬山顶的蓝莓灌丛先转红，10 月上中旬整座岛的枫树、桦树和橡树变成红、橙、金色，乔丹池、鹰湖马车道和卡迪拉克山顶都是看红叶的好地方，一般 10 月中下旬过了高峰。": "In late September, the blueberry bushes on the summits turn red first, and in early to mid-October the maples, birches, and oaks across the island turn red, orange, and gold. Jordan Pond, the Eagle Lake carriage roads, and the top of Cadillac Mountain are all good places for fall color, which is usually past peak by mid-to-late October.",
  "不用预约；红叶季周末（尤其 10 月第二个周一的哥伦布日 / 原住民日长周末）巴尔港住宿很早订满，停车场也像夏天一样一早就满。": "No reservation needed. On fall color weekends (especially the long Columbus Day/Indigenous Peoples' Day weekend, the second Monday in October), Bar Harbor lodging books up early, and parking lots fill early just as in summer.",
  "Island Explorer 2026 年大部分线路只开到 10 月 12 日，红叶季后半段要自己开车。": "In 2026 most Island Explorer routes run only through October 12, so for the later part of the foliage season you'll need to drive yourself.",
  "卡迪拉克山“全美第一缕阳光”": "First sunrise in the U.S. from Cadillac Mountain",
  "大约 10 月 7 日到次年 3 月 6 日，卡迪拉克山顶是美国本土最早看到日出的地方（其余时间是更东边的 Mars Hill 等地）；夏天虽然不是第一，山顶看海上日出照样是阿卡迪亚的招牌。": "From about October 7 to March 6, the summit of Cadillac Mountain is the first place in the contiguous U.S. to see the sunrise (the rest of the year, it's places farther east such as Mars Hill). In summer it may not be first, but sunrise over the ocean from the summit is still one of Acadia's signature experiences.",
  "5 月 20 日到 10 月 25 日（2026 年）开车上山要订日出车证（Recreation.gov，每车 $6）；12 月 1 日到次年 4 月 14 日山顶路不通车，只能沿 North Ridge 步道走上去。": "From May 20 to October 25 (in 2026), driving up requires a sunrise vehicle reservation (Recreation.gov, $6 per vehicle). From December 1 to April 14 the summit road is closed to cars, and you can get up only on foot via the North Ridge Trail.",
  "Island Explorer 免费班车季": "Island Explorer fare-free shuttle season",
  "免费的班车连接巴尔港、Hulls Cove 游客中心、Sand Beach、雷鸣洞、乔丹池、各营地、马车道入口和 Southwest Harbor 等地，还有 Schoodic 半岛的一条线；坐班车就不用抢停车位，车后的架子能放 6 辆自行车。不到卡迪拉克山顶和 Bass Harbor 灯塔。": "Free shuttles link Bar Harbor, the Hulls Cove Visitor Center, Sand Beach, Thunder Hole, Jordan Pond, the campgrounds, carriage road entrances, Southwest Harbor, and more, plus a route on the Schoodic Peninsula. Riding the shuttle means no fighting for parking, and the rack on the back holds six bikes. Shuttles don't go to the top of Cadillac Mountain or Bass Harbor Head Light.",
  "不用预约，上车免费，但坐车进园也要有公园门票；时刻表在 exploreacadia.com。": "No reservation needed and the ride is free, but you still need a park pass to enter the park by shuttle. Schedules are at exploreacadia.com.",
  "2026 年 Gateway Center、Loop Road、Schoodic 三条线 5 月 20 日起先开，其余线路 6 月 23 日到 10 月 12 日，8 月 17 日起换成秋季班次（班次少一些）。": "In 2026, the Gateway Center, Loop Road, and Schoodic routes started May 20, the other routes ran June 23–October 12, and fall schedules (with fewer runs) began August 17.",
  "游隼繁殖季（步道关闭和观鸟）": "Peregrine falcon nesting season",
  "游隼一度在美国东部绝迹，1980 年代起在阿卡迪亚重新放归，现在每年春天在 Champlain 山、Jordan Cliffs 等地的崖壁上筑巢。繁殖季绝壁步道、Jordan Cliffs、Penobscot East、Valley Cove 几条步道关闭，雏鸟会飞以后（往年多在 7 月底到 8 月）才重开。": "Peregrine falcons once disappeared from the eastern U.S. They were reintroduced at Acadia starting in the 1980s and now nest each spring on cliffs such as Champlain Mountain and Jordan Cliffs. During nesting season, the Precipice, Jordan Cliffs, Penobscot East, and Valley Cove trails close, reopening once the chicks can fly (in past years, usually late July to August).",
  "不用预约；护林员有时在 Precipice 停车场架望远镜带大家看游隼，时间看公园活动日历。": "No reservation needed. Rangers sometimes set up spotting scopes in the Precipice parking area to show visitors the falcons; check the park events calendar for times.",
  "2026 年 3 月 1 日起照例关闭；10 月 15 日公园公告里已经没有这几条步道的关闭通知。": "In 2026 the trails closed March 1 as usual; as of October 15, park alerts no longer listed closures for these trails.",
  "马车道马车游": "Carriage rides from Wildwood Stables",
  "从乔丹池南边的 Wildwood Stables 坐马车走洛克菲勒修的马车道，经过手工砌的石桥，有 1 小时和 2 小时的路线（有一条上 Day 山顶看海）；也有能上轮椅的马车。": "Ride a horse-drawn carriage from Wildwood Stables, south of Jordan Pond, along the carriage roads Rockefeller built, past hand-built stone bridges. There are 1-hour and 2-hour routes (one goes up Day Mountain for an ocean view), and wheelchair-accessible carriages are available.",
  "在特许经营商 Carriages of Acadia 的网站提前订，位子少。": "Book ahead on the website of the concessioner, Carriages of Acadia; seats are limited.",
  "2026 年的营业期是 5 月 24 日到 10 月 15 日。": "The 2026 season runs May 24–October 15.",
  "看星空": "Stargazing",
  "美国东海岸光污染少的地方不多，阿卡迪亚是其中之一：Sand Beach、Seawall、乔丹池南岸和 Ocean Path 都是公园推荐的看星空地点，夏天无月的晚上能看到银河。": "Acadia is one of the few places on the East Coast with little light pollution. Sand Beach, Seawall, the south shore of Jordan Pond, and Ocean Path are the park's recommended stargazing spots, and on moonless summer nights you can see the Milky Way.",
  "不用预约；5–10 月卡迪拉克山顶路每晚 9 点对车辆关闭、不许过夜停车，想在山顶看星星只能走路或骑车上去（带头灯）。": "No reservation needed. From May to October, the Cadillac summit road closes to vehicles at 9 p.m. nightly and overnight parking isn't allowed, so to stargaze from the summit you have to walk or bike up (bring a headlamp).",
  "旱季看鳄鱼和涉禽": "Dry-season wildlife viewing",
  "旱季草原上的水越来越少，鱼被困在水塘和水沟里，短吻鳄和成群的苍鹭、白鹭、林鹳、粉红琵鹭都聚过来觅食，也是涉禽筑巢的季节。蛇鸟步道、Shark Valley 和 Pa-hay-okee 路边是最容易看到的地方。": "In the dry season, water on the sawgrass prairie shrinks and fish get trapped in ponds and ditches, drawing alligators and flocks of herons, egrets, wood storks, and roseate spoonbills to feed. It's also nesting season for wading birds. The Anhinga Trail, Shark Valley, and the Pa-hay-okee road are the easiest places to see them.",
  "不用预约；早上和傍晚动物最活跃。": "No reservation needed. Animals are most active in the morning and evening.",
  "Royal Palm 护林员活动": "Ranger programs at Royal Palm",
  "旱季 Royal Palm 每天有护林员活动：10:30 的蛇鸟步道漫步（约 1 小时）、13:30 的 20 分钟短讲，每周一、三、五 20:30 还有蛇鸟步道夜间漫步，用手电看鳄鱼和夜行动物；Long Pine Key 有带自行车的骑行导览和晚间讲座。": "In the dry season, Royal Palm has ranger programs every day: an Anhinga Trail stroll at 10:30 a.m. (about 1 hour) and a 20-minute talk at 1:30 p.m., plus Anhinga Trail night walks at 8:30 p.m. on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Fridays, using flashlights to find alligators and nocturnal animals. Long Pine Key has guided bike rides and evening talks.",
  "大部分不用预约，到 Royal Palm 的长椅集合；骑行导览要在 FareHarbor 上预约。具体日期看公园活动日历或打 305-242-7700。": "Most need no reservation; meet at the benches at Royal Palm. Guided bike rides require a reservation on FareHarbor. Check the park events calendar or call 305-242-7700 for dates.",
  "护林员活动随人手和季节变化，雨季（5–11 月）很少。": "Ranger programs vary with staffing and the season and are rare in the wet season (May–November).",
  "佛罗里达湾护林员划艇（Paddling in Paradise）": "Paddling in Paradise (ranger-led kayak trip)",
  "从 Flamingo 出发、护林员带队在佛罗里达湾划约 3 小时皮划艇，看红树林岸边的鸟和海里的海牛、海豚；装备公园提供。": "A roughly 3-hour ranger-led kayak trip on Florida Bay from Flamingo, looking for birds along the mangrove shore and manatees and dolphins in the water. The park provides the gear.",
  "免费（只收门票），必须预约：在 FareHarbor 上订或打 239-695-2945；16 岁以上、要有划艇经验，强度较大。": "Free (entrance fee only), but reservations are required: book on FareHarbor or call 239-695-2945. Ages 16 and up, with paddling experience; it's fairly strenuous.",
  "2026–27 年冬季：11 月 14 日到 12 月 18 日每周六、周日和感恩节、11 月 27 日的 8:00；12 月 19 日到 2027 年 2 月 26 日每周五到周一的 8:00。": "Winter 2026–27: 8 a.m. on Saturdays and Sundays plus Thanksgiving and November 27 from November 14 to December 18, and 8 a.m. Friday through Monday from December 19 to February 26, 2027.",
  "Nike 导弹基地开放日": "Nike Missile Site HM-69 open houses",
  "冷战时期的防空导弹基地平时锁着，旱季由志愿者和护林员开放参观日（一般 10:00–14:00），可以看导弹库、装弹棚和一枚 Nike Hercules 导弹；每年 3 月还有 Nike 基地节。": "This Cold War air defense missile site is normally locked, but in the dry season volunteers and rangers hold open houses (usually 10 a.m.–2 p.m.), where you can see the missile barns, the assembly building, and a Nike Hercules missile. There's also a Nike Missile Site festival each March.",
  "免费（只收门票），不用预约；开放日不是每天，看公园活动日历。": "Free (entrance fee only), no reservation needed. Open houses aren't held every day; check the park events calendar.",
  "2026 年的 Nike 基地节在 3 月 7 日；2027 年的日期还没公布。": "The 2026 Nike Missile Site festival was March 7; 2027 dates haven't been announced.",
  "Everglades 海鲜节": "Everglades Seafood Festival",
  "Everglades City 每年 2 月办的海鲜节，正赶上石蟹季：石蟹钳、炸鳄鱼肉、蛙腿和各种海鲜摊，还有现场音乐和手工艺品市集，是这个渔村一年最热闹的三天。": "Everglades City's seafood festival each February, right in stone crab season: stone crab claws, fried alligator, frog legs, and all kinds of seafood stands, plus live music and a craft market. It's the liveliest three days of the year in this fishing village.",
  "在镇政府前举办，门票现场买；那几天 Everglades City 的住宿很早订满。": "Held in front of City Hall; buy admission at the gate. Lodging in Everglades City books up early for those days.",
  "2027 年是第 57 届，2 月 19–21 日。": "The 57th festival is February 19–21, 2027.",
  "Boca Chita 灯塔重新开放": "Boca Chita Key Lighthouse reopening",
  "Boca Chita 岛上 1938 年建的装饰灯塔因为生锈、飓风损坏关了两年多，2026 年 6 月修好重新开放：换了铁栏杆和门窗、修了砖石，游客又能爬到顶上看比斯坎湾和迈阿密的天际线。": "The 1938 ornamental lighthouse on Boca Chita Key, closed for more than two years by rust and hurricane damage, reopened after repairs in June 2026. With new iron railings, doors, and windows and restored masonry, visitors can once again climb to the top for views of Biscayne Bay and the Miami skyline.",
  "只能坐船去：跟 Biscayne National Park Institute 从 Coconut Grove 出发的 Boca Chita 游船（每天一班），或者自己开船（周五到周一和联邦假日白天停靠 $25）。": "By boat only: take Biscayne National Park Institute's Boca Chita boat tour from Coconut Grove (one trip daily), or bring your own boat ($25 to dock during the day Friday through Monday and on federal holidays).",
  "2026 年 6 月 25 日公园宣布重新开放；进灯塔要身高 42 英寸（约 107 厘米）以上。": "The park announced the reopening on June 25, 2026. You must be at least 42 inches tall to enter the lighthouse.",
  "夏季浮潜季": "Summer snorkeling season",
  "夏天信风弱，湾外的珊瑚礁浪小、水清，是一年里浮潜最好的时候；冬春冷锋一来就刮好几天大风，船团常取消。6–8 月 Coconut Grove 出发的 Boca Chita 游船也加 1 小时湾里的入门浮潜。": "In summer the trade winds are light, and the reefs outside the bay have small waves and clear water, making it the best snorkeling of the year. In winter and spring, cold fronts bring days of strong wind, and boat tours are often canceled. In June–August, the Boca Chita boat tour from Coconut Grove also adds a 1-hour beginner snorkel in the bay.",
  "向 Biscayne National Park Institute 订浮潜团（2026 年每人 $115），每天 9:15、13:30 从 Convoy Point 出发。": "Book a snorkeling tour with Biscayne National Park Institute ($115 per person in 2026), departing Convoy Point daily at 9:15 a.m. and 1:30 p.m.",
  "夏天午后常有雷雨，挑上午的班次；6–11 月是飓风季，有热带风暴时停航。": "Afternoon thunderstorms are common in summer, so pick a morning trip. June–November is hurricane season, and boats don't run when there's a tropical storm.",
  "傍晚游船（Park After Dark）": "Evening Bay Cruise",
  "1.5 小时的傍晚游船，17:00 从 Convoy Point 开进比斯坎湾，船上的向导讲公园的海和岛，18:30 回来；冬季日落早，正好赶上晚霞。": "A 1.5-hour evening cruise that leaves Convoy Point at 5 p.m. for Biscayne Bay, with a guide talking about the park's waters and islands, and returns at 6:30 p.m. In winter the sun sets early, so you catch the sunset colors.",
  "向 Biscayne National Park Institute 订票（2026 年每人 $68，6 人以内包船 $390），开船前 30 分钟到游客中心二楼报到。": "Book with Biscayne National Park Institute ($68 per person in 2026, or $390 for a private boat for up to six). Check in on the second floor of the visitor center 30 minutes before departure.",
  "拼船只在节假日一段开（上一季是 2025 年 12 月 18 日到 2026 年 1 月 4 日），2026–27 年冬季的日期官网还没公布；平时可以包船。": "Shared cruises run only during the holiday period (last season, December 18, 2025–January 4, 2026); winter 2026–27 dates haven't been posted on the website yet. Private charters are available at other times.",
  "Homestead 国家公园免费电车": "Homestead National Parks Trolley",
  "Homestead 市冬季周末开的免费电车，从市中心的 Homestead Station 和 Turnpike 2 号出口旁的 Courtyard 酒店出发，开到比斯坎的 Convoy Point、Homestead Bayfront Park 和大沼泽地，坐电车进大沼泽地还免门票。": "A free trolley run by the City of Homestead on winter weekends, departing from Homestead Station downtown and the Courtyard hotel by Turnpike Exit 2, to Biscayne's Convoy Point, Homestead Bayfront Park, and the Everglades. Riding the trolley into the Everglades also gets you in without paying the entrance fee.",
  "免费，在 Homestead 市的 gateway 页面看时刻表、预约座位。": "Free. See the schedule and reserve seats on the City of Homestead's gateway page.",
  "2025–26 年季是 2026 年 1 月 4 日到 4 月 20 日的周末，外加 2025 年 12 月 26–31 日每天开；2026–27 年季的日期还没公布。": "The 2025–26 season ran weekends January 4–April 20, 2026, plus daily December 26–31, 2025. Dates for the 2026–27 season haven't been announced.",
  "Family Fun Fest 亲子活动日": "Family Fun Fest",
  "公园办了二十多年的免费亲子活动：冬春每个月第二个星期日下午在游客中心，有护林员带的手工、小实验和海洋生物主题的游戏。": "A free family event the park has held for more than 20 years: in winter and spring, on the second Sunday afternoon of each month at the visitor center, rangers lead crafts, simple experiments, and marine-life games.",
  "往年是 12 月到 4 月每月第二个星期日 13:00–16:00；2026–27 年季的日期还没查到公告，去之前问游客中心。": "In past years it ran 1–4 p.m. on the second Sunday of each month, December through April. No announcement for the 2026–27 season could be found; ask at the visitor center before you go.",
  "哥伦布日周末的 Elliott Key 船会": "Columbus Day weekend boat gathering",
  "每年 10 月哥伦布日周末，迈阿密的帆船赛之后，几百条私人游艇聚到 Elliott Key 西侧的浅水里开派对，是公园一年里最乱、最危险的几天，公园和海岸警卫队会严查酒驾船、限制并船数量。": "Every October on Columbus Day weekend, after a Miami regatta, hundreds of private boats gather in the shallows off the west side of Elliott Key to party. These are the rowdiest and most dangerous days of the year in the park, and the park and the Coast Guard crack down on boating under the influence and limit how many boats can raft up together.",
  "不用参加；这个周末想安静上岛的，换个日子。": "Not something to join. If you want a quiet day on the island, pick a different weekend.",
  "帆船赛本身在公园外；公园每年会公布当周末的停泊规定。": "The regatta itself takes place outside the park; each year the park announces the mooring rules for that weekend.",
  "乌燕鸥筑巢季": "Sooty tern nesting season",
  "每年 1 月底到 7 月初，成群的乌燕鸥和白顶玄燕鸥挤在杰斐逊堡东边的 Bush Key 上筑巢，叫声在要塞里都听得见；夏天还常见军舰鸟在要塞上空盘旋。": "From late January to early July each year, crowds of sooty terns and brown noddies nest on Bush Key just east of Fort Jefferson, loud enough to hear from inside the fort. In summer, magnificent frigatebirds often circle over the fort.",
  "坐渡轮或水上飞机到 Garden Key，在要塞的墙上或岸边用望远镜看，不用另外预约。": "Take the ferry or a seaplane to Garden Key and watch with binoculars from the fort walls or the shore; no separate reservation needed.",
  "筑巢期 Bush Key 封闭（一般只在 10 月中到 1 月中开放）；2026 年 9 月 29 日的公告说 Bush Key 大部分已经开放，北侧一小块、整个 Long Key 和所有植被区仍为保护军舰鸟封闭。": "Bush Key is closed during nesting season (it's generally open only from mid-October to mid-January). A September 29, 2026, notice said most of Bush Key had reopened, but a small area on the north side, all of Long Key, and all vegetated areas remain closed to protect frigatebirds.",
  "春季候鸟迁徙": "Spring bird migration",
  "干龟是候鸟从南美、加勒比海北飞途中难得的落脚点：2 月中就有先到的，3 月明显变多，4 月到 5 月中最盛，前后有 200 多种鸟经过，林莺、唐纳雀常累得停在 Garden Key 的树上和要塞里的饮水处，是美国观鸟人心中的圣地之一。": "The Dry Tortugas are a rare stopover for birds flying north from South America and the Caribbean. The first arrivals show up in mid-February, numbers climb noticeably in March, and migration peaks from April to mid-May, with more than 200 species passing through. Exhausted warblers and tanagers often rest in the trees on Garden Key and at the water drips inside the fort, making this one of the most celebrated birding spots in the U.S.",
  "坐渡轮一日游能看几个小时；想看早晚的鸟要露营（渡轮露营票提前 6 个月放）。": "A ferry day trip gives you a few hours; to see birds in the early morning and evening, camp (ferry camping tickets are released 6 months ahead).",
  "Garden Key 露营看星空": "Camping on Garden Key",
  "一日游的人 15:00 跟船走了以后，岛上只剩露营的人：傍晚在要塞墙上看日落，夜里离最近的城市 100 多公里，银河很清楚，清早可以在没人的护城河墙边浮潜。原始营地，水、冰块、食物都要自己从 Key West 带。": "Once the day-trippers leave on the boat at 3 p.m., only campers remain on the island. Watch the sunset from the fort walls in the evening; at night, with the nearest city more than 60 miles away, the Milky Way is sharp, and early in the morning you can snorkel along the empty moat wall. It's a primitive campground, so bring all your water, ice, and food from Key West.",
  "渡轮的露营票每月第一个工作日 8:00 放 6 个月后整个月的票，很快卖完；营位先到先得，每晚 $15（10–20 人的团体营位 $30，要提前申请），用 Recreation.gov App 付款。渡轮最多接 3 晚。": "Ferry camping tickets for an entire month go on sale at 8 a.m. on the first business day of the month six months before, and sell out fast. Campsites are first come, first served at $15 per night (group sites for 10–20 people are $30 and require an advance application); pay with the Recreation.gov app. The ferry allows stays of up to 3 nights.",
  "Key West 奇幻节（Fantasy Fest）": "Fantasy Fest",
  "Key West 每年 10 月下旬的十天成人狂欢节：变装、派对和 Duval 街的大游行。这几天 Key West 住宿最贵、最难订，老城人山人海，带孩子的避开。": "Key West's 10-day adult carnival in late October: costumes, parties, and a big parade on Duval Street. Lodging in Key West is at its most expensive and hardest to book, Old Town is packed, and families with kids should avoid it.",
  "街头活动免费，舞会、派对要买票。": "Street events are free; balls and parties require tickets.",
  "2026 年是 10 月 16 日到 25 日，大游行在 10 月 24 日（周六）晚上。": "In 2026 it runs October 16–25, with the big parade on the evening of Saturday, October 24.",
  "秋叶季": "Fall colors",
  "大烟山有 100 多种本土乔木，秋天颜色特别杂。红叶从高处往低处走：海拔 1,200 米以上 10 月上中旬先变色（Kuwohi、Newfound Gap 一带），中低海拔一般 10 月中旬到 11 月初最好（Cades Cove、Roaring Fork、Little River 路）。每年早晚差一两周，没法提前预测。": "With more than 100 native tree species, the Smokies have unusually varied fall color. Color moves from high elevations down: above about 4,000 feet it turns first in early to mid-October (around Kuwohi and Newfound Gap), and middle and low elevations are usually best from mid-October to early November (Cades Cove, Roaring Fork, Little River Road). Timing shifts by a week or two each year and can't be predicted in advance.",
  "不用预约；但这是一年最挤的时候，住宿要提前几个月订，周末进出 Gatlinburg 和 Cades Cove 常堵 1 小时以上，尽量平日、一早出发。": "No reservation needed, but this is the busiest time of year. Book lodging months ahead; on weekends, traffic in and out of Gatlinburg and Cades Cove often backs up for more than an hour, so go on a weekday and start early.",
  "同步萤火虫": "Synchronous fireflies at Elkmont",
  "每年 5 月底到 6 月中，Elkmont 一带林子里的一种萤火虫（Photinus carolinus）会成群同步闪光，几秒钟一起亮、再一起暗，是北美少数能看到这种现象的地方。公园在高峰期的 8 个晚上按抽签发停车证，每晚约 120 辆车。": "From late May to mid-June each year, one firefly species in the Elkmont woods (Photinus carolinus) flashes in sync: thousands light up together for a few seconds, then go dark together. It's one of the few places in North America to see this. During the peak, the park issues parking passes by lottery for eight nights, about 120 vehicles a night.",
  "4 月下旬在 Recreation.gov 抽签（2026 年是 4 月 24–27 日，申请费 $1），5 月初出结果，中签再付 $29；每年 2 万多人抽，中签率很低。没抽中可以在园外的私人营地或别处碰运气，但闪光规模小很多。": "Enter the lottery on Recreation.gov in late April (April 24–27 in 2026, with a $1 application fee); results come out in early May, and winners pay $29. More than 20,000 people apply each year, so the odds are low. If you don't win, you can try your luck at private campgrounds or elsewhere outside the park, though the displays are much smaller.",
  "2026 年的观赏期是 5 月 20–27 日；2027 年的日期一般 4 月公布。": "The 2026 viewing period was May 20–27; 2027 dates are usually announced in April.",
  "春季野花季": "Spring wildflowers",
  "大烟山被称为“野花之国”，有 1,500 多种开花植物。3 月底到 5 月林下的延龄草、獐耳细辛、紫罗兰一片片开，低处先开、高处后开；4 月下旬 Gatlinburg 有办了 70 多年的春季野花朝圣节（Spring Wildflower Pilgrimage），几天里有上百场导览徒步和讲座。": "The Smokies are known as the “Wildflower National Park,” with more than 1,500 kinds of flowering plants. From late March through May, trillium, hepatica, and violets bloom in drifts on the forest floor, lower elevations first and higher ones later. In late April, Gatlinburg hosts the Spring Wildflower Pilgrimage, held for more than 70 years, with over 100 guided walks and talks over several days.",
  "看野花不用预约；朝圣节的导览要在官网报名付费，一般冬末开放报名。": "Seeing the wildflowers needs no reservation; Pilgrimage walks require paid registration on its website, which usually opens in late winter.",
  "2026 年的朝圣节是 4 月 22–25 日；2027 年的日期还没公布，一般也在 4 月下旬。": "The 2026 Pilgrimage was April 22–25. 2027 dates haven't been announced but are usually in late April as well.",
  "麋鹿发情季": "Elk rut",
  "大烟山的麋鹿是 2001 年从外地重新引进的，现在西北卡约有 270 头，其中约 150 头至少一部分时间待在园内。9–10 月发情期公鹿在 Cataloochee 谷和 Oconaluftee 游客中心旁的草地上嘶鸣、角斗，清早和傍晚最活跃，是一年里看麋鹿最精彩的时候。": "Elk were reintroduced to the Smokies in 2001 and now number about 270 in western North Carolina, about 150 of which spend at least part of their time in the park. During the September–October rut, bulls bugle and spar in Cataloochee Valley and the fields beside the Oconaluftee Visitor Center, most actively in the early morning and evening. It's the best time of year to watch elk.",
  "不用预约；发情期的公鹿有攻击性，园规是至少离 50 码（约 46 米），惊扰到麋鹿就算太近，不许喂食。": "No reservation needed. Bulls in rut are aggressive. Park rules require staying at least 50 yards (150 feet) away; if you disturb an elk, you're too close. Feeding is prohibited.",
  "Cataloochee 谷 2024 年飓风 Helene 后只重开了下段（到 Beech Grove 学校），上段的草地只能走路进去。": "Since Hurricane Helene in 2024, only the lower part of Cataloochee Valley (to Beech Grove School) has reopened; you can reach the upper fields only on foot.",
  "Cades Cove 无车周三": "Cades Cove Vehicle-Free Wednesdays",
  "每年 5 月初到 9 月底的每个周三，Cades Cove 约 18 公里的环路全天只许走路和骑车，没有汽车，可以慢慢骑一圈看鹿、看老木屋；环路入口的营地商店旁可以租自行车。": "Every Wednesday from early May to late September, the 11-mile Cades Cove Loop Road is open only to walkers and cyclists all day, with no cars, so you can ride a slow loop looking for deer and old cabins. Bikes are for rent next to the campground store at the loop entrance.",
  "不用预约；环路入口的停车场一早就满，满了就不放车进来，最好 8 点前到。租车先到先得，常要排队。": "No reservation needed. The parking lot at the loop entrance fills early and no more cars are let in once it's full, so arrive before 8 a.m. Bike rentals are first come, first served, and there's often a line.",
  "2026 年是 5 月 6 日到 9 月 30 日；2027 年的日期没公布，按往年也是 5 月到 9 月的周三。": "In 2026 it runs May 6–September 30. 2027 dates haven't been announced, but by tradition it's again Wednesdays from May to September.",
  "火焰杜鹃与卡托巴杜鹃花期": "Flame azalea and rhododendron bloom",
  "6 月中下旬高处的草甸开满火焰杜鹃（橙红到黄色）和紫红的卡托巴杜鹃，Andrews Bald、Gregory Bald 最有名；低处溪边的大白杜鹃 6 月底到 7 月开。蓝岭公路上的 Craggy Gardens 也在这时候花开成片。": "In mid-to-late June, the high balds fill with flame azalea (orange-red to yellow) and purplish Catawba rhododendron, most famously at Andrews Bald and Gregory Bald. Lower down, great rhododendron along the streams blooms white from late June into July. Craggy Gardens on the Blue Ridge Parkway also blooms in masses at this time.",
  "不用预约；Andrews Bald 从 Kuwohi 停车场出发，花期周末停车场很早就满。": "No reservation needed. Andrews Bald starts from the Kuwohi parking area, which fills very early on bloom-season weekends.",
  "山地生活节": "Mountain Life Festival",
  "每年 9 月在 Oconaluftee 游客中心后面的山地农庄博物馆办一天，演示做苹果酱、高粱糖浆、打铁、纺线和阿巴拉契亚民间音乐，免费。": "A one-day festival each September at the Mountain Farm Museum behind the Oconaluftee Visitor Center, with demonstrations of apple butter and sorghum molasses making, blacksmithing, spinning, and Appalachian folk music. Free.",
  "不用预约，免费；10:00–16:00。": "No reservation needed, and free; 10 a.m.–4 p.m.",
  "2025 年是 9 月 20 日；2026、2027 年的日期没查到，一般在 9 月中下旬的周六。": "In 2025 it was September 20. No dates for 2026 or 2027 could be found; it's usually on a Saturday in mid-to-late September."
};
